13,species,Casuariiformes,Casuariidae,Emu and Cassowaries,Dromaius novaehollandiae,"(Latham, J, 1790)","Index ornithologicus, sive systema ornithologiæ; complectens avium divisionem in classes, ordines, genera, species, ipsarumque varietates: adjectis synonymis, locis, descriptionibus, &c. 2 p.665",Emu,Emu,,30,"Taxa minor and baudinianus are treated as subspecies of Dromaius novaehollandiae based on similarity in mitochondrial DNA (Heupink et al. 2011; Thomson et al. 2018; Cibois et al. 2020). Despite the tremendous size difference of minor, the repeated evolution of small size in isolated island populations over short time periods also argues against species status.",,,NE,,emu1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/emu1/,avibase-FD2456D5,,,"Novae Hollandiae, restricted to Sydney, NSW (fide Mathews, 1910a, The Birds of Australia 1: 3)",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/226469#page/205/mode/1up,Casuarius N. Hollandiae
