27,species,Apterygiformes,Apterygidae,Kiwis,Apteryx owenii,"Gould, J, 1847","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.15, no.175 p.94",Little Spotted Kiwi,Little Spotted Kiwi,Little Spotted Kiwi,,,"Kapiti, South, and formerly North islands (New Zealand)",,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22678129,liskiw1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/liskiw1/,avibase-187706CF,,,"New Zealand. Type probably from Nelson or Marlborough, fide Oliver, 1955, N. Z. Birds, ed. 2, p. 53.",On a new species of Apteryx.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46217#page/596/mode/1up,Apteryx Owenii
28,species,Apterygiformes,Apterygidae,Kiwis,Apteryx maxima,"Sclater, PL; von Hochstetter, F, 1861","The Natural History Review 1, no.IV p.506",Great Spotted Kiwi,Great Spotted Kiwi,Great Spotted Kiwi,N-70,"Shepherd et al. (2021) show genetically that the syntypes of the Great Spotted Kiwi Apteryx haastii Potts, 1872, are hybrids between the Rowi, A. rowi Tennyson et al., 2003, and Little Spotted Kiwi, A. owenii Gould, 1847. Therefore, Potts' name haastii does not apply to the species known as the Great Spotted Kiwi. The earliest name that does apply to the Great Spotted Kiwi is Apteryx maxima Sclater & von Hochstetter, 1861, an earlier name than haastii which Palma et al. (2003) had designated a nomen oblitum under Art. 23.9 of the Code. The grounds for that designation under that article no longer exist; and as nomina oblita remain available names under the Code's Glossary and there is no other younger name in wide use, Shepherd et al. (2021) returned to maxima Sclater & Hochstetter, 1861 as the name for the Great Spotted. Hence, the correct name for the Great Spotted Kiwi is Apteryx maxima.",montane forest of northwestern South Island (New Zealand),,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22678132,grskiw1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/grskiw1/,avibase-0D8B9E40,,,,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/30158#page/518/mode/1up,Apteryx maxima
