283,subspecies,Anseriformes,Anatidae,"Ducks, Swans, and Geese",Oxyura jamaicensis andina,"Lehmann V, FC, 1946","The Auk 63, no.2 p.221",,,,52,"Taxa ferruginea and andina are treated as subspecies of Oxyura jamaicensis based on available evidence. Although ferruginea and nominate jamaicensis are phenotypically distinct, low mitochondrial DNA divergence (McCracken & Sorenson 2005) and shared haplotypes occur (Lozano-Jaramillo et al. 2018). Furthermore, the geographically intermediate taxon, andina, is of hybrid origin (Adams & Slavid 1984; Fjeldså 1986; McCracken & Sorenson 2005, Muñoz-Fuentes et al. 2013; Donegan et al. 2015; Lozano-Jaramillo et al. 2018), suggesting that all three are best treated as conspecific pending further research.",central and eastern Andes of Colombia,,,,andduc2,,avibase-8507AEF0,,,"Lagunas del Paramo de Boca-Grande, Cundinamarca. Eastern Andes of Colombia; altitude 4,000 meters.",Two New Birds from the Andes of Colombia,https://sora.unm.edu/sites/default/files/journals/auk/v063n02/p0218-p0223.pdf,Oxyura jamaicensis andina
