347,species,Anseriformes,Anatidae,"Ducks, Swans, and Geese",Anser brachyrhynchus,"Baillon, LAF, 1834",Mémoires de la Société Royale d'Émulation d'Abbeville (1833) p.74,Pink-footed Goose,Pink-footed Goose,Pink-footed Goose,,,"breeds Greenland, Iceland, and Spitsbergen; winters northwestern Europe",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22679872,pifgoo,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/pifgoo/,avibase-AFA7EE74,,,"Abbeville, lower Somme River, France.","Catalogue des Mammifères, Oiseaux, Reptiles, Poissons et Mollusques testacés marins, observés dans l'arrondissement d'Abbeville.",,Anser Brachyrhynchus
348,species,Anseriformes,Anatidae,"Ducks, Swans, and Geese",Anser fabalis,"(Latham, J, 1787)",Supplement to the general synopsis of birds p.297,Taiga Bean Goose,Taiga Bean-Goose,,8,"Taxon serrirostris (polytypic, including rossicus) is treated as a species separate from Anser fabalis (polytypic, including johanseni and middendorffii) based on available evidence. The species are morphologically diagnosable (de Jong 2019) and ecologically separated to a large extent (Sangster & Oreel 1996). Genetic data are complicated by a history of introgressive hybridization (Ottenburghs et al. 2020, 2023), rapid speciation (Ottenburghs et al. 2016), and incongruent phylogenetic reconstructions (Ruokenen et al. 2008; Ottenburghs et al. 2016, 2020, 2023). However, genomic data consistently show A. brachyrhynchus to be nested within the fabalis-serrirostris complex (Ottenburghs et al. 2016, 2023) with highly differentiated genomic regions providing strong support for a 3-species treatment (Ottenburghs et al. 2023): A. fabalis, A. brachyrhynchus, and A. serrirostris. For taxonomic stability, middendorffii is treated as a subspecies of A. fabalis, but a more comprehensive genomic review is needed to determine if species status is warranted (Ruokenen et al. 2008).",,,NE,,taibeg1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/taibeg1/,avibase-BDB497A3,,,Great Britain.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/103199#page/335/mode/1up,Anas Fabalis
