350,subspecies,Anseriformes,Anatidae,"Ducks, Swans, and Geese",Anser fabalis johanseni,"Delacour, JT, 1951",Ardea 39 p.139,,,,,,"breeds taiga and wooded tundra of Ural Mountains to Lake Baikal; winters mainly to southeastern Kazakhstan, eastern Kyrgyzstan, and Iran eastwards to northwestern China",,,,taibeg3,,avibase-EEF6740E,,,"Tai-pai Shan, Tsinling (= Chin Ling) Mountains, Shensi, China.","Taxonomic notes on the Bean Geese, Anser fabalis Lath..",http://ardea.nou.nu/ardea_show_article.php?nr=984,Anser fabalis johanseni
351,subspecies,Anseriformes,Anatidae,"Ducks, Swans, and Geese",Anser fabalis middendorffii,"Severtsov, NA, 1873","Izvestiya Imperatorskago Obshchestva Lyubitelei Estestvoznaniya, Antropologii i Etnografii 8 pt2 p.70,149",,,,8,"Taxon serrirostris (polytypic, including rossicus) is treated as a species separate from Anser fabalis (polytypic, including johanseni and middendorffii) based on available evidence. The species are morphologically diagnosable (de Jong 2019) and ecologically separated to a large extent (Sangster & Oreel 1996). Genetic data are complicated by a history of introgressive hybridization (Ottenburghs et al. 2020, 2023), rapid speciation (Ottenburghs et al. 2016), and incongruent phylogenetic reconstructions (Ruokenen et al. 2008; Ottenburghs et al. 2016, 2020, 2023). However, genomic data consistently show A. brachyrhynchus to be nested within the fabalis-serrirostris complex (Ottenburghs et al. 2016, 2023) with highly differentiated genomic regions providing strong support for a 3-species treatment (Ottenburghs et al. 2023): A. fabalis, A. brachyrhynchus, and A. serrirostris. For taxonomic stability, middendorffii is treated as a subspecies of A. fabalis, but a more comprehensive genomic review is needed to determine if species status is warranted (Ruokenen et al. 2008).","breeds taiga of Altai region, eastern Siberia (east of Lake Baikal), and northern Mongolia, and eastwards to the Sea of Okhotsk; winters in central and eastern China, the Korean Peninsula, Japan, and Taiwan",,,,taibeg4,,avibase-97E7761F,,,eastern Siberia.,Vertikal Turkestan Zhivotn.,http://books.e-heritage.ru/book/10080878,Anser Middendorffii
