491,species,Anseriformes,Anatidae,"Ducks, Swans, and Geese",Tachyeres patachonicus,"(King, PP, 1828)","The Zoological Journal 4, no.13 p.100",Flying Steamer Duck,Flying Steamer-Duck,Flying Steamerduck,6,"The Falkland Islands are retained in the range circumscription of Tachyeres patachonicus based on morphological and genetic evidence that it occurs there. Although Fulton et al. (2012), using mitochondrial DNA, suggested that flighted birds on the Falkland Islands were T. brachypterus, with flight ability a polymorphic trait, genomic data (Campagna et al. 2019) confirmed the presence of both species with the patachonicus genomes showing evidence of introgression from brachypterus; further research would be informative.",southern Chile (north to Maule) and southern Argentina (north to Neuquén and southern Buenos Aires provinces); scarce Falkland Islands,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22680052,flystd1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/flystd1/,avibase-B3F9BB06,,,Strait of Magellan.,Exhibition of several new species of birds belonging to the collection brought home from the Straits of Magellan by Captain King.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/87902#page/112/mode/1up,Oidemia Patachonica
