1717,genus,Musophagiformes,Musophagidae,Turacos,Gallirex,"Lesson, RP, 1844",L'Écho du Monde Savant 11 no.5 col.110,,,,688,"Revised generic limits in Tauraco are based on the mitochondrial-DNA dominated data of Perktaş et al. (2020) and include recognition of a polytypic Gallirex (species porphyreolophus and johnstoni, the latter sometimes placed in Ruwenzorornis), a polytypic Menelikornis (species leucotis and ruspolii), and a broad Tauraco (remaining species). While Musophaga is sometimes used for rossae and violaceus, those are subsumed within Tauraco as Perktaş et al. (2020) showed that, while phenotypically distinct from green-bodied turacos, they form a well-supported clade that also includes T. macrorhynchus.",,,,,,,,M,"Corythaix porphyreolopha [Vigors, 1831]; type by subsequent designation (Gray, GR, 1855, Cat. of the Genera and Subgenera of Birds, p. 149).",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/180990#page/45/mode/1up,Gallirex
