2573,genus,Columbiformes,Columbidae,Doves and Pigeons,Spilopelia,"Sundevall, CJ, 1873",Methodi naturalis avium disponendarum tentamen. Försök till fogelklassens naturenliga uppställning fasc. 2 p.100,,,,402,Spilopelia is adopted for chinensis and senegalensis based on genetic evidence. Combined analyses of nuclear and mitochondrial DNA sequences in Streptopelia sensu lato (Johnson et al. 2001; Fulton et al. 2012) recovered Spilopelia as part of a basal polytomy with Nesoenas and a reduced Streptopelia. Retaining a monophyletic Streptopelia sensu lato is valid but would result in a phenotypically diverse genus.,,,,,,,,F,"Columba tigrina [Temminck, 1809]; type by subsequent designation (Sundevall, 1873, Methodi Naturalis Avium Disponendarum Tentamen, p. 186).",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/214645#page/182/mode/1up,Spilopelia
2574,species,Columbiformes,Columbidae,Doves and Pigeons,Spilopelia chinensis,"(Scopoli, GA, 1786)",Deliciae Florae et Faunae Insubricae 2 p.94,Spotted Dove,Spotted Dove,,401,"Taxon suratensis (monotypic) is treated as a subspecies of Spilopelia chinensis (polytypic) based on available evidence. Although western suratensis differs from eastern chinensis in voice and morphology, the geographically intermediate taxon tigrina is intermediate in appearance and vocalizations. A more detailed analysis of all forms, including genetics, is needed.",,,NE,,spodov,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/spodov/,avibase-C8EF4F36,,,"China, restricted to Canton, by Stresemann, injra, p. 67.",,,Columba chinensis
