2586,genus,Columbiformes,Columbidae,Doves and Pigeons,Nesoenas,"Salvadori, AT, 1893",Catalogue of the birds in the British Museum 21 p.327,,,,402,Spilopelia is adopted for chinensis and senegalensis based on genetic evidence. Combined analyses of nuclear and mitochondrial DNA sequences in Streptopelia sensu lato (Johnson et al. 2001; Fulton et al. 2012) recovered Spilopelia as part of a basal polytomy with Nesoenas and a reduced Streptopelia. Retaining a monophyletic Streptopelia sensu lato is valid but would result in a phenotypically diverse genus.,,,,,,,,F,"Columba mayeri [Prévost, 1843]; type by original designation and monotypy",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/34475#page/351/mode/1up,Nesoenas
2587,species,Columbiformes,Columbidae,Doves and Pigeons,Nesoenas picturatus,"(Temminck, CJ, 1813)","Histoire naturelle générale des pigeons et des gallinacés, accompagné de planches anatomiques 1 p.315,480",Malagasy Turtle Dove,Malagasy Turtle-Dove,Madagascar Turtle-dove,425,"Taxon picturatus (polytypic) is placed in the genus Nesoenas based on genetics and vocalizations. Formerly placed in Streptopelia, mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Johnson et al. 2001) show that picturatus is sister to Nesoenas mayeri, and the two share striking vocal similarities (Johnson et al. 2001; Wolfenden et al. 2015).",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22690364,matdov1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/matdov1/,avibase-CDDEA7EB,,,"lie de France, i.e. Mauritius.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/148601#page/337/mode/1up,Columba Picturata
