3191,species,Columbiformes,Columbidae,Doves and Pigeons,Ptilinopus speciosus,"Schlegel, H, 1871",Nederlandsch Tijdschrift voor de Dierkunde 4 p.23,Geelvink Fruit Dove,Geelvink Fruit-Dove,Geelvink Fruit-dove,420,"Taxon speciosus is treated as a monotypic species separate from Ptilinopus solomonensis (polytypic) based on differences in plumage, presence of a yellow peri-orbital skin patch, and vocalizations. Additionally, speciosus is a highly disjunct population from an endemism-rich area (Gregory 2017). Broader genetic sampling of the P. solomonensis-P. rivoli complex is needed to better define species limits in this group.","Numfor, Biak, and Yapen (Cenderawasih Bay, off northwestern New Guinea)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22728089,yebfrd1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/yebfrd1/,avibase-BE752C4F,,,"Islands of Numfor [Mafor] and Biak [Soek], Geelvink Bay.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/193078#page/35/mode/1up,Ptilopus speciosus
3192,species,Columbiformes,Columbidae,Doves and Pigeons,Ptilinopus solomonensis,"Gray, GR, 1870","The Annals and Magazine of Natural History including Zoology, Botany, and Geology ser.4, vol.5, no.29 p.328",Yellow-bibbed Fruit Dove,Yellow-bibbed Fruit-Dove,Yellow-banded Fruit-dove,420,"Taxon speciosus is treated as a monotypic species separate from Ptilinopus solomonensis (polytypic) based on differences in plumage, presence of a yellow peri-orbital skin patch, and vocalizations. Additionally, speciosus is a highly disjunct population from an endemism-rich area (Gregory 2017). Broader genetic sampling of the P. solomonensis-P. rivoli complex is needed to better define species limits in this group.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22728082,yebfrd2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/yebfrd2/,avibase-C15DD431,,,"Wanga, San Cristobal, Solomon Islands.",XXXIV. Descriptions of new Species of Birds from the Solomon and Banks's Groups of Islands.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/55190#page/342/mode/1up,Ptilonopus solomonensis
