3660,genus,Gruiformes,Rallidae,"Rails, Gallinules, and Coots",Poliolimnas,"Sharpe, RB, 1893","Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 1, no.5 p.28",,,,1148,Taxon cinereus is placed in the monospecific genus Poliolimnas based on nuclear (Garcia-R et al. 2020) and genomic DNA (Kirchman et al. 2021) evidence. Sometimes placed in Amaurornis but recovered as a deeply diverged sister lineage to Megacrex from which it differs in morphology and ecology indicating that cinereus is best treated as a monotypic genus.,,,,,,,,M,"Poliolimnas cinereus [Vieillot]; type by original designation,",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101092#page/53/mode/1up,Poliolimnas
