3922,species,Charadriiformes,Charadriidae,Plovers and Lapwings,Anarhynchus obscurus,"(Gmelin, JF, 1789)","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I. Pars II 1 pt2 p.686",New Zealand Plover,Red-breasted Dotterel,,909,"Taxon aquilonius is treated as a subspecies of Anarhynchus obscurus based on available evidence. Mitochondrial DNA divergence is weak (Barth et al. 2013), and differences in plumage, proportions, ecology, and behavior are best considered subspecific. Loss of intermediate populations also means that clinality cannot be assessed, and differences in ecology and behavior might be explained by geography and climate.",,,NE,,rebdot1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rebdot1/,avibase-358D1CDA,,,"New Zealand, i.e. Dusky Sound, South Island, ex Latham.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10286#page/187/mode/1up,Charadrius obscurus
