4114,species,Charadriiformes,Scolopacidae,Sandpipers and Allies,Tringa incana,"(Gmelin, JF, 1789)","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I. Pars II 1 pt2 p.658 dSM",Wandering Tattler,Wandering Tattler,Wandering Tattler,,,"breeds montane tundra from Chukotka (northeastern Siberia) through Alaskan mainland (except far north) to northwestern Canada; winters mainly rocky Pacific coasts from eastern Australasia, Melanesia, Micronesia, Polynesia, isolated eastern Pacific islands, and southwestern Canada to Ecuador",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22693305,wantat1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/wantat1/,avibase-13854B6E,,,Eimeo [= Moorea of the Society Group] and Palmerston Islands.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10286#page/159/mode/1up,Scolopax incana
4115,species,Charadriiformes,Scolopacidae,Sandpipers and Allies,Tringa brevipes,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1816)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 6 p.410",Grey-tailed Tattler,Gray-tailed Tattler,Grey-tailed Tattler,,,breeds montane tundra of Krasnoyarsk (west-central Siberia) and Yana River eastward to Kamchatka (eastern Siberia); winters muddy to sandy Pacific coasts from Malay Peninsula eastward through Micronesia and western Polynesia and southward to northern Australia,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22693289,gyttat1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gyttat1/,avibase-29256A38,,,No locality given; the type is from Timor.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/60102#page/434/mode/1up,Totanus brevipes
