4185,species,Charadriiformes,Scolopacidae,Sandpipers and Allies,Calidris bairdii,"(Coues, E, 1861)",Proceedings of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Philadelphia 13 p.194,Baird's Sandpiper,Baird's Sandpiper,Baird's Sandpiper,,,"breeds high Arctic dry tundra from Wrangel Island to eastern Chukotskiy Peninsula (northeastern Siberia) through northern and central Alaska, northern Canada including Arctic islands from Banks to Ellesmere and Baffin islands, and northwestern Greenland; winters in mountains and coastally from southern Peru through Chile and southern Argentina",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22693404,baisan,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/baisan/,avibase-1F1AD154,,,"Fort Resolution. North America east of the Rocky Mountains; specimen in U. S. National Museum claimed as type is from Fort Resolution, Great Slave Lake, Mackenzie.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/17713#page/206/mode/1up,Actodromas (Actodromas) Bairdii
4186,species,Charadriiformes,Scolopacidae,Sandpipers and Allies,Calidris melanotos,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1819)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 34 p.462",Pectoral Sandpiper,Pectoral Sandpiper,Pectoral Sandpiper,,,"breeds wet tundra from Yamal Peninsula eastward to Chukotskiy Peninsula (northwestern to eastern Siberia), including New Siberian and Wrangel islands, also western and northern Alaska eastward through northeastern Canada, including Arctic islands; winters wet grassland and wetland edge mainly to Peru, Bolivia, and southern Brazil southward to Tierra del Fuego; prone to extreme vagrancy",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22693408,pecsan,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/pecsan/,avibase-ACC99F35,,,"Paraguay, ex Azara, no. 401.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/64021#page/486/mode/1up,Tringa melanotos
4187,species,Charadriiformes,Scolopacidae,Sandpipers and Allies,Calidris pusilla,"(Linnaeus, C, 1766)",Systema Naturæ. Editio duodecima reformata. Tomus I [part 1] p.252,Semipalmated Sandpiper,Semipalmated Sandpiper,Semipalmated Sandpiper,,,"breeds tundra from eastern Chukotskiy Peninsula (northeastern Siberia) through northern Alaska and eastward in northern Canada to northern Labrador, including southern Canadian Arctic islands from Banks to Baffin; winters coasts from Isthmus of Tehuantepec and Yucatan Peninsula (southwestern Mexico) and Caribbean to far northern Chile and northeastern Brazil",,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22693373,semsan,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/semsan/,avibase-F35821AA,,,Santo Domingo.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/137337#page/256/mode/1up,Tringa pusilla
4188,species,Charadriiformes,Scolopacidae,Sandpipers and Allies,Calidris mauri,"(Cabanis, JL, 1857)","Journal für Ornithologie 4, no.24 p.419",Western Sandpiper,Western Sandpiper,Western Sandpiper,,,"breeds Chukotskiy Peninsula and Anadyr (northeastern Siberia; few), St. Lawrence Island (Bering Sea), and western and northern Alaska mainland; winters coastal Washington to Peru and Galapagos, southeastern Canada to Caribbean, and inland central Mexico to northern Costa Rica",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22693376,wessan,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/wessan/,avibase-01060BFD,,,Cuba.,Dr. J. Gundlach's Beiträge zur Ornithologie Cuba's. Nach Mittheilungen des Reisenden an Hr. Bez.-Dir. Sezekorn in Cassel ; von Letzterem zusammengestellt. Mit Zusätzen und Anmerkungen vom Herausgeber. (Fortsetzung von S. 337-352.)'.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/49380#page/967/mode/1up,Ereunetes Mauri
4189,species,Charadriiformes,Scolopacidae,Sandpipers and Allies,Calidris minuta,"(Leisler, JPA, 1812)",Nachträge zu Bechsteins Naturgeschichte Deutschlands pt1 p.74,Little Stint,Little Stint,Little Stint,,,breeds drier tundra from northern Scandinavia eastward through northern Russia to New Siberian Islands (east-central Siberia); winters mudflats and marshes from southern Europe and Africa eastward to southern Asia,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22693379,litsti,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/litsti/,avibase-9936FF4A,,,"Hanau am Main, Germany.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/202450#page/98/mode/1up,Tringa minuta
4190,species,Charadriiformes,Scolopacidae,Sandpipers and Allies,Calidris minutilla,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1819)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 34 p.466",Least Sandpiper,Least Sandpiper,Least Sandpiper,,,"breeds tundra and taiga wetlands from eastern Aleutian Is through Alaska and Canada eastward to Labrador and Nova Scotia; winters mudflats and wetlands from southeastern USA, Caribbean, and Mexico southward to northern South America",,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22693396,leasan,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/leasan/,avibase-A47B0BD4,,,"'Amérique jusq'au dela du Canada': restricted type locality, Halifax, Nova Scotia, apud A. O. U. Check-List, ed. 4, p. 120.)",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/64021#page/490/mode/1up,Tringa minutilla
4191,species,Charadriiformes,Scolopacidae,Sandpipers and Allies,Calidris fuscicollis,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1819)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 34 p.461",White-rumped Sandpiper,White-rumped Sandpiper,White-rumped Sandpiper,,,"breeds wet tundra from North Slope of Alaska eastward in coastal northern Canada to northwestern Hudson Bay, and Banks to Devon and Baffin islands (northeastern Canada); winters to wetlands of southern Chile, southeastern Brazil, northwestern to southeastern Argentina, and Falkland Islands",,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22693399,whrsan,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/whrsan/,avibase-153BA306,,,"Paraguay, ex Azara, no. 404.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/64021#page/485/mode/1up,Tringa fuscicollis
