4496,species,Charadriiformes,Laridae,"Skimmers, Noddies, Terns, and Gulls",Thalasseus maximus,"(Boddaert, P, 1783)",Table des planches enluminéez d'histoire naturelle de M. D'Aubenton p.58,Royal Tern,Royal Tern,,916,"Taxon albididorsalis is treated as a species separate from Thalasseus maximus based on differences in morphology and vocalizations (Dufour & Crochet 2020), as well as genetics (Collinson et al. 2017). Mitochondrial and nuclear DNA data both indicate that T. maximus sensu lato is not monophyletic, with albididorsalis being more closely aligned with T. bengalensis.","breeds coastal southern California and Gulf of California to Sinaloa and Islas Tres Marias, and Atlantic from Virginia southward to Florida, Gulf of Mexico to s Texas, and Caribbean including peripheral islands southeastward to French Guiana, and disjunctly coastal southern Brazil, Uruguay, and east-central Argentina",,NE,,royter1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/royter1/,avibase-719935EF,,,"Cayenne, ex Daubenton, pi. 988.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/88617#page/80/mode/1up,Sterna maxima
4497,species,Charadriiformes,Laridae,"Skimmers, Noddies, Terns, and Gulls",Thalasseus albididorsalis,"(Hartert, EJO, 1921)","Die Vögel der paläarktischen Fauna. Systematische Übersicht der in Europa, Nord-Asien und der Mittelmeerregion vorkommenden Vögel 2 p.1698",West African Crested Tern,West African Crested Tern,,916,"Taxon albididorsalis is treated as a species separate from Thalasseus maximus based on differences in morphology and vocalizations (Dufour & Crochet 2020), as well as genetics (Collinson et al. 2017). Mitochondrial and nuclear DNA data both indicate that T. maximus sensu lato is not monophyletic, with albididorsalis being more closely aligned with T. bengalensis.",breeds coastal Mauritania to Guinea; winters to Morocco and Namibia,,NE,,royter2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/royter2/,avibase-CF8461BF,,,"Bale du Levrier, Cape Blanco, Morocco.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/49568#page/924/mode/1up,Sterna maxima albididorsalis
