4711,species,Sphenisciformes,Spheniscidae,Penguins,Eudyptes chrysocome,"(Forster, JR, 1781)","Commentationes Societatis Regiae Scientiarum Gottingensis 3(1780) p.133,135",Western Rockhopper Penguin,,,709,"Taxon filholi is treated as a species separate from Eudyptes chrysocome based on genomic DNA divergence (Frugone et al. 2021), supported by differences in bare parts color and possibly other traits (e.g., eyebrow shape, species of feather lice). However, vocalizations of the two taxa seem similar and require formal assessment.",breeds far southern Chilean islands of Magallanes Province to Cape Horn Archipelago and Falkland Islands; winters northward along Patagonian coast,,NE,,rocpen2,,avibase-ECEE0622,,,"Tasmania and Falkland Islands = Falkland Islands; further restricted to Kidney Island, Berkeley Sound, East Falkland Island, by Carins, 1974, Emu, 74, p. 56.",,,Aptenodytes chrysocome
4712,species,Sphenisciformes,Spheniscidae,Penguins,Eudyptes filholi,"Hutton, FW, 1879",Proceedings of the Linnean Society of New South Wales 3 p.334,Eastern Rockhopper Penguin,,,709,"Taxon filholi is treated as a species separate from Eudyptes chrysocome based on genomic DNA divergence (Frugone et al. 2021), supported by differences in bare parts color and possibly other traits (e.g., eyebrow shape, species of feather lice). However, vocalizations of the two taxa seem similar and require formal assessment.","breeds coastally on Prince Edward, Crozet, Kerguelen, Heard (southern Indian Ocean), Macquarie (southeast of Australia), and Auckland, Campbell, and Antipodes islands (New Zealand)",,NE,,rocpen3,,avibase-D5A715E4,,,Campbell Island.,"On an apparently new species of Penguin, from Campbell Island.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/30232#page/396/mode/1up,Eudyptes filholi
4713,species,Sphenisciformes,Spheniscidae,Penguins,Eudyptes moseleyi,"Mathews, GM; Iredale, T, 1921",A manual of the birds of Australia 1 p.11,Northern Rockhopper Penguin,Moseley's Rockhopper Penguin,Northern Rockhopper Penguin,,,"breeds among coastal rocks and tussocks of Tristan da Cunha group and Gough (South Atlantic), and St. Paul and Amsterdam islands (South Indian Ocean)",,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22734408,rocpen4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rocpen4/,avibase-8722DFC2,,,Inaccessible Island.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/70888#page/39/mode/1up,Eudyptes serresianus moseleyi
