4719,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Phoebastria immutabilis,"(Rothschild, LW, 1893)","Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 1, no.9 p.48",Laysan Albatross,Laysan Albatross,Laysan Albatross,,,breeds western Hawaiian and Revillagigedo islands; ranges North Pacific,,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698365,layalb,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/layalb/,avibase-98FB6D4B,,,Laysan Island.,[Description of a new species of Albatross].,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101092#page/74/mode/1up,Diomedea immutabilis
4720,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Phoebastria nigripes,"(Audubon, JJ, 1839)",Ornithological Biography (etc.) 5 p.327,Black-footed Albatross,Black-footed Albatross,Black-footed Albatross,,,"breeds western Hawaiian Islands, and Izu, Bonin, and southern Ryukyu islands (southern Japan); ranges North Pacific from Bering Sea to Tropic of Cancer",,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698350,bkfalb,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkfalb/,avibase-EE8ECB1D,,,"Pacific Ocean, lat. 30° 44' N., long. 146° W.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/103786#page/371/mode/1up,Diomedea nigripes
4721,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Phoebastria albatrus,"(Pallas, PS, 1769)","Spicilegia zoologica, quibus novae imprimis et obscurae animalium species iconibus, descriptionibus atque commentariis illustrantur 1 fasc.5 p.28",Short-tailed Albatross,Short-tailed Albatross,Short-tailed Albatross,,,breeds Torishima (Izu Islands) and Senkaku Islands; ranges through North Pacific,,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698335,shtalb,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/shtalb/,avibase-B5565AD8,,,off Kamchatka.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/88609#page/218/mode/1up,Diomedea albatrus
4722,genus,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Diomedea,"Linnaeus, C, 1758","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.132",,,,,,,,,,,,,F,"Diomedea exulans [Linnaeus, 1758]; type by subsequent designation (Gray, GR, 1840, A List of the Genera of Birds, p. 78).",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/150/mode/1up,Diomedea
4723,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Diomedea sanfordi,"Murphy, RC, 1917",Bulletin of the American Museum of Natural History 37 p.861,Northern Royal Albatross,Northern Royal Albatross,Northern Royal Albatross,883,"Taxon sanfordi is treated as a monotypic species separate from Diomedea epomophora based primarily on differences in morphology and plumage, supported by mitochondrial DNA data (Robertson & Nunn 1998). However, occasional interbreeding has been reported and a more thorough investigation of gene flow and divergence across the main breeding populations is desirable.","breeds mostly Sisters and Forty Fours (Chatham Islands), also Otago Peninsula of southeastern South Island (New Zealand); ranges all southern temperate and subantarctic oceans, mostly Pacific",,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22728323,royalb3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/royalb3/,avibase-1A5E5AE7,,,"Off Corral, Chile.",A new Albatross from the west coast of South America.,https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/1841,Diomedea (Rhothonia) sanfordi
4724,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Diomedea epomophora,"Lesson, RP, 1825",Annales des Sciences Naturelles 6 p.95,Southern Royal Albatross,Southern Royal Albatross,Southern Royal Albatross,883,"Taxon sanfordi is treated as a monotypic species separate from Diomedea epomophora based primarily on differences in morphology and plumage, supported by mitochondrial DNA data (Robertson & Nunn 1998). However, occasional interbreeding has been reported and a more thorough investigation of gene flow and divergence across the main breeding populations is desirable.",breeds Enderby Island (Auckland Islands) and Campbell Islands (New Zealand); ranges all south temperate and subantarctic oceans,,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698314,royalb2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/royalb2/,avibase-4D8C9B97,,,"No type locality given in original description, = Campbell Island.","Distribution géographique de quelques OISEAUX marins, observés dans le Voyage autour du Monde de la Corvette La Coquille.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/28624#page/103/mode/1up,Diomedaea epomophora
4725,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Diomedea exulans,"Linnaeus, C, 1758","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.132",Snowy Albatross,Snowy Albatross,Snowy Albatross,882,"Four species are recognized in the Diomedea exulans complex based primarily on differences in morphology and plumage, supported by a combination of mitochondrial DNA (Burg & Croxall 2004; Chambers et al. 2009; Rains et al. 2011) and microsatellite data (Burg & Croxall 2004): D. exulans; D. dabbenena; D. antipodensis (polytypic, including gibsoni); and D. amsterdamensis. Furthermore, the geographic distribution of taxa indicates parapatry or partial sympatry between circumpolar exulans and the remaining subantarctic taxa.","breeds high-latitude islands of South Georgia, Prince Edward, Crozet, Heard, Kerguelen, and Macquarie islands; ranges all southern oceans",,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698305,wanalb1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/wanalb1/,avibase-A28D8D38,,,intra tropicos Pelagi ad. Cap. b. Spei' = Cape of Good Hope ex Edwards.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/150/mode/1up,Diomedea exulans
4726,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Diomedea dabbenena,"Mathews, GM, 1929",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 50 p.11,Tristan Albatross,Tristan Albatross,Tristan Albatross,882,"Four species are recognized in the Diomedea exulans complex based primarily on differences in morphology and plumage, supported by a combination of mitochondrial DNA (Burg & Croxall 2004; Chambers et al. 2009; Rains et al. 2011) and microsatellite data (Burg & Croxall 2004): D. exulans; D. dabbenena; D. antipodensis (polytypic, including gibsoni); and D. amsterdamensis. Furthermore, the geographic distribution of taxa indicates parapatry or partial sympatry between circumpolar exulans and the remaining subantarctic taxa.",breeds Inaccessible and Gough islands (Tristan da Cunha group); ranges subtropical and temperate southern Atlantic Ocean,,CR,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22728364,wanalb3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/wanalb3/,avibase-1048BC8A,,,,"Descriptions of a new genus, new forms, and new names.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/125292#page/45/mode/1up,Diomedea dabbenena
4727,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Diomedea antipodensis,"Robertson, CJR; Warham, J, 1992",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 112 p.74,Antipodean Albatross,Antipodean Albatross,Antipodean Albatross,882,"Four species are recognized in the Diomedea exulans complex based primarily on differences in morphology and plumage, supported by a combination of mitochondrial DNA (Burg & Croxall 2004; Chambers et al. 2009; Rains et al. 2011) and microsatellite data (Burg & Croxall 2004): D. exulans; D. dabbenena; D. antipodensis (polytypic, including gibsoni); and D. amsterdamensis. Furthermore, the geographic distribution of taxa indicates parapatry or partial sympatry between circumpolar exulans and the remaining subantarctic taxa.",,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22728318,antalb1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/antalb1/,avibase-89706CA9,,,,Nomenclature of the New Zealand Wandering Albatrosses Diomedea exulans.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/123709#page/374/mode/1up,Diomedea exulans antipodensis
4728,subspecies,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Diomedea antipodensis antipodensis,"Robertson, CJR; Warham, J, 1992",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 112 p.74,,,,,,breeds mostly Antipodes Islands and (small numbers) Pitt and Campbell islands (New Zealand); ranges to Tasman Sea (east of Australia) eastward across southern Pacific Ocean,,,,wanalb2,,avibase-4C26D29D,,,,Nomenclature of the New Zealand Wandering Albatrosses Diomedea exulans.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/123709#page/374/mode/1up,Diomedea exulans antipodensis
4729,subspecies,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Diomedea antipodensis gibsoni,"Robertson, CJR; Warham, J, 1992",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 112 p.76,,,,,,breeds Auckland Islands (New Zealand); ranges at least from Tasman Sea eastward to mid-Pacific Ocean,,,,wanalb4,,avibase-282962B4,,,,Nomenclature of the New Zealand Wandering Albatrosses Diomedea exulans.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/123709#page/376/mode/1up,Diomedea exulans gibsoni
4730,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Diomedea amsterdamensis,"Roux, J-P; Jouventin, P; Mougin, J-L; Stahl, J-C; Weimerskirch, H, 1983",L'Oiseau et la Revue Française d'Ornithologie 53 p.1,Amsterdam Albatross,Amsterdam Albatross,Amsterdam Albatross,882,"Four species are recognized in the Diomedea exulans complex based primarily on differences in morphology and plumage, supported by a combination of mitochondrial DNA (Burg & Croxall 2004; Chambers et al. 2009; Rains et al. 2011) and microsatellite data (Burg & Croxall 2004): D. exulans; D. dabbenena; D. antipodensis (polytypic, including gibsoni); and D. amsterdamensis. Furthermore, the geographic distribution of taxa indicates parapatry or partial sympatry between circumpolar exulans and the remaining subantarctic taxa.",breeds Amsterdam Island (French subantarctic islands); ranges mainly south Indian Ocean,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698310,wanalb5,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/wanalb5/,avibase-D93548A7,,,,"Un nouvel albatros Diomedea amsterdamensis n. sp. découvert sur l'île Amsterdam (37°50'S, 77°35'E).",https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Jean-Paul-Roux/publication/280133184,Diomedea amsterdamensis
4731,genus,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Phoebetria,"Reichenbach, HGL, 1853",Avium Systema Naturale. Das natürliche System der Vögel mit hundert Tafeln grösstentheils Original-Abbildungen der bis jetzt entdecken fast zwölfhundert typischen Formen. Vorlaüfer einer Iconographie der Arten der Vögel aller Welttheile lfr.3DieVogel p.V,,,,,,,,,,,,,F,"Diomedea fuliginosa [Gmelin, JF, 1789]; type by original designation = Diomedea palpebrata J.R. Forster, 1785",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/183487#page/61/mode/1up,Phoebetria
4732,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Phoebetria palpebrata,"(Forster, JR, 1785)","Mémoires de mathématique et de physique, presentés à l'Académie royale des sciences, par divers savans, et lûs dans ses assemblées 10 p.571 pl.15",Light-mantled Albatross,Light-mantled Albatross,Light-mantled Albatross,,,breeds circumpolar subantarctic islands; ranges through subantarctic and Antarctic oceans,,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698448,limalb1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/limalb1/,avibase-1819ECCE,,,"'depuis le degre quarante-septieme de latitude australe jusqu'au soixanteonzieme et dix minutes' = south of Prince Edward and Marion Islands, fide Mathews, 1934, Novit. Zool., 39, p. 157.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46986#page/419/mode/1up,Diomedea palpebrata
4733,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Phoebetria fusca,"(Hilsenberg, CT, 1822)",Notizen aus dem Gebiete der Natur- und Heilkunde 3 col.74,Sooty Albatross,Sooty Albatross,Sooty Albatross,,,breeds temperate zone islands of South Atlantic and south Indian oceans; ranges through temperate zone of those oceans,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698431,sooalb1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/sooalb1/,avibase-4976BF1D,,,Mozambique Channel.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46986#page/419/mode/1up,Diomedea fusca
4734,genus,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Thalassarche,"Reichenbach, HGL, 1853",Avium Systema Naturale. Das natürliche System der Vögel mit hundert Tafeln grösstentheils Original-Abbildungen der bis jetzt entdecken fast zwölfhundert typischen Formen. Vorlaüfer einer Iconographie der Arten der Vögel aller Welttheile lfr.3DieVogel p.V,,,,,,,,,,,,,F,"Diomedea melanophris [Temminck, 1828]; type by original designation",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/183487#page/61/mode/1up,Thalassarche
4735,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Thalassarche chlororhynchos,"(Gmelin, JF, 1789)","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I. Pars II 1 pt2 p.568",Atlantic Yellow-nosed Albatross,Atlantic Yellow-nosed Albatross,Atlantic Yellow-nosed Albatross,886,"Taxon carteri is treated as a species separate from Thalassarche chlororhynchos based on differences in plumage, bill coloration and architecture, size, and mitochondrial DNA divergence (Chambers et al. 2009; Abeyrama et al. 2021). However, a low level of mtDNA introgression has been detected in carteri (Abeyrama et al. 2021) indicating that further research is warranted.",breeds Tristan da Cunha and Gough islands; ranges southern oceans,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698425,yenalb2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/yenalb2/,avibase-EA2FA918,,,Cape of Good Hope.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10286#page/69/mode/1up,Diomedea chlororhynchos
4736,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Thalassarche carteri,"(Rothschild, LW, 1903)",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 14 p.6,Indian Yellow-nosed Albatross,Indian Yellow-nosed Albatross,Indian Yellow-nosed Albatross,886,"Taxon carteri is treated as a species separate from Thalassarche chlororhynchos based on differences in plumage, bill coloration and architecture, size, and mitochondrial DNA divergence (Chambers et al. 2009; Abeyrama et al. 2021). However, a low level of mtDNA introgression has been detected in carteri (Abeyrama et al. 2021) indicating that further research is warranted.",breeds on southern Indian Ocean islands; ranges mainly southern Indian Ocean between Tropic of Capricorn and Subtropical Convergence,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22728372,yenalb3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/yenalb3/,avibase-65882F71,,,"Point Cloates, northwestern Australia",On a new species of albatross from NW Australia.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/114181#page/486/mode/1up,Thalassogeron carteri
4737,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Thalassarche chrysostoma,"(Forster, JR, 1785)","Mémoires de mathématique et de physique, presentés à l'Académie royale des sciences, par divers savans, et lûs dans ses assemblées 10 p.571 pl.14",Grey-headed Albatross,Gray-headed Albatross,Grey-headed Albatross,,,breeds circumpolar high southern latitudes; ranges southern oceans mostly south of South Polar Front,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698398,gyhalb,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gyhalb/,avibase-0E4475F6,,,vicinity of the Antarctic Circle and in the Pacific Ocean.,,,Diomedea chrysostoma
4738,species,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Thalassarche melanophris,"(Temminck, CJ, 1828)","Nouveau recueil de planches coloriées d'oiseaux, pour servir de suite et de complément aux planches enluminées de Buffon livr.77, vol.5 pl.456,text",Black-browed Albatross,Black-browed Albatross,,884,"Taxon impavida is treated as a subspecies of Thalassarche melanophris based on available evidence. Although the taxa can be separated based on mitochondrial DNA (Burg & Croxall 2001; Burg et al. 2017) and iris color, there is little evidence of assortative mating on Campbell Island where a few individuals of melanophris occur in the colony of impavida (Alderman et al. 2005). Further study using genomic techniques may clarify the situation.",,,NE,,bkbalb,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkbalb/,avibase-F9FCB9FF,,,Cape of Good Hope.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/110039#page/623/mode/1up,Diomedea melanophris
4739,subspecies,Procellariiformes,Diomedeidae,Albatrosses,Thalassarche melanophris melanophris,"(Temminck, CJ, 1828)","Nouveau recueil de planches coloriées d'oiseaux, pour servir de suite et de complément aux planches enluminées de Buffon livr.77, vol.5 pl.456,text",,,,,,"breeds Antarctic and subantarctic islands including islands off southern Chile, Falkland Islands, South Georgia, South Sandwich, Crozet, Heard and Kerguelen islands, Macquarie Island (southeast of Australia), Antipodes, Snares and Campbell Islands (south of New Zealand); ranges all southern oceans from north of Antarctic Convergence to Tropic of Capricorn",,,,bkbalb1,,avibase-F9CBC9EB,,,Cape of Good Hope.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/110039#page/623/mode/1up,Diomedea melanophris
