4874,species,Procellariiformes,Procellariidae,"Petrels, Shearwaters, and Diving Petrels",Puffinus baroli,"(Bonaparte, CLJL, 1856)",Conspectus generum avium 2 p.204,Barolo Shearwater,Barolo Shearwater,,889,"Taxa boydi and baroli are treated as species separate from Puffinus lherminieri based on a combination of morphological, genomic (Ferrer Obiol et al. 2021, 2022), and multilocus DNA data (Torres et al. 2021). Although morphological characters align boydi with lherminieri, all genetic studies recover boydi and the distinctive-looking baroli as sister taxa, thus supporting a 3-species treatment.","breeds Azores, Madeira including Desertas and Salvage islands, and Canary islands; ranges (rarely) to coasts of southwestern Europe and northwestern Africa, and near shelf-slope break off New England (northeastern USA)",,NE,,litshe1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/litshe1/,avibase-5F555FDD,,,"Mediterranean, Desertas near Madeira, Canary Islands; restricted to Desertas by Bannerman, 1914, Ibis, p. 477.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/141377#page/762/mode/1up,Procellaria baroli
4875,species,Procellariiformes,Procellariidae,"Petrels, Shearwaters, and Diving Petrels",Puffinus boydi,"Mathews, GM, 1912",The birds of Australia 2 p.70,Boyd's Shearwater,Boyd's Shearwater,,889,"Taxa boydi and baroli are treated as species separate from Puffinus lherminieri based on a combination of morphological, genomic (Ferrer Obiol et al. 2021, 2022), and multilocus DNA data (Torres et al. 2021). Although morphological characters align boydi with lherminieri, all genetic studies recover boydi and the distinctive-looking baroli as sister taxa, thus supporting a 3-species treatment.","breeds Cape Verde Islands; ranges (rarely) to Canary Islands, northwestern African coastal waters and Amazon Reef (northeastern South America)",,NE,,litshe2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/litshe2/,avibase-C817F455,,,Cape Verde Islands.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/223654#page/100/mode/1up,Puffinus lherminieri boydi
