4932,species,Procellariiformes,Procellariidae,"Petrels, Shearwaters, and Diving Petrels",Pterodroma gouldi,"(Hutton, FW, 1869)","Ibis ser.2, vol.5, no.19 p.351",Grey-faced Petrel,Gray-faced Petrel,Grey-faced Petrel,,,"breeds on headlands and islands off northern North Island (New Zealand), especially Moutohora Island and Hongiora Island (Bay of Plenty); non-breeding range in deep subtropical water from Tasman Sea (off southeastern Australia) to southern Melanesian waters (southwestern Pacific Ocean)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/45048990,grwpet2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/grwpet2/,avibase-DF92B7F9,,,New Zealand seas.,"[Letter of F. W. Hutton from Auckland, 7th March, 1869].",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/35145#page/393/mode/1up,Aestrelata gouldi
4933,species,Procellariiformes,Procellariidae,"Petrels, Shearwaters, and Diving Petrels",Pterodroma lessonii,"(Garnot, P, 1826)",Annales des Sciences Naturelles 7 p.54 pl.4,White-headed Petrel,White-headed Petrel,White-headed Petrel,,,"breeds subantarctic islands of South Indian and South Pacific oceans, from Crozet to Antipodes and Auckland islands; ranges to southern waters off South America, Africa, Australasia, and Antarctica",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698055,whhpet1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/whhpet1/,avibase-7C787E7D,,,'Dans les parages du Cap Horn et de la mer Pacifique par 52° de lat. sept. [= austr.] et 85° de longit.,"Remarques sur la Zoologie des îles Malouines, faites pendant le Voyage autour du monde de la Corvette la Coquille, éxécuté en 1822, 1823, 1824 et 1825.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/28626#page/68/mode/1up,Procellaria Lessonii
4934,species,Procellariiformes,Procellariidae,"Petrels, Shearwaters, and Diving Petrels",Pterodroma macroptera,"(Smith, A, 1840)","Illustrations of the zoology of South Africa; consisting chiefly of figures and descriptions of the objects of natural history collected during an expedition into the interior of South Africa, in the years 1834, 1835, and 1836 pt.11 pl.52,text",Great-winged Petrel,Great-winged Petrel,Great-winged Petrel,,,"breeds on subtropical to temperate islands from Tristan da Cunha and Gough (south-central South Atlantic Ocean) to Kerguelen Island (southern Indian Ocean), and Eclipse and Coffin islands (off southwestern Australia); non-breeding range in subtropical to temperate South Atlantic and southern Indian oceans from east of southern South America to southern Australian waters",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/45048812,grwpet3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/grwpet3/,avibase-508E7E59,,,Cape seas.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/210547#page/219/mode/1up,Procellaria macroptera
4935,species,Procellariiformes,Procellariidae,"Petrels, Shearwaters, and Diving Petrels",Pterodroma hasitata,"(Kuhl, H, 1820)",Beiträge zur Zoologie und vergleichenden Anatomie 1 p.142,Black-capped Petrel,Black-capped Petrel,Black-capped Petrel,890,"Extinct taxon caribbaea is treated as a monotypic species separate from Pterodroma hasitata based on consistent differences in plumage, tarsal coloration, size, and proportions, combined with data on mitochondrial DNA divergence (Manly et al. 2013) and feather lice. Sometimes considered a dark morph of hasitata, the combined evidence suggests that caribbaea is better treated as a separate species.","breeds montane Hispaniola (""Black-faced"") and Dominica (""White-faced""), perhaps also southeastern Cuba and northeastern Jamaica; extinct as a breeder Guadeloupe; ranges to Gulf Stream off southern Canada to North Carolina and throughout Caribbean",,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698092,bkcpet,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkcpet/,avibase-DCD73C3A,,,no locality.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/89679#page/156/mode/1up,Procellaria hasitata
4936,species,Procellariiformes,Procellariidae,"Petrels, Shearwaters, and Diving Petrels",Pterodroma caribbaea,"Carte, A, 1866","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1866, pt.1 p.93 pl.11",Jamaican Petrel,Jamaican Petrel,Jamaican Petrel,,,formerly bred montane eastern Jamaica; probably extinct ca. 1936,Possibly Extinct,CR (PE),https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698097,bkcpet2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkcpet2/,avibase-8B2FD890,,,"Blue Mountains, Jamaica.",On an Undescribed Species of Petrel from the Blue Mountains of Jamaica.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/90954#page/135/mode/1up,Pterodroma caribbaea
4937,species,Procellariiformes,Procellariidae,"Petrels, Shearwaters, and Diving Petrels",Pterodroma cahow,"(Nichols, JT; Mowbray, LLA, 1916)","The Auk 33, no.2 p.194",Bermuda Petrel,Bermuda Petrel,Bermuda Petrel,890,"Extinct taxon caribbaea is treated as a monotypic species separate from Pterodroma hasitata based on consistent differences in plumage, tarsal coloration, size, and proportions, combined with data on mitochondrial DNA divergence (Manly et al. 2013) and feather lice. Sometimes considered a dark morph of hasitata, the combined evidence suggests that caribbaea is better treated as a separate species.",breeds Nonsuch Island (Bermuda); disperses to Gulf Stream,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698088,berpet,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/berpet/,avibase-F6533C4B,,,"southeastern side of Castle Island, Bermuda.",Two new forms of Petrels from the Bermudas.,https://sora.unm.edu/sites/default/files/journals/auk/v033n02/p0194-p0195.pdf,Aestrelata cahow
