5104,species,Suliformes,Phalacrocoracidae,Cormorants and Shags,Leucocarbo atriceps,"(King, PP, 1828)","The Zoological Journal 4, no.13 p.102",Imperial Shag,,,897,"Six taxa often previously considered species are treated as subspecies of Leucocarbo atriceps (polytypic, including verrucosus, nivalis, melanogenis, purpurascens, bransfieldensis, and georgianus) based on multilocus DNA evidence (Rawlence et al. 2022). Despite being widely separated on subantarctic islands and their sedentary nature, taxa in the L. atriceps complex are only weakly diverged in plumage and in mitochondrial and nuclear DNA. An expanded L. atriceps is recognized pending further research on taxonomic limits within this complex.",,,NE,,,,avibase-20ADDF78,,,Straits of Magellan.,"X. Extracts from a Letter addressed [from Adventure, Rio de Janeiro, July, 8, 1827] by Capt. Philip Parker King, R.N., F.R.S. and L.S., to N. A. Vigors, Esq., on the Animals of the Straits of Magellan [Concluded from Vol. III. p. 432.]",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/87902#page/114/mode/1up,Phalacrocorax atriceps
