5293,genus,Pelecaniformes,Ardeidae,"Herons, Egrets, and Bitterns",Gorsachius,"Bonaparte, CLJL, 1855",Conspectus generum avium 2 p.138,,,,899,"Gorsachius is treated as 3 genera based on the genomic and mitochondrial DNA data of Hruska et al. (2023): monospecific Calherodius (C. leuconotus) and monospecific Oroanassa (O. magnifica), with taxa goisagi and melanolophus retained in Gorsachius. Although Hruska et al. (2023) proposed combining leuconotus and magnificus in Calherodius, these taxa are deeply diverged and occur on different continents, prompting treatment as separate genera.",,,,,,,,M,"Nycticorax goisagi [Temminck, 1836]; type by monotypy",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/141377#page/696/mode/1up,Gorsachius
