5325,species,Pelecaniformes,Ardeidae,"Herons, Egrets, and Bitterns",Egretta gularis,"(Bosc, LAG, 1792)","Actes de la Société d'Histoire Naturelle de Paris 1, pt.1 p.4 pl.2",Western Reef Heron,Western Reef-Heron,,905,"Taxon dimorpha is treated as a subspecies of Egretta garzetta (polytypic, including Australasian immaculata) based on available evidence. Sometimes split as a separate species, or treated as a subspecies of gularis, based largely on the presence of a dark morph, the bare parts color and bill form suggest that dimorpha is better treated as a subspecies of E. garzetta. Furthermore, the name nigripes is considered invalid (nigripes=immaculata) as some syntypes appear to be of hybrid origin, and phenotypic intermediacy suggests widespread intergradation between garzetta and immaculata in the Sundaic region.",,,NE,,werher,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/werher/,avibase-DF32B1F9,,,Senegal River.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/163187#page/38/mode/1up,Ardea gularis
