5327,subspecies,Pelecaniformes,Ardeidae,"Herons, Egrets, and Bitterns",Egretta gularis schistacea,"(Hemprich, WF; Ehrenberg, CG, 1828)","Symbolae physicae seu icones et descriptiones corporum naturalium novorum aut minus cognitorum quae ex itineribus per Libyam Aegyptum Nubiam Dongolam Syrian Arabiam et Habessianiam publico institutis (etc.) sig.i p.21,pl.6",,,,,,"coastal eastern Africa to Red Sea, Persian Gulf, and southeastern India",,,,wesreh2,,avibase-6D833566,,,Red Sea.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/189249#page/31/mode/1up,"Ardea, Lepterodas, schistacea"
5328,species,Pelecaniformes,Ardeidae,"Herons, Egrets, and Bitterns",Egretta garzetta,"(Linnaeus, C, 1766)",Systema Naturæ. Editio duodecima reformata. Tomus I [part 1] p.237,Little Egret,Little Egret,,905,"Taxon dimorpha is treated as a subspecies of Egretta garzetta (polytypic, including Australasian immaculata) based on available evidence. Sometimes split as a separate species, or treated as a subspecies of gularis, based largely on the presence of a dark morph, the bare parts color and bill form suggest that dimorpha is better treated as a subspecies of E. garzetta. Furthermore, the name nigripes is considered invalid (nigripes=immaculata) as some syntypes appear to be of hybrid origin, and phenotypic intermediacy suggests widespread intergradation between garzetta and immaculata in the Sundaic region.",,,NE,,litegr,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/litegr/,avibase-F2858F9F,,,"'Oriente,' ex Brisson.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/137337#page/241/mode/1up,Ardea Garzetta
5329,subspecies,Pelecaniformes,Ardeidae,"Herons, Egrets, and Bitterns",Egretta garzetta garzetta,"(Linnaeus, C, 1766)",Systema Naturæ. Editio duodecima reformata. Tomus I [part 1] p.237,,,,,,"widespread Eurasia, eastern and southern Africa",,,,litegr1,,avibase-4713982B,,,"'Oriente,' ex Brisson.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/137337#page/241/mode/1up,Ardea Garzetta
5330,subspecies,Pelecaniformes,Ardeidae,"Herons, Egrets, and Bitterns",Egretta garzetta dimorpha,"Hartert, EJO, 1914",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 35 p.14,,,,,,"East African coast and locally inland; Europa Island (southern Mozambique Channel), Aldabra (southwestern Seychelles), and Madagascar",,,,litegr2,,avibase-7C15B36B,,,West Madagascar = southeast coast of Madagascar.,Description of two new Herons.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/100962#page/44/mode/1up,Egretta dimorpha
5331,subspecies,Pelecaniformes,Ardeidae,"Herons, Egrets, and Bitterns",Egretta garzetta immaculata,"(Gould, J, 1846)",The birds of Australia pl.and text,,,,905,"Taxon dimorpha is treated as a subspecies of Egretta garzetta (polytypic, including Australasian immaculata) based on available evidence. Sometimes split as a separate species, or treated as a subspecies of gularis, based largely on the presence of a dark morph, the bare parts color and bill form suggest that dimorpha is better treated as a subspecies of E. garzetta. Furthermore, the name nigripes is considered invalid (nigripes=immaculata) as some syntypes appear to be of hybrid origin, and phenotypic intermediacy suggests widespread intergradation between garzetta and immaculata in the Sundaic region.",Greater Sundas eastward to Australia (except western deserts) and North and South islands (New Zealand),,,,litegr3,,avibase-3CBA55B1,,,"Northern portion of Australia' = Port Essington, Northern Territory, fide Mathews, 1912, Novit. Zool., 18, p. 231.",,,Herodias immaculata
