5481,genus,Caprimulgiformes,Caprimulgidae,Nightjars and Nighthawks,Tepuiornis,"Costa, TVV; van Els, P; Braun, MJ; Whitney, BM; Cleere, N; Sigurðsson, S; Silveira, LF, 2023","Avian Systematics 1, no.6 p.70 [55-99]",,,,1199,"Widespread non-monophyly in some New World caprimulgids (Han et al. 2010; Sigurðsson & Cracraft 2014) is resolved through recognition of eight genera based mostly on the recommendations of Costa et al. (2023): Tepuiornis whitelyi; polytypic Uropsalis (U. segmentata and U. lyra); Quechuavis decussata; polytypic Setopagis (S. heterura, S. maculosa, and S. parvula); Antiurus maculicaudus; polytypic Hydropsalis (H. forcipata, H. cayennensis, H. climacocerca, and H. torquata); Systellura longirostris; and polytypic Eleothreptus (E. candicans and E. anomalus).",,,,,,,,M,"Antrostomus whitelyi [Salvin, 1885]; Type by original designation and monotypy",,"Systematic revision and generic classification of a clade of New World nightjars (Caprimulgidae), with descriptions of new genera from South America",https://www.aviansystematics.org/uploads/texteditor/AS_1_6_PDFA.pdf,Tepuiornis
