5691,species,Caprimulgiformes,Caprimulgidae,Nightjars and Nighthawks,Caprimulgus affinis,"Horsfield, T, 1821","Transactions of the Linnean Society of London 13, pt.1 p.142",Savanna Nightjar,Savanna Nightjar,,708,"Taxon griseatus (polytypic) is treated as a species separate from Caprimulgus affinis based on vocalizations (Sangster et al. 2021a). Although Sangster et al. (2021a) proposed a 3-way split, vocal differences between monticolus and affinis are less pronounced, and show some overlap. Little-known taxon mindanensis (if valid) is treated as a subspecies of C. griseatus based on geography, but was not sampled and future analyses might find that it forms a link between griseatus and affinis. Further research needed as differences in plumage, genetics, and biometrics remain undescribed.",,,NE,,savnig1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/savnig1/,avibase-50EDFCF2,,,Java.,Systematic Arrangement and Description of Birds from the Island of Java.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/13692#page/161/mode/1up,Caprimulgus affinis
