6316,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Colibri thalassinus,"(Swainson, WJ, 1827)","The Philosophical Magazine, New Series n.s., 1 p.441",Mexican Violetear,Mexican Violetear,,283,"Taxon cyanotus (polytypic) is treated as a species separate from Colibri thalassinus (monotypic) based on plumage and genetics. Differences in ventral plumage between thalassinus and nominate cyanotus are clear and consistent, although plumages in the geographically intermediate cabanidis appear more variable. Species status for cyanotus is also supported by large differences in mitochondrial DNA (Quintero & Perktas 2018) and an absence of mitochondrial DNA gene flow from P. cyanotus (Hernandez-Soto et al. 2018); further research on species limits in this complex is needed.",open mountain slopes of southern Mexico to north-central Nicaragua,,NE,,grnvie1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/grnvie1/,avibase-B9BA2058,,,"Temascaltepec, Mexico.","LXXII. A Synopsis of the Birds discovered in Mexico by W. Bullock, F.L.S. and H.S., and Mr. William Bullock, jun..",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/53108#page/457/mode/1up,Trochilus thalassinus
6317,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Colibri cyanotus,"(Bourcier, J, 1843)","Revue Zoologique, par la Société Cuvierienne 6 p.101",Lesser Violetear,Lesser Violetear,,283,"Taxon cyanotus (polytypic) is treated as a species separate from Colibri thalassinus (monotypic) based on plumage and genetics. Differences in ventral plumage between thalassinus and nominate cyanotus are clear and consistent, although plumages in the geographically intermediate cabanidis appear more variable. Species status for cyanotus is also supported by large differences in mitochondrial DNA (Quintero & Perktas 2018) and an absence of mitochondrial DNA gene flow from P. cyanotus (Hernandez-Soto et al. 2018); further research on species limits in this complex is needed.",,,NE,,lesvio1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/lesvio1/,avibase-94CB63F7,,,"Caracas, Venezuela.",Oiseaux-mouches nouveaux.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/19446#page/109/mode/1up,Trochilus cyanotus
