6429,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Coeligena prunellei,"(Bourcier, J, 1843)","Revue Zoologique, par la Société Cuvierienne 6 p.70",Black Inca,Black Inca,Black Inca,,,"montane forest and edge of west slope of eastern Andes of Colombia and both slopes of Serranía de los Yariguíes (Santander, north-central Colombia)",,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22687813,blainc1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/blainc1/,avibase-76079E12,,,"Facativa, Colombia.",Descriptions et figures de plusieurs espèces nouvelles d'oiseaux-mouches.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/19446#page/78/mode/1up,Trochilus Prunellei
6430,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Coeligena torquata,"(Boissonneau, A, 1840)","Revue Zoologique, par la Société Cuvierienne 3 p.6",Collared Inca,Collared Inca,,290,"Coeligena torquata sensu lato is treated as three species based on plumage and genetics: C. torquata (polytypic); C. inca (polytypic, including omissa); and C. conradii (monotypic). Plumage differences among all three are substantial and mitochondrial DNA data (Parra et al. 2009; McGuire et al. 2014) separate torquata and inca at species level; genetic data for conradii, and the less distinctive eisenmanni, are lacking. Further research is needed to determine species limits in this complex.",,,NE,,colinc1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/colinc1/,avibase-A40F87D8,,,"Bogota, Colombia.",Oiseaux nouveaux ou peu connus de Santa-Fé de Bogota.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/48713#page/16/mode/1up,Ornismia torquata
