6436,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Coeligena conradii,"(Bourcier, J, 1847)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.15, no.171 p.45",Green Inca,Green Inca,Green Inca,290,"Coeligena torquata sensu lato is treated as three species based on plumage and genetics: C. torquata (polytypic); C. inca (polytypic, including omissa); and C. conradii (monotypic). Plumage differences among all three are substantial and mitochondrial DNA data (Parra et al. 2009; McGuire et al. 2014) separate torquata and inca at species level; genetic data for conradii, and the less distinctive eisenmanni, are lacking. Further research is needed to determine species limits in this complex.",eastern Andes of Colombia to northwestern Venezuela (Trujillo and Mérida),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22726729,colinc4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/colinc4/,avibase-507994F5,,,Vicinity of Caracas.,Description de quinze espèces de Trochilidées du cabinet de M. Loddiges.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46217#page/547/mode/1up,Trochilus Conradii
6437,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Coeligena inca,"(Gould, J, 1852)",Contributions to ornithology 6 p.136,Gould's Inca,Gould's Inca,Gould's Inca,290,"Coeligena torquata sensu lato is treated as three species based on plumage and genetics: C. torquata (polytypic); C. inca (polytypic, including omissa); and C. conradii (monotypic). Plumage differences among all three are substantial and mitochondrial DNA data (Parra et al. 2009; McGuire et al. 2014) separate torquata and inca at species level; genetic data for conradii, and the less distinctive eisenmanni, are lacking. Further research is needed to determine species limits in this complex.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22726743,colinc3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/colinc3/,avibase-3DC76B80,,,"Coroico, Bolivia.",Descriptions of three new species of Humming Birds.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/209972#page/184/mode/1up,Bourcieria inca
