6456,subspecies,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Coeligena lutetiae albimaculata,"Sánchez Osés, C, 2006",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 126 p.5,,,,,,west slope of the Andes of northwestern Ecuador (Carchi southward to northern Bolívar),,,,buwsta3,,avibase-0000CC03,,,,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/127064#page/7/mode/1up,Coeligena lutetiae albimaculata
6457,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Coeligena consita,"Wetmore, A; Phelps, WH Jr, 1952",Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington 65 p.135,Perija Starfrontlet,Perija Starfrontlet,Perija Starfrontlet,291,"Coeligena bonapartei sensu lato is treated as three monotypic species based on considerable differences in plumage: C. bonapartei; C. eos; and C. consita. Genetic patterns are complex; while eos is separable based on low mitochondrial DNA divergence, bonapartei and consita form a complex with C. helianthea, with haplotypes shared across all three species (Palacios et al. 2019). Limited genomic data also show C. helianthea embedded within this complex as the sister clade to bonapartei (Palacios et al. 2019), indicating genome-wide paraphyly and a history of hybridization; further research is needed.",Sierra de Perijá (Colombia/Venezuela border),,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/61173094,gobsta2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gobsta2/,avibase-ED9636C0,,,,A new form of Hummingbird from the Perija Mountains of Venezuela and Colombia.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/107526#page/333/mode/1up,Coeligena bonapartei consita
6458,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Coeligena bonapartei,"(Boissonneau, A, 1840)","Revue Zoologique, par la Société Cuvierienne 3 p.6",Golden-bellied Starfrontlet,Golden-bellied Starfrontlet,Golden-bellied Starfrontlet,291,"Coeligena bonapartei sensu lato is treated as three monotypic species based on considerable differences in plumage: C. bonapartei; C. eos; and C. consita. Genetic patterns are complex; while eos is separable based on low mitochondrial DNA divergence, bonapartei and consita form a complex with C. helianthea, with haplotypes shared across all three species (Palacios et al. 2019). Limited genomic data also show C. helianthea embedded within this complex as the sister clade to bonapartei (Palacios et al. 2019), indicating genome-wide paraphyly and a history of hybridization; further research is needed.",eastern Andes of Colombia (Boyacá to Bogotá),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/61172969,gobsta1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gobsta1/,avibase-BABFAFDA,,,Bogota.,Oiseaux nouveaux ou peu connus de Santa-Fé de Bogota.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/48713#page/16/mode/1up,Ornismia bonarpartei
6459,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Coeligena eos,"(Gould, J, 1848)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.16, no.180 p.11",Golden-tailed Starfrontlet,Merida Starfrontlet,Golden Starfrontlet,291,"Coeligena bonapartei sensu lato is treated as three monotypic species based on considerable differences in plumage: C. bonapartei; C. eos; and C. consita. Genetic patterns are complex; while eos is separable based on low mitochondrial DNA divergence, bonapartei and consita form a complex with C. helianthea, with haplotypes shared across all three species (Palacios et al. 2019). Limited genomic data also show C. helianthea embedded within this complex as the sister clade to bonapartei (Palacios et al. 2019), indicating genome-wide paraphyly and a history of hybridization; further research is needed.","Andes of western Venezuela (Trujillo, Barinas, Mérida, and Táchira)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/61173059,gobsta4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gobsta4/,avibase-D58197D4,,,'Highlands of New Grenada [error] and Venezuela.',Drafts for a new arrangement of the Trochilidae. (continued from Part XV).,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46216#page/25/mode/1up,Helianthea Eos
