6821,genus,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Cynanthus,"Swainson, WJ, 1827","The Philosophical Magazine, New Series n.s., 1 p.441",,,,,,,,,,,,,M,"Cynanthus latirostris [Swainson, 1827]; type by subsequent designation (Stone, 1907, Auk, 24, p. 192).",,"LXXII. A Synopsis of the Birds discovered in Mexico by W. Bullock, F.L.S. and H.S., and Mr. William Bullock, jun..",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/53108#page/457/mode/1up,Cynanthus
6822,species,Apodiformes,Trochilidae,Hummingbirds,Cynanthus latirostris,"Swainson, WJ, 1827","The Philosophical Magazine, New Series n.s., 1 p.441",Broad-billed Hummingbird,Broad-billed Hummingbird,Broad-billed Hummingbird,296,"Cynanthus latirostris sensu lato is treated as three species based on plumage and genetics: C. latirostris (polytypic); C. doubledayi (monotypic); and C. lawrencei (monotypic). A combined analysis of nuclear and mitochondrial DNA did not recover C. latirostris sensu lato as monophyletic but placed the phenotypically distinct doubledayi as sister to C. auriceps (Hernández-Baños et al. 2020). Species status for lawrencei is less clear; despite differences in plumage, genetic divergence from latirostris is relatively shallow (Hernández-Baños et al. 2020).",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22725767,brbhum,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/brbhum/,avibase-C29BA985,,,"Tableland of Mexico; probably does not occur there. Valley of Mexico near Mexico City, designated as type locality by Moore, antea, p. 59.","LXXII. A Synopsis of the Birds discovered in Mexico by W. Bullock, F.L.S. and H.S., and Mr. William Bullock, jun..",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/53108#page/457/mode/1up,Cynanthus latirostris
