7172,species,Strigiformes,Tytonidae,Bay Owls and Barn Owls,Tyto novaehollandiae,"(Stephens, JF, 1826)","General Zoology, or systematic natural history 13, pt2 p.61",Australasian Masked Owl,,Australasian Masked-owl,"450, 451","450)) Tyto almae is a recently described taxon, known from a single specimen (Jønsson et al. 2013). Morphological differences from Tyto sororcula (also known from very few specimens) are slight, and the available genetic data (mitochondrial DNA only) suggest that neither almae nor Tyto sororcula show significant genetic divergence from Tyto novaehollandiae (Jønsson et al. 2013; Uva et al. 2018). 451)) Taxon manusi (monotypic) and sororcula (polytypic, including cayelii) are retained in Tyto novaehollandiae based on genetic evidence. Limited mitochondrial DNA data suggest that manusi and sororcula are embedded within T. novaehollandiae (Uva et al. 2018), but broader genomic sampling and documentation of vocalizations are needed to better understand relationships among these taxa, including the equally distinctive castanops.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/230023167,,,avibase-A953B080,,,New Holland = New South Wales.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/113482#page/89/mode/1up,Strix (?) Novae Hollandiae
