7605,species,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Otus rutilus,"(Pucheran, J, 1849)","Revue et Magasin de Zoologie Pure et Appliquée (2), 1 p.29,note",Madagascar Scops Owl,Madagascar Scops-Owl,Madagascar Scops-owl,373,"Taxon madagascariensis is treated as conspecific with Otus rutilus based on available evidence. Sometimes split based on differences in vocalizations, plumage, and habitat (Rasmussen et al. 2000), variation in vocalizations may be clinal or intergrading. In addition, mitochondrial DNA-dominated data (Fuchs et al. 2007a; Pons et al. 2013) show low levels of divergence between madagascariensis and rutilus. A geographically comprehensive analysis of vocalizations and genetics is needed.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22735960,madsco1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/madsco1/,avibase-C1B0BDEA,,,Madagascar.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/19604#page/35/mode/1up,Scops rutilus
