7653,genus,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Bubo,"Duméril, AMC, 1805","Zoologie analytique, ou méthode naturelle de classification des animaux, rendue plus facile à l'aide de tableaux synoptiques p.34",,,,384,"The genus Ketupa (polytypic, comprising blakistoni, ketupu, zeylonensis and flavipes) is expanded to include eight species previously placed in Bubo; four of these (poensis, lactea, nipalensis, and sumatrana) group with Ketupa sensu stricto based on genetic data (Omote et al. 2013; Salter et al. 2020; Wink & Sauer-Gürth 2021), while the remaining four (shelleyi, coromanda, leucosticta, and philippensis) are provisionally placed in Ketupa based on morphology. This arrangement recognizes three genera: a reduced Bubo (Old and New World taxa); an expanded Ketupa (tropical Afro-Asian taxa); and the morphologically distinct Scotopelia, recovered as the sister clade to Ketupa based on genomic data (Salter et al. 2020), or embedded within it based on mitochondrial DNA (Wink & Sauer-Gürth 2021); further research needed.",,,,,,,,M,"Strix bubo [Linnaeus, 1758]; type by subsequent monotypy (Froriep, 1806, C. Dumeril's Analytische Zoologie, p. 35).",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/97389#page/74/mode/1up,Bubo
