7698,genus,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Scotopelia,"Bonaparte, CLJL, 1850",Conspectus generum avium 1 p.44,,,,384,"The genus Ketupa (polytypic, comprising blakistoni, ketupu, zeylonensis and flavipes) is expanded to include eight species previously placed in Bubo; four of these (poensis, lactea, nipalensis, and sumatrana) group with Ketupa sensu stricto based on genetic data (Omote et al. 2013; Salter et al. 2020; Wink & Sauer-Gürth 2021), while the remaining four (shelleyi, coromanda, leucosticta, and philippensis) are provisionally placed in Ketupa based on morphology. This arrangement recognizes three genera: a reduced Bubo (Old and New World taxa); an expanded Ketupa (tropical Afro-Asian taxa); and the morphologically distinct Scotopelia, recovered as the sister clade to Ketupa based on genomic data (Salter et al. 2020), or embedded within it based on mitochondrial DNA (Wink & Sauer-Gürth 2021); further research needed.",,,,,,,,F,"Strix peli [Temminck]; type by monotypy = Scotopelia peli Bonaparte, 1850",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/141467#page/88/mode/1up,Scotopelia
7699,species,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Scotopelia peli,"(Bonaparte, CLJL, 1850)",Conspectus generum avium 1 p.44,Pel's Fishing Owl,Pel's Fishing-Owl,Pel's Fishing-owl,,,locally in riverine forest of sub-Saharan Africa,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22689032,pefowl1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/pefowl1/,avibase-034B2A6A,,,Ashanti.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/141467#page/88/mode/1up,Strix peli
7700,species,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Scotopelia ussheri,"Sharpe, RB, 1871","Ibis ser.3, vol.1 p.101 pl.12",Rufous Fishing Owl,Rufous Fishing-Owl,Rufous Fishing-owl,,,"rainforest of Sierra Leone, Liberia, Ivory Coast, and Ghana",,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22689038,rufowl1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rufowl1/,avibase-F07B8BD1,,,"Fanti, Gold Coast.",Description of Two new Species of African Birds.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/35065#page/129/mode/1up,Scotopelia ussheri
7701,species,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Scotopelia bouvieri,"Sharpe, RB, 1875","Ibis ser.3, vol.5 p.260",Vermiculated Fishing Owl,Vermiculated Fishing-Owl,Vermiculated Fishing-owl,,,"southern Cameroon to Central African Republic, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Gabon, and northern Angola",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22689048,vefowl1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/vefowl1/,avibase-E0D3E4C1,,,"Lop6, Ogowe River, Gaboon.",Contributions to a History of the Accipitres. Notes on Birds of Prey in the Museum at the Jardin des Plantes and in the Collection of Mons. A. Bouvier.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/35133#page/292/mode/1up,Scotopelia bouvieri
7702,genus,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Ketupa,"Lesson, RP, 1830","Traité d'Ornithologie, ou Tableau Méthodique des ordres, sous-ordres, familles, tribus, genres, sous-genres et races d'oiseaux livr.2 p.114",,,,384,"The genus Ketupa (polytypic, comprising blakistoni, ketupu, zeylonensis and flavipes) is expanded to include eight species previously placed in Bubo; four of these (poensis, lactea, nipalensis, and sumatrana) group with Ketupa sensu stricto based on genetic data (Omote et al. 2013; Salter et al. 2020; Wink & Sauer-Gürth 2021), while the remaining four (shelleyi, coromanda, leucosticta, and philippensis) are provisionally placed in Ketupa based on morphology. This arrangement recognizes three genera: a reduced Bubo (Old and New World taxa); an expanded Ketupa (tropical Afro-Asian taxa); and the morphologically distinct Scotopelia, recovered as the sister clade to Ketupa based on genomic data (Salter et al. 2020), or embedded within it based on mitochondrial DNA (Wink & Sauer-Gürth 2021); further research needed.",,,,,,,,F,"Ketupa javanensis [Lesson, 1830]; type by virtual tautonymy = Strix ketupu Horsfield, 1821  ",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/111050#page/152/mode/1up,Ketupa
