7765,subspecies,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Megascops koepckeae hockingi,"Fjeldså, J; Baiker, J; Engblom, G; Franke, I; Geale, D; Krabbe, NK; Lane, DF; Lezana, M; Schmitt, F; Williams, RSR; Ugarte-Núñez, J; Yábar, V; Yábar, R, 2012","Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 132, no.3 p.189 [180-193]",,,,,,inter-Andean valleys of central Peru,,,,apusco1,,avibase-9C5A5C3E,,,"C'onoq [= Cconoc] am Rio Apurimac, Apurimac, Peru",Reappraisal of Koepcke’s Screech Owl (Megascops koepckeae) and description of a new subspecies,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/229127#page/55/mode/1up,Megascops koepckeae hockingi
7766,species,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Megascops ingens,"(Salvin, O, 1897)",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 6 p.37,Rufescent Screech Owl,Rufescent Screech-Owl,Rufescent Screech-owl,"395, 396","395)) Taxon colombianus is treated as a subspecies of Otus ingens based on vocalizations and genetics. Although morphological differences between ingens and colombianus (Fitzpatrick & O'Neill 1986) are apparent (e.g., tarsal length and extent of tarsal feathering), vocalizations (Krabbe 2017), and mitochondrial DNA divergence (Dantas et al. 2019) are more consistent with subspecies-level divergence. 396)) Taxon aequatorialis is not recognized, as it is a junior synonym of nominate Megascops ingens (Traylor 1952).",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/232594776,rufsco1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rufsco1/,avibase-CA408A36,,,"Jima, Ecuador.",On new species of Scops.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101092#page/397/mode/1up,Scops ingens
