7772,species,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Megascops hoyi,"(König, C; Straneck, RJ, 1989)",Stuttgarter Beiträge zur Naturkunde 428 p.4,Yungas Screech Owl,Montane Forest Screech-Owl,Yungas Screech-owl,,,montane forest of southern Bolivia and northwestern Argentina,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22733712,mofsco1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/mofsco1/,avibase-A910C62B,,,,Eine neue Eule (Aves: Strigidae) aus Nordargentinien.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/104208#page/12/mode/1up,Otus hoyi
7773,species,Strigiformes,Strigidae,Owls,Megascops guatemalae,"(Sharpe, RB, 1875)",Catalogue of the birds in the British Museum 2 p.112 pl.9,Middle American Screech Owl,Middle American Screech-Owl,,"377, 382","377)) Although sometimes split as a monotypic species, taxon vermiculatus is treated as a subspecies of Megascops guatemalae based on available evidence. Limited vocal data suggest that the song of vermiculatus is close to that of M. guatemalae (Krabbe 2017) but a formal bioacoustic analysis is lacking. Genetic data are also needed as the sample labeled vermiculatus in the mitochondrial DNA phylogeny of Dantas et al. (2016) appears to be taxon centralis based on locality. 382)) Taxon centralis (monotypic) and taxon roraimae (polytypic, including pallidus and napensis) are treated as separate species within Megascops based on vocalizations and genetics. Sometimes included in M. guatemalae or M. vermiculatus, centralis is vocally the most distinctive (Krabbe 2017), and mitochondrial DNA data (Dantas et al. 2016) support separation of roraimae from the M. guatemalae complex.",,,NE,,vesowl,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/vesowl/,avibase-024EB09F,,,Guatemala.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/34313#page/128/mode/1up,Scops guatemalae
