7995,species,Accipitriformes,Accipitridae,"Kites, Old World Vultures, Eagles, and Hawks",Chondrohierax wilsonii,"(Cassin, J, 1847)",Proceedings of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Philadelphia 3 p.199,Cuban Kite,Cuban Kite,Cuban Kite,353,"Taxon wilsonii is treated as a monotypic species separate from Chondrohierax uncinatus (polytypic, including mirus) based on combined morphological and genetic evidence. The island endemic C. wilsonii is smaller in size, possesses a larger, all-yellow bill, and is the most distinctive taxon based on mitochondrial DNA divergences (Johnson et al. 2007). These differences are considered significant given the presence of weak geographic structure in variation within Chondrohierax uncinatus across the rest of its extensive geographic range.",varied lowland forest and woodland types in far eastern Cuba; possibly extinct,(possibly extinct),CR,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22728485,hobkit2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/hobkit2/,avibase-B028452B,,,"near Gibara, Cuba; La Silla, c. 13.5 km south of Gibara, Holguín province, northeast Cuba (Kirwan & Kirconnell 2022)",Description of a new rapacious bird in the Museum of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Philadelphia,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/17669#page/207/mode/1up,Cymindis Wilsonii
7996,species,Accipitriformes,Accipitridae,"Kites, Old World Vultures, Eagles, and Hawks",Chondrohierax uncinatus,"(Temminck, CJ, 1822)","Nouveau recueil de planches coloriées d'oiseaux, pour servir de suite et de complément aux planches enluminées de Buffon livr.18, vol.1 pl.103,104",Hook-billed Kite,Hook-billed Kite,Hook-billed Kite,353,"Taxon wilsonii is treated as a monotypic species separate from Chondrohierax uncinatus (polytypic, including mirus) based on combined morphological and genetic evidence. The island endemic C. wilsonii is smaller in size, possesses a larger, all-yellow bill, and is the most distinctive taxon based on mitochondrial DNA divergences (Johnson et al. 2007). These differences are considered significant given the presence of weak geographic structure in variation within Chondrohierax uncinatus across the rest of its extensive geographic range.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22694971,hobkit,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/hobkit/,avibase-DCB3560C,,,'Vicinity of Rio to the north of Brazil and all of Guiana.',,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/109466#page/387/mode/1up,Falco uncinatus
