8115,species,Accipitriformes,Accipitridae,"Kites, Old World Vultures, Eagles, and Hawks",Circaetus spectabilis,"(Schlegel, H, 1863)",Nederlandsch Tijdschrift voor de Dierkunde 1 p.131 pl.6,Congo Serpent Eagle,Congo Snake-Eagle,Congo Serpent-eagle,354,"Taxon spectabilis is placed in Circaetus, rather than in Dryotriorchis, based on genomic DNA evidence (Catanach et al. 2024) that recovered Circaetus as paraphyletic. However, a three-genus arrangement could also be tenable if a generic name becomes available for the basal clade containing C. cinerascens and C. fasciolatus; this would render Circaetus as monophyletic and allow retention of Dryotriorchis for spectabilis.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22695330,coseag1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/coseag1/,avibase-3DA062BF,,,"St. George Elmina, Gold Coast.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/45346#page/155/mode/1up,Astur spectabilis
