8130,species,Accipitriformes,Accipitridae,"Kites, Old World Vultures, Eagles, and Hawks",Nisaetus kelaarti,"(Legge, WV, 1878)","Ibis ser.4, vol.2, no.6 p.202",Legge's Hawk-Eagle,Legge's Hawk-Eagle,,355,"Taxon kelaarti is treated as a monotypic species separate from Nisaetus nipalensis based on differences in plumage, proportions, vocalizations (Gjershaug et al. 2008), and genetics (Haring et al. 2007; Lerner et al. 2017; Catanach et al. 2024). The treatment of N. kelaarti as a separate species seems well-supported but its position within Nisaetus is unresolved; as phylogenetic reconstructions for kelaarti are based on short mitochondrial DNA segments, denser genetic sampling across Nisaetus is desirable.",southwestern India (Western Ghats) and Sri Lanka,,NE,,mouhae2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/mouhae2/,avibase-38856722,,,Ceylon.,"[Letter from ?, March 4th, 1878].",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/34861#page/238/mode/1up,Spizaetus kelaarti
8131,species,Accipitriformes,Accipitridae,"Kites, Old World Vultures, Eagles, and Hawks",Nisaetus nipalensis,"Hodgson, BH, 1836","Journal of the Asiatic Society of Bengal 5, no.52 p.229 pl.7",Mountain Hawk-Eagle,Mountain Hawk-Eagle,,355,"Taxon kelaarti is treated as a monotypic species separate from Nisaetus nipalensis based on differences in plumage, proportions, vocalizations (Gjershaug et al. 2008), and genetics (Haring et al. 2007; Lerner et al. 2017; Catanach et al. 2024). The treatment of N. kelaarti as a separate species seems well-supported but its position within Nisaetus is unresolved; as phylogenetic reconstructions for kelaarti are based on short mitochondrial DNA segments, denser genetic sampling across Nisaetus is desirable.",,,NE,,mouhae1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/mouhae1/,avibase-9EA9701E,,,Nepal.,Summary Description of some New Species of Falconidae.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/114404#page/277/mode/1up,Nisactus (sic) Nipalensis
