8407,species,Accipitriformes,Accipitridae,"Kites, Old World Vultures, Eagles, and Hawks",Astur atricapillus,"(Wilson, A, 1812)","American Ornithology or, the Natural History of the Birds of the United States: Illustrated with Plates Engraved and Colored from Original Drawings taken from Nature 6 p.80 pl.52 fig.3",American Goshawk,American Goshawk,,710,"Taxon atricapillus (polytypic, including laingi and apache) is treated as a species separate from Astur gentilis based on mitochondrial DNA data (Kunz et al. 2019) that recovered A. gentilis sensu lato as non-monophyletic. The split of A. atricapillus is supported by nuclear DNA evidence (Geraldes et al. 2019), vocalizations, plumage, and iris color (Sangster 2022), although the analysis of vocalizations suffers from incomplete sampling.",,,NE,,norgos,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/norgos/,avibase-AE5956D5,,,"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/175484#page/106/mode/1up,Falco atricapillus
