8450,genus,Accipitriformes,Accipitridae,"Kites, Old World Vultures, Eagles, and Hawks",Microspizias,"Sangster, G; Kirwan, GM; Fuchs, J; Dickinson, EC; Elliott, A; Gregory, SMS, 2021",Vertebrate Zoology 71 p.419-424,,,,1168,"The genus Microspizias is recognized following Sangster et al. (2021) based on osteological evidence (Olson 2006) and deep genetic divergence from other accipitrine hawks (Mindell et al. 2018). Although placed as sister to Kaupifalco, support for this relationship is unclear and geographical, behavioral, and ecological traits suggest they are best treated as separate genera.",,,,,,,,M,"Falco superciliosus [Linnaeus, 1766]",,"A new genus for the tiny hawk Accipiter superciliosus and semicollared hawk A. collaris (Aves: Accipitridae), with comments on the generic name for the crested goshawk A. trivirgatus and Sulawesi goshawk A. griseiceps",https://vertebrate-zoology.arphahub.com/article/67501/,Microspizias
