8639,species,Accipitriformes,Accipitridae,"Kites, Old World Vultures, Eagles, and Hawks",Buteo augur,"(Rüppell, WPES, 1836)",Neue Wirbelthiere zu der Fauna von Abyssinien gehörig. Vögel p.38 pl.16,Augur Buzzard,Augur Buzzard,Augur Buzzard,363,"Taxon archeri is treated as conspecific with Buteo augur, as the evidentiary basis for a split is weak. Sometimes treated as a distinct species, variation in plumage characters suggests it is a rufous color-morph (Clark 2003) or subspecies of B. augur (Clark 1996). Genetic data for archeri are uninformative, being limited to a short section of mitochondrial DNA (Riesing et al. 2003) of uncertain provenance; although aligned with a group that includes augur and rufofuscus, the position of archeri remains poorly resolved.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22732019,augbuz2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/augbuz2/,avibase-EBDC03AA,,,Ethiopia.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/114234#page/118/mode/1up,Falco (Buteo) Augur
