8779,genus,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Priotelus,"Gray, GR, 1840","A list of the genera of birds, with an indication of the typical species of each genus ed. 1 p.10",,,,929,"Taxon roseigaster is placed in the genus Priotelus rather than Temnotrogon based on available evidence. Mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Moyle 2005; Hosner et al. 2010) recovered P. roseigaster and P. temnurus as deeply diverged sister taxa with strong support. Although they also differ substantially in plumage and vocalizations, we consider it more informative to recognize a single genus with two species, an arrangement supported by biogeography and deep genetic intra-generic divergences being typical in trogons.",,,,,,,,M,"Trogon temnurus [Temminck, 1825]; type by monotypy",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/48588#page/24/mode/1up,Priotelus
8780,species,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Priotelus roseigaster,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1817)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 8 p.314",Hispaniolan Trogon,Hispaniolan Trogon,Hispaniolan Trogon,929,"Taxon roseigaster is placed in the genus Priotelus rather than Temnotrogon based on available evidence. Mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Moyle 2005; Hosner et al. 2010) recovered P. roseigaster and P. temnurus as deeply diverged sister taxa with strong support. Although they also differ substantially in plumage and vocalizations, we consider it more informative to recognize a single genus with two species, an arrangement supported by biogeography and deep genetic intra-generic divergences being typical in trogons.",montane forest of Hispaniola; locally in coastal mangroves,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22682751,histro1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/histro1/,avibase-D0BAA2BA,,,Santo Domingo and Mexico.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/60104#page/338/mode/1up,Trogon roseigaster
