8802,species,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon bairdii,"Lawrence, GN, 1868",Annals of the Lyceum of Natural History of New York 9(1870) p.119,Baird's Trogon,Baird's Trogon,Baird's Trogon,,,Pacific slope of southwestern Costa Rica and western Panama,,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22682776,baitro1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/baitro1/,avibase-8FEE6F95,,,"San Mateo, Costa Rica.",A catalogue of the birds found in Costa Rica.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22948#page/135/mode/1up,Trogon bairdii
8803,species,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon caligatus,"Gould, J, 1838","A monograph of the Trogonidae, or family of trogons. 1st ed. pt3 pl.6,text",Gartered Trogon,Gartered Trogon,,932,"Trogon violaceus is split into three species, based in large part on the mitochondrial DNA data of DaCosta & Klicka (2008) that recovered the complex as non-monophyletic, with T. curucui and T. surrucura embedded within it: polytypic T. caligatus (including sallaei and concinnus); monotypic T. violaceus (sister to T. curucui); and polytypic T. ramonianus (including crissalis). Vocalizations reportedly also differ between the three groups but a formal bioacoustic analysis is lacking.",,,NE,,gartro1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gartro1/,avibase-94E42A23,,,"No type locality, but plate agrees with specimens from the Magdalena Valley, Colombia.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/215223#page/23/mode/1up,Trogon caligatus
8804,subspecies,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon caligatus sallaei,"Bonaparte, CLJL, 1856","Comptes Rendus Hebdomadaires des Séances de l'Académie des Sciences 42, no.20 p.955, note",,,,,,tropical southern Mexico (Oaxaca) to Costa Rica,,,,gartro2,,avibase-9842AD36,,,Vera Cruz.,Note sur les Tableaux des Gallinacés.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/16554#page/965/mode/1up,Trogon sallaei
8805,subspecies,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon caligatus concinnus,"Lawrence, GN, 1862",Annals of the Lyceum of Natural History of New York 7 p.463,,,,,,"tropical Panama to Colombia, western Ecuador, and northwestern Peru",,,,gartro3,,avibase-9DD9CA94,,,"'New Grenada' i.e. Lion Hill, Panama.","Catalogue of a collection of birds, made in New Grenada, by James McLeannan, Esq., of New York, with notes and descriptions of new species. Part 3.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/54888#page/495/mode/1up,Trogon concinnus
8806,subspecies,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon caligatus caligatus,"Gould, J, 1838","A monograph of the Trogonidae, or family of trogons. 1st ed. pt3 pl.6,text",,,,,,northern Colombia to western Venezuela (Maracaibo basin),,,,gartro4,,avibase-CA307879,,,"No type locality, but plate agrees with specimens from the Magdalena Valley, Colombia.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/215223#page/23/mode/1up,Trogon caligatus
8807,species,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon violaceus,"Gmelin, JF, 1788","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I [pars I] p.404",Guianan Trogon,Guianan Trogon,,932,"Trogon violaceus is split into three species, based in large part on the mitochondrial DNA data of DaCosta & Klicka (2008) that recovered the complex as non-monophyletic, with T. curucui and T. surrucura embedded within it: polytypic T. caligatus (including sallaei and concinnus); monotypic T. violaceus (sister to T. curucui); and polytypic T. ramonianus (including crissalis). Vocalizations reportedly also differ between the three groups but a formal bioacoustic analysis is lacking.","Venezuela, Trinidad, the Guianas, and adjacent northern Brazil",,NE,,viotro2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/viotro2/,avibase-563C5F5D,,,No locality = Surinam.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10285#page/416/mode/1up,Trogon violaceus
8808,species,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon ramonianus,"Deville, É; des Murs, MAPO, 1849","Revue et Magasin de Zoologie Pure et Appliquée (2), 3 p.331",Amazonian Trogon,Amazonian Trogon,,932,"Trogon violaceus is split into three species, based in large part on the mitochondrial DNA data of DaCosta & Klicka (2008) that recovered the complex as non-monophyletic, with T. curucui and T. surrucura embedded within it: polytypic T. caligatus (including sallaei and concinnus); monotypic T. violaceus (sister to T. curucui); and polytypic T. ramonianus (including crissalis). Vocalizations reportedly also differ between the three groups but a formal bioacoustic analysis is lacking.",,,NE,,viotro3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/viotro3/,avibase-09B20241,,,"Sarayacii and Pampa del Sacramento, Peru.","Note sur une nouvelle espèce de Couroucou (Trogon ramoniana), et sur le Trogon meridionalis.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/19604#page/355/mode/1up,Trogon ramoniana
