8814,subspecies,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon curucui behni,"Gould, J, 1875","A Monograph of the Trogonidae, or Family of Trogons. 2nd ed. ed.2, pt4 pl.6,text [=pl.20 of vol.]",,,,,,"eastern Bolivia to northwestern Argentina, Paraguay, and northern Formosa (north-central Argentina), and Mato Grosso do Sul (south-central Brazil)",,,,buctro3,,avibase-8A4F9162,,,Bolivia.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/267606#page/45/mode/1up,Trogon behni
8815,species,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon surrucura,"Vieillot, LJP, 1817","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 8 p.321",Surucua Trogon,Surucua Trogon,,931,"Taxon aurantius is treated as a subspecies of Trogon surrucura based on available evidence. Despite differences in plumage, vocalizations are not known to differ, mitochondrial DNA divergence is weak (DaCosta 2006), and there is evidence of hybridization (Santos 2012); however, areas of local sympatry have also been reported (Falcão et al. 2017). Further research into their interactions across the contact zone will be needed to clarify species status for aurantius.",,,NE,,surtro1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/surtro1/,avibase-1D555193,,,Paraguay.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/60104#page/345/mode/1up,Trogon surrucura
8816,subspecies,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon surrucura aurantius,"Spix, JB, 1824","Avium species novae, quas in itinere per Brasiliam annis MDCCCXVII-MDCCCXX (etc.) 1 p.47 pl.36",,,,,,eastern Brazil (Minas Gerais to Rio de Janeiro and northern São Paulo),,,,surtro2,,avibase-899C70E6,,,'In sylvis Rio de Janeiro.',,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/128666#page/67/mode/1up,Trogon aurantius
8817,subspecies,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon surrucura surrucura,"Vieillot, LJP, 1817","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 8 p.321",,,,,,"southern Brazil to Paraguay, Uruguay, and northern Argentina",,,,surtro3,,avibase-8F2D3109,,,Paraguay.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/60104#page/345/mode/1up,Trogon surrucura
8818,species,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon tenellus,"Cabanis, JL, 1862","Journal für Ornithologie 10, no.57 p.173",Graceful Black-throated Trogon,Northern Black-throated Trogon,,927,"Trogon rufus is split into four species based largely on the integrative study of plumage, morphometrics, vocalizations, and mitochondrial DNA data by Dickens et al. (2021): a monotypic T. tenellus; a monotypic T. cupreicauda; a polytypic T. rufus (including amazonicus and sulphureus); and a polytypic T. chrysochloros (including newly described muriciensis). Although mitochondrial DNA data support placement of muriciensis in T. chrysochloros, some vocal and plumage traits suggest its affinities may lie elsewhere within this complex or warrant recognition as a full species, as proposed by Dickens et al. (2021); further research needed.",northern Honduras to far northwestern Colombia,,NE,,bkttro7,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkttro7/,avibase-A70C6C93,,,Costa Rica.,"Uebersicht der im Berliner Museum befindlichen Vögel von Costa Rica. (Fortsetzung ; s. Juli-Heft 1861, S. 241-256.)'.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101707#page/195/mode/1up,Trogon tenellus
8819,species,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon cupreicauda,"(Chapman, FM, 1914)",Bulletin of the American Museum of Natural History 33 p.606,Choco Black-throated Trogon,Choco Black-throated Trogon,,927,"Trogon rufus is split into four species based largely on the integrative study of plumage, morphometrics, vocalizations, and mitochondrial DNA data by Dickens et al. (2021): a monotypic T. tenellus; a monotypic T. cupreicauda; a polytypic T. rufus (including amazonicus and sulphureus); and a polytypic T. chrysochloros (including newly described muriciensis). Although mitochondrial DNA data support placement of muriciensis in T. chrysochloros, some vocal and plumage traits suggest its affinities may lie elsewhere within this complex or warrant recognition as a full species, as proposed by Dickens et al. (2021); further research needed.",tropical western Colombia and western Ecuador,,NE,,bkttro5,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkttro5/,avibase-525CCA55,,,"Bagado, 1000 feet, Choco, Colombia.",Diagnoses of apparently new Colombian Birds. III.,https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/1751,Trogonurus curucui cupreicauda
8820,species,Trogoniformes,Trogonidae,Trogons,Trogon rufus,"Gmelin, JF, 1788","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I [pars I] p.404",Amazonian Black-throated Trogon,Amazonian Black-throated Trogon,,927,"Trogon rufus is split into four species based largely on the integrative study of plumage, morphometrics, vocalizations, and mitochondrial DNA data by Dickens et al. (2021): a monotypic T. tenellus; a monotypic T. cupreicauda; a polytypic T. rufus (including amazonicus and sulphureus); and a polytypic T. chrysochloros (including newly described muriciensis). Although mitochondrial DNA data support placement of muriciensis in T. chrysochloros, some vocal and plumage traits suggest its affinities may lie elsewhere within this complex or warrant recognition as a full species, as proposed by Dickens et al. (2021); further research needed.",,,NE,,bkttro6,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkttro6/,avibase-3687A50D,,,Cayenne.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10285#page/416/mode/1up,Trogon rufus
