8915,species,Bucerotiformes,Bucerotidae,Hornbills,Lophoceros semifasciatus,"(Hartlaub, KJG, 1855)","Journal für Ornithologie 3, no.17 p.356",West African Pied Hornbill,West African Pied Hornbill,West African Pied Hornbill,691,"Taxon semifasciatus is treated as a species separate from Lophoceros fasciatus based on differences in plumage as well as bill color and pattern, and a hybrid zone of limited extent (Louette 1981; Marchant 1953). Although mitochondrial DNA data (Gonzalez et al. 2013) indicate deep divergences within this complex, a more comprehensive genetic review is needed to verify this result.",Senegambia to just east of Niger River,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/61612971,afphor2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/afphor2/,avibase-89218876,,,"Rio Boutry, Gold Coast.","Beschreibung einiger neuen, von Herrn H. S. Pel, höllandischem Residenten an der Goldküste, dasselbst gesammelten Vögelarten.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/49380#page/368/mode/1up,Buceros semifasciatus
8916,species,Bucerotiformes,Bucerotidae,Hornbills,Lophoceros fasciatus,"(Shaw, G, 1812)","General Zoology, or systematic natural history 8 pt1 p.34",Congo Pied Hornbill,Congo Pied Hornbill,Congo Pied Hornbill,691,"Taxon semifasciatus is treated as a species separate from Lophoceros fasciatus based on differences in plumage as well as bill color and pattern, and a hybrid zone of limited extent (Louette 1981; Marchant 1953). Although mitochondrial DNA data (Gonzalez et al. 2013) indicate deep divergences within this complex, a more comprehensive genetic review is needed to verify this result.","Nigeria (east of Niger River) to Angola, Democratic Republic of the Congo, and Uganda",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/61612961,afphor3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/afphor3/,avibase-4B8F7AF5,,,Angola.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/64421#page/54/mode/1up,Buceros fasciatus
