8932,species,Bucerotiformes,Bucerotidae,Hornbills,Tockus rufirostris,"(Sundevall, CJ, 1850)","Öfversigt af Kongliga Vetenskaps-Akademiens Förhandlingar 7, no.4 p.108",Southern Red-billed Hornbill,Southern Red-billed Hornbill,,690,"Five species are recognized in the Tockus erythrorhynchus complex based on a combination of plumage, bare parts color, vocalizations, genetics (Kemp & Delport 2002; Viseshakul et al. 2011; Gonzalez et al. 2013), and hybrid zone dynamics (Delport et al. 2004): T. erythrorhynchus; T. ruahae; T. kempi; T. rufirostris; and T. damarensis. Mitochondrial DNA data (Gonzalez et al. 2013) suggested that these may divide into two groups: northern erythrorhynchus, kempi, and ruahae and southern rufirostris and damarensis. Further research is needed in areas of parapatry to assess levels of gene flow and a more comprehensive genetic review would be informative.",Angola and northern Namibia to Mozambique and eastern South Africa,,NE,,srbhor1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/srbhor1/,avibase-73A7F4D0,,,,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/285379#page/118/mode/1up,Buceros rufirostris
8933,species,Bucerotiformes,Bucerotidae,Hornbills,Tockus damarensis,"(Shelley, GE, 1888)","Ibis ser.5, vol.6, no.21 p.58,66",Damara Red-billed Hornbill,Damara Red-billed Hornbill,Damara Red-billed Hornbill,690,"Five species are recognized in the Tockus erythrorhynchus complex based on a combination of plumage, bare parts color, vocalizations, genetics (Kemp & Delport 2002; Viseshakul et al. 2011; Gonzalez et al. 2013), and hybrid zone dynamics (Delport et al. 2004): T. erythrorhynchus; T. ruahae; T. kempi; T. rufirostris; and T. damarensis. Mitochondrial DNA data (Gonzalez et al. 2013) suggested that these may divide into two groups: northern erythrorhynchus, kempi, and ruahae and southern rufirostris and damarensis. Further research is needed in areas of parapatry to assess levels of gene flow and a more comprehensive genetic review would be informative.",central Namibia (southern Damaraland),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22725940,drbhor1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/drbhor1/,avibase-4C4AADAB,,,"Otjimbinque, Damaraland.",On the Hornbills of the Ethiopian Region.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/55018#page/86/mode/1up,Lophoceros damarensis
8934,species,Bucerotiformes,Bucerotidae,Hornbills,Tockus ruahae,"Kemp, AC; Delport, W, 2002",Annals of the Transvaal Museum 39 p.4,Tanzanian Red-billed Hornbill,Tanzanian Red-billed Hornbill,,690,"Five species are recognized in the Tockus erythrorhynchus complex based on a combination of plumage, bare parts color, vocalizations, genetics (Kemp & Delport 2002; Viseshakul et al. 2011; Gonzalez et al. 2013), and hybrid zone dynamics (Delport et al. 2004): T. erythrorhynchus; T. ruahae; T. kempi; T. rufirostris; and T. damarensis. Mitochondrial DNA data (Gonzalez et al. 2013) suggested that these may divide into two groups: northern erythrorhynchus, kempi, and ruahae and southern rufirostris and damarensis. Further research is needed in areas of parapatry to assess levels of gene flow and a more comprehensive genetic review would be informative.",central and southern Tanzania,,NE,,trbhor1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/trbhor1/,avibase-1A34CC23,,,,"Comments on the status of subspecies in the red-billed hornbill (Tockus erythrorhynchus) complex (Aves: Bucerotidae), with the description of a new taxon endemic to Tanzania",https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.541.1124&rep=rep1&type=pdf,Tockus erythrorhynchus ruahae
8935,species,Bucerotiformes,Bucerotidae,Hornbills,Tockus kempi,"Tréca, B; Érard, C, 2000",Ostrich 71 p.363-366,Western Red-billed Hornbill,Western Red-billed Hornbill,,690,"Five species are recognized in the Tockus erythrorhynchus complex based on a combination of plumage, bare parts color, vocalizations, genetics (Kemp & Delport 2002; Viseshakul et al. 2011; Gonzalez et al. 2013), and hybrid zone dynamics (Delport et al. 2004): T. erythrorhynchus; T. ruahae; T. kempi; T. rufirostris; and T. damarensis. Mitochondrial DNA data (Gonzalez et al. 2013) suggested that these may divide into two groups: northern erythrorhynchus, kempi, and ruahae and southern rufirostris and damarensis. Further research is needed in areas of parapatry to assess levels of gene flow and a more comprehensive genetic review would be informative.",Senegambia to (Mali) inner Niger delta,,NE,,wrbhor2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/wrbhor2/,avibase-1ADEF52B,,,,"A new subspecies of the Red-billed Hornbill, Tockus erythrorhynchus from West Africa.",,Tockus erythrorhynchus kempi
8936,species,Bucerotiformes,Bucerotidae,Hornbills,Tockus erythrorhynchus,"(Temminck, CJ, 1823)","Nouveau recueil de planches coloriées d'oiseaux, pour servir de suite et de complément aux planches enluminées de Buffon livr.36, vol.2 text to genus Buceros, sp.19",Northern Red-billed Hornbill,Northern Red-billed Hornbill,,690,"Five species are recognized in the Tockus erythrorhynchus complex based on a combination of plumage, bare parts color, vocalizations, genetics (Kemp & Delport 2002; Viseshakul et al. 2011; Gonzalez et al. 2013), and hybrid zone dynamics (Delport et al. 2004): T. erythrorhynchus; T. ruahae; T. kempi; T. rufirostris; and T. damarensis. Mitochondrial DNA data (Gonzalez et al. 2013) suggested that these may divide into two groups: northern erythrorhynchus, kempi, and ruahae and southern rufirostris and damarensis. Further research is needed in areas of parapatry to assess levels of gene flow and a more comprehensive genetic review would be informative.",Sierra Leone to Somalia and southward to Tanzania,,NE,,rebhor1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rebhor1/,avibase-AF75AC32,,,"Senegal and Guinea; based on Brisson, Buff on and LeVaillant.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/109469#page/130/mode/1up,Buceros erythrorhynchus
