8957,species,Bucerotiformes,Bucerotidae,Hornbills,Bycanistes fistulator,"(Cassin, J, 1850)",Proceedings of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Philadelphia 5 p.68,Piping Hornbill,Piping Hornbill,,697,"Taxon sharpii (polytypic) is treated as a subspecies of Bycanistes fistulator based on available evidence. Morphological differences are slight, some traits (e.g., bill color) are variable within taxa (Dowsett-Lemaire & Dowsett 2014, 2019), and their behavior (including voice) and ecology are similar. Preliminary mitochondrial DNA data (Gonzalez et al. 2013) indicate substantial divergence within the range of sharpii; further research needed to assess levels of gene flow between these taxa.",,,NE,,piphor1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/piphor1/,avibase-2AAFDD00,,,West Africa = Senegal.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/17633#page/88/mode/1up,Buceros Fistulator
