9487,species,Coraciiformes,Alcedinidae,Kingfishers,Actenoides princeps,"(Reichenbach, HGL, 1851)",Handbuch der speciellen Ornithologie no.8 (Alcedineae) p.38 pl.,Scaly-breasted Kingfisher,Scaly-breasted Kingfisher,Scaly-breasted Kingfisher,259,"Taxon regalis (monotypic) is treated as a subspecies of Actenoides princeps (polytypic) based on available evidence. Restricted to montane forest, A. princeps sensu lato is readily separated from its lowland counterpart A. monachus based on combined mitochondrial and nuclear DNA data (Andersen et al. 2018). Despite this, the plumage of regalis is similar to that of immature monachus, suggesting that adult plumages of regalis are unknown. Furthermore, it is likely that additional taxonomic diversity is present within this complex (Rheindt et al. 2014); further research needed to better understand species limits.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22683556,scakin1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/scakin1/,avibase-E26A54EC,,,Celebes.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/183489#page/52/mode/1up,Monachalcyon princeps
