9633,species,Galbuliformes,Galbulidae,Jacamars,Galbula albirostris,"Latham, J, 1790","Index ornithologicus, sive systema ornithologiæ; complectens avium divisionem in classes, ordines, genera, species, ipsarumque varietates: adjectis synonymis, locis, descriptionibus, &c. 1 p.245",Yellow-billed Jacamar,Yellow-billed Jacamar,,267,"Taxon chalcocephala is treated as a subspecies of Galbula albirostris based on available evidence. Apart from crown and outer rectrix color, differences in plumage are minor (Haffer 1974), and there has been no formal analysis of vocalizations. Mitochondrial DNA data do not recover G. albirostris as monophyletic (Ferriera 2018), and relatively deep divergences occur amongst some clades (Naka et al. 2012; Ferriera et al. 2018). Limited genomic data also suggest that G. albirostris is paraphyletic, with G. cyanicollis embedded within it; further research needed.",,,NE,,yebjac1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/yebjac1/,avibase-3F3135FF,,,"South America; Cayenne substituted as type locality by Berlepsch and Hartert, Nov. Zool., 9, 1902, p. 104.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/226470#page/267/mode/1up,Galbula albirostris
