9667,species,Galbuliformes,Bucconidae,Puffbirds,Nystalus radiatus,"(Sclater, PL, 1854)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.21, no.255 p.122 pl.50",Barred Puffbird,Barred Puffbird,Barred Puffbird,,,humid forest of western Panama to western Ecuador,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22682261,barpuf1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/barpuf1/,avibase-4B154EA6,,,"Colombia = Magdalena Valley, fide Chapman, antea.",Descriptions of New Species of Bucconidae.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/96679#page/158/mode/1up,Bucco radiatus
9668,species,Galbuliformes,Bucconidae,Puffbirds,Nystalus obamai,"Whitney, BM; Piacentini, VQ; Schunck, F; Aleixo, ALP; Sousa, BRS; Silveira, LF; Rêgo, MA, 2013",Handbook of the birds of the world p.240-244,Western Striolated Puffbird,Western Striolated-Puffbird,,269,"Taxon obamai is treated as a monotypic species separate from Nystalus striolatus (polytypic, including torridus) following Whitney et al. (2013). While the vocalizations of obamai are distinctive, diagnostic plumage and morphological characters are mostly lacking, and genetic data have produced conflicting results. Contra the preliminary mitochondrial DNA data of Whitney et al. (2013), broader geographic sampling (Duarte 2015) did not recover obamai or striolatus as monophyletic clades, and genomic data (Ferreira 2018) are limited. Furthermore, issues of data quality, small sample sizes, and mislabeling (e.g., Annex 1, Duarte 2015), indicate the need for a thorough genetic review of this complex.","western Amazonia: Ecuador southward to Bolivia and east, south of the Amazon River, to Brazil west of the Rio Madeira",,NE,,wespuf1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/wespuf1/,avibase-012084A9,,,,A name for Striolated Puffbird west of the Rio Madeira with revision of the Nystalus striolatus (Aves: Bucconidae) complex,https://fieldguides.com/files_miscellaneous/HBW-linked/240-244_Original%20Scientific%20Descriptions.pdf,Nystalus obamai
9669,species,Galbuliformes,Bucconidae,Puffbirds,Nystalus striolatus,"(Pelzeln, A, 1856)",Sitzungsberichte der Kaiserlichen Akademie der Wissenschaften. Mathematisch-Naturwissenschaftliche Classe 20 p.500,Eastern Striolated Puffbird,Eastern Striolated-Puffbird,,269,"Taxon obamai is treated as a monotypic species separate from Nystalus striolatus (polytypic, including torridus) following Whitney et al. (2013). While the vocalizations of obamai are distinctive, diagnostic plumage and morphological characters are mostly lacking, and genetic data have produced conflicting results. Contra the preliminary mitochondrial DNA data of Whitney et al. (2013), broader geographic sampling (Duarte 2015) did not recover obamai or striolatus as monophyletic clades, and genomic data (Ferreira 2018) are limited. Furthermore, issues of data quality, small sample sizes, and mislabeling (e.g., Annex 1, Duarte 2015), indicate the need for a thorough genetic review of this complex.",,,NE,,strpuf1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/strpuf1/,avibase-427AF246,,,"Engenho do Gama and No Dourado, Mato Grosso.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/108785#page/608/mode/1up,Bucco striolatus
