10070,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Ramphastos vitellinus,"Lichtenstein, MHC, 1823","Verzeichniss der Doubletten des zoologischen Museums der Königl. Universität zu Berlin nebst Beschreibung vieler bisher unbekannter Arten von Säugethieren, Vögeln, Amphibien und Fischen p.7",Channel-billed Toucan,Channel-billed Toucan,,1189,"Ramphastos vitellinus is treated as a single polytypic species based on available evidence. Sometimes split into 2 or 4 species based on differences in plumage, bill color, and iris color; however, vocal differences have not been properly documented, introgressive hybridisation appears to be extensive, and mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Patané et al. 2009) show evidence of mtDNA capture leading to paraphyly of taxon ariel. A recent genomic DNA analysis (Ostrow et al. 2023a) suggests there are five deeply diverged lineages within R. vitellinus; further research is desirable.",,,NE,,chbtou1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/chbtou1/,avibase-5C18D846,,,Cayenne.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/89675#page/27/mode/1up,Ramphastos vitellinus
