10077,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus bailloni,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1819)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 34 p.283",Saffron Toucanet,Saffron Toucanet,Saffron Toucanet,,,humid forest of southeastern Brazil to northeastern Argentina and eastern Paraguay,,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22682044,saftou2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/saftou2/,avibase-13435110,,,"No locality = Brazil ex LeVaillant, Hist. Nat. Toucans, no. 18.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/64021#page/301/mode/1up,Ramphastos Bailloni
10078,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus viridis,"(Linnaeus, C, 1766)",Systema Naturæ. Editio duodecima reformata. Tomus I [part 1] p.150,Green Aracari,Green Aracari,Green Araçari,,,eastern Venezuela to the Guianas and northern Brazil,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22681994,greara1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/greara1/,avibase-10FE38DF,,,Cayenne.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/137337#page/154/mode/1up,Ramphastos viridis
10079,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus inscriptus,"Swainson, WJ, 1822","Zoological Illustrations ser.1, vol.2, no.17 pl.90,text",Lettered Aracari,Lettered Aracari,,944,"Taxon humboldti is treated as a subspecies of Pteroglossus inscriptus based on available evidence. These taxa differ in size, minor plumage traits, and bill color patterns, and there is evidence that they hybridize along the Rio Madeira (Haffer 1974). Although mitochondrial DNA divergence is low (Patel et al. 2011; Ostrow et al. 2023a), divergence in genomic data (Ostrow et al. 2023a) is more pronounced; further research may support species recognition.",,,NE,,letara1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/letara1/,avibase-1B7DFB64,,,"Interior of Guiana; error =: Para, by designation of Hellmayr, Nov. Zool., 17, 1910, p. 399.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/92675#page/153/mode/1up,Pteroglossus inscriptus
10080,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus inscriptus inscriptus,"Swainson, WJ, 1822","Zoological Illustrations ser.1, vol.2, no.17 pl.90,text",,,,,,"Amazonian Brazil south of the Amazon River and east of the Rio Madeira, southward to eastern Bolivia and eastward to Maranhão and northwestern Piauí, also northeastern Brazil in Pernambuco and Alagoas",,,,letara3,,avibase-B0B61550,,,"Interior of Guiana; error =: Para, by designation of Hellmayr, Nov. Zool., 17, 1910, p. 399.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/92675#page/153/mode/1up,Pteroglossus inscriptus
10081,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus inscriptus humboldti,"Wagler, JG, 1827",Systema Avium pt.1 p.9,,,,,,"western Amazonia, from southern Colombia east, north of the Amazon River, narrowly to the mouth of the Rio Negro, and, southward to northwestern Bolivia and east, south of the Amazon River, to the Rio Madeira",,,,letara2,,avibase-45FA2A61,,,Brazil.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/233421#page/51/mode/1up,Pteroglossus Humboldti
10082,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus torquatus,"(Gmelin, JF, 1788)","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I [pars I] p.354",Collared Aracari,,Collared Araçari,941,"Three species are recognized in the Collared/Fiery-billed Aracari complex (Pteroglossus torquatus/P. frantzii) based mostly on patterns of genetic divergence (Eberhard & Bermingham 2005; Patel et al. 2011) and extent of hybridization at contact zones (Haffer 1967, 1974; Ridgely & Greenfield 2001): polytypic Pteroglossus torquatus (including erythrozonus and nuchalis), which is the most distinctive taxon based on mitochondrial-dominated DNA data and forms a narrow hybrid zone with P. erythropygius sanguineus; monotypic P. frantzii that is parapatric, or narrowly sympatric, with P. torquatus without evidence of hybridization; and polytypic P. erythropygius, including sanguineus, as these taxa appear to form a narrow hybrid zone and exhibit minimal mtDNA divergence from each other. Further research based on nuclear or genomic data would be informative.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22726200,colara2,,avibase-542B4FCB,,,"Mexico; restricted to Veracruz by Brodkorb, infra.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10285#page/366/mode/1up,Ramphastos torquatus
10083,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus torquatus torquatus,"(Gmelin, JF, 1788)","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I [pars I] p.354",,,,,,tropical southern Mexico to northwestern Colombia,,,,colara6,,avibase-DB4624AC,,,"Mexico; restricted to Veracruz by Brodkorb, infra.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10285#page/366/mode/1up,Ramphastos torquatus
10084,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus torquatus erythrozonus,"Ridgway, R, 1912",Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington 25 p.88,,,,,,Yucatan Peninsula to Belize and Petén of northeastern Guatemala,,,,colara7,,avibase-4AFCF25E,,,"Temax, Yucatan.",Descriptions of some new species and subspecies from tropical America.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22880#page/120/mode/1up,Pteroglossus torquatus erythrozonus
10085,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus torquatus nuchalis,"Cabanis, JL, 1862","Journal für Ornithologie 10, no.59 p.332",,,,,,northeastern Colombia (Santa Marta Mountains) and mountains of northern Venezuela,,,,colara8,,avibase-33F3C30F,,,"Puerto Cabello, Venezuela.","Uebersicht der im Berliner Museum befindlichen Vögel von Costa Rica. (Fortsetzung ; s. Mai-Heft, S. 161-176.)'.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101707#page/362/mode/1up,Pteroglossus nuchalis
10086,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus erythropygius,"Gould, J, 1843","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.11, no.121 p.15",Pale-mandibled Aracari,,,941,"Three species are recognized in the Collared/Fiery-billed Aracari complex (Pteroglossus torquatus/P. frantzii) based mostly on patterns of genetic divergence (Eberhard & Bermingham 2005; Patel et al. 2011) and extent of hybridization at contact zones (Haffer 1967, 1974; Ridgely & Greenfield 2001): polytypic Pteroglossus torquatus (including erythrozonus and nuchalis), which is the most distinctive taxon based on mitochondrial-dominated DNA data and forms a narrow hybrid zone with P. erythropygius sanguineus; monotypic P. frantzii that is parapatric, or narrowly sympatric, with P. torquatus without evidence of hybridization; and polytypic P. erythropygius, including sanguineus, as these taxa appear to form a narrow hybrid zone and exhibit minimal mtDNA divergence from each other. Further research based on nuclear or genomic data would be informative.",,,NE,,,,avibase-F15523C6,,,"No locality = Realejo, Central America, ex Gould, Zool. Voy. 'Sulphur', Bds, 1844, p. 46; error = Ecuador.","Exhibition and description of two new species of Birds, from the collection formed by Capt. Sir Edward Belcher, R.N., during the voyage of Her Majesty's Ship 'Sulphur'.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/96442#page/383/mode/1up,Pteroglossus erythropygius
