10088,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus erythropygius erythropygius,"Gould, J, 1843","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.11, no.121 p.15",,,,,,western Ecuador (western Esmeraldas southward to El Oro) and northwestern Peru (eastern Tumbes),,,,colara5,,avibase-897C1A75,,,"No locality = Realejo, Central America, ex Gould, Zool. Voy. 'Sulphur', Bds, 1844, p. 46; error = Ecuador.","Exhibition and description of two new species of Birds, from the collection formed by Capt. Sir Edward Belcher, R.N., during the voyage of Her Majesty's Ship 'Sulphur'.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/96442#page/383/mode/1up,Pteroglossus erythropygius
10089,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus frantzii,"Cabanis, JL, 1861",Sitzungsberichte der Gesellschaft Naturforschender Freunde zu Berlin [no p.],Fiery-billed Aracari,Fiery-billed Aracari,Fiery-billed Araçari,941,"Three species are recognized in the Collared/Fiery-billed Aracari complex (Pteroglossus torquatus/P. frantzii) based mostly on patterns of genetic divergence (Eberhard & Bermingham 2005; Patel et al. 2011) and extent of hybridization at contact zones (Haffer 1967, 1974; Ridgely & Greenfield 2001): polytypic Pteroglossus torquatus (including erythrozonus and nuchalis), which is the most distinctive taxon based on mitochondrial-dominated DNA data and forms a narrow hybrid zone with P. erythropygius sanguineus; monotypic P. frantzii that is parapatric, or narrowly sympatric, with P. torquatus without evidence of hybridization; and polytypic P. erythropygius, including sanguineus, as these taxa appear to form a narrow hybrid zone and exhibit minimal mtDNA divergence from each other. Further research based on nuclear or genomic data would be informative.",Pacific slope of Costa Rica and western Panama (western Chiriquí),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22682028,fibara1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/fibara1/,avibase-9230DF7D,,,"Costa Rica, type from Aguacate.",,,Pteroglossus Frantzii
