10098,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus azara,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1819)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 34 p.282",Ivory-billed Aracari,Ivory-billed Aracari,Ivory-billed Araçari,942,"Taxon mariae is treated as a subspecies of Pteroglossus azara, as the evidentiary basis for a split is weak. Members of this complex differ only in bill color, areas of apparent introgression have been reported for all taxon pairs (Haffer 1974), and mitochondrial-dominated DNA data suggest that mariae is sister to flavirostris, making azara paraphyletic (Patel et al. 2011). Further research would be informative.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22735207,ivbara1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/ivbara1/,avibase-E8654FA3,,,Brazil.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/64021#page/300/mode/1up,Ramphastos Azara
10099,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus azara flavirostris,"Fraser, L, 1841","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.8, no.90 p.61",,,,,,"southeastern Colombia to Ecuador, northeastern Peru, southern Venezuela, and northwestern Brazil eastward to Roraima (south to northern bank of the Amazon River)",,,,ivbara4,,avibase-7C8E0ABD,,,"Rio Negro on the Amazon; = Rio Solimoes, Brazil, substituted by Berlepsch and Hartert, Nov. Zool., 9, 1902, p. 101.",On some new Species of Birds from the Collection of the Earl of Derby.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/96163#page/783/mode/1up,Pteroglossus flavirostris
10100,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus azara azara,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1819)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 34 p.282",,,,,,"western Brazil in Amazonas, between Rio Negro and Amazon River",,,,ivbara5,,avibase-27B594DA,,,Brazil.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/64021#page/300/mode/1up,Ramphastos Azara
10101,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus azara mariae,"Gould, J, 1854","A monograph of the Ramphastidæ, or family of toucans, rev. ed. Ed.2 pl.30,text",,,,,,eastern Peru and western Brazil south of the Amazon River to north-central Bolivia,,,,ivbara3,,avibase-B67CB8F6,,,"Lower Amazon; 'Peruvian Amazons' substituted by Hellmayr, Nov. Zool., 14, 1907, p. 83.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/263319#page/151/mode/1up,Pteroglossus mariae
10102,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus beauharnaisii,"Wagler, JG, 1832",Isis von Oken 25 col.280,Curl-crested Aracari,Curl-crested Aracari,Curl-crested Araçari,N-60,"The original spelling beauharnaisii is here retained as correct. Much controversy has surrounded the use of a subsequent spelling ""beauharnaesii"", which—at times—was used more frequently than the original spelling. Disagreements over the correct application of beauharnaesii notwithstanding, usage proportions have shifted greatly since the argument unfolded. The continued use of the original spelling therefore seems well-advised.",eastern Peru to northern Bolivia and western Amazonian Brazil south of the Amazon,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22682041,cucara1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/cucara1/,avibase-C98EC8FF,,,"State of Para, Brazil; upper Amazonian region of eastern Peru substituted by Cory, Field Mus. Nat. Hist. Publ., Zool. Sen, 13, pt. 2, no. 2, 1919, p. 373, note a.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/85170#page/158/mode/1up,Pteroglossus Beauharnaesii
10103,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus bitorquatus,"Vigors, NA, 1826","The Zoological Journal 2, no.8 p.481 Suppl. pl.17",Red-necked Aracari,Red-necked Aracari,,943,"Taxon sturmii is treated as a subspecies of Pteroglossus bitorquatus based on available evidence. Reported to differ only in the colors of the iris and the bill, and photographic evidence suggests that these traits frequently do not assort in tandem, and divergence in mitochondrial-dominated DNA (Patel et al. 2011) is relatively weak. Further research in areas of contact may be informative.",,,NE,,renara1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/renara1/,avibase-ECBCE9EB,,,No locality = northeastern Brazil.,"L. Sketches in Ornithology ; or, Observations on the leading Affinities of some of the more extensive groups of Birds. (Continued from p. 405.)'",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/87917#page/507/mode/1up,Pteroglossus bitorquatus
10104,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus bitorquatus sturmii,"Natterer, J, 1842","J. Gould's Monographie der Ramphastiden oder Tukanartigen Voegel. Aus dem Englischen übersetzt, mit Zusätzen und einigen neuen Arten vermehrt Heft3 p.3 pl.7",,,,,,"north-central Brazil south of the Amazon River (between Rio Madeira and Rio Tapajós, southward to Rondônia) to eastern Bolivia and Mato Grosso",,,,renara2,,avibase-FC70352C,,,"Borba, Brazil.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/135881#page/115/mode/1up,Pteroglossus sturmii
10105,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus bitorquatus reichenowi,"Snethlage, HMMEE, 1907",Ornithologische Monatsberichte 15 p.195,,,,,,Brazil south of the Amazon River (between Rio Tapajós and Rio Tocantins),,,,renara4,,avibase-D32E8285,,,"Monte Alegre, lower Amazon.",Neue Vogelarten aus Südamerika.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101411#page/213/mode/1up,Pteroglossus reichenowi
10106,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Pteroglossus bitorquatus bitorquatus,"Vigors, NA, 1826","The Zoological Journal 2, no.8 p.481 Suppl. pl.17",,,,,,northeastern Brazil south of the Amazon east of Rio Tocantins to Maranhão,,,,renara5,,avibase-06F4A940,,,No locality = northeastern Brazil.,"L. Sketches in Ornithology ; or, Observations on the leading Affinities of some of the more extensive groups of Birds. (Continued from p. 405.)'",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/87917#page/507/mode/1up,Pteroglossus bitorquatus
10107,genus,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Aulacorhynchus,"Gould, J, 1835","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.2, no.24 p.147,text",,,,,,,,,,,,,M,"Pteroglossus sulcatus [Swainson, 1820]; type by subsequent designation (Gray, GR, 1840, A List of the Genera of Birds, p. 50).  ",,Characters of a New Species of Toucan.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/96158#page/159/mode/1up,Aulacorhynchus
10108,species,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Aulacorhynchus prasinus,"(Gould, J, 1833)","A monograph of the Ramphastidæ, or family of toucans Pt1 pl.29,text",Northern Emerald Toucanet,Northern Emerald-Toucanet,,938,"The seven taxa in the Aulacorhynchus prasinus complex are treated as conspecific based on available evidence. Sometimes split into three (e.g., Winker 2016) or four (Navarro-Sigüenza et al. 2001) species based on a combination of plumage and bill color differences; however, vocal differences have not been well-documented, and mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Puebla-Olivares et al. 2008; Bonaccorso et al. 2011) indicate relatively modest divergences consistent with subspecific differentiation in A. albivitta, and suggest that A. caeruleogularis would be paraphyletic (Puebla-Olivares et al. 2008) if it included cognatus as proposed by Winker (2016).",,,NE,,noremt1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/noremt1/,avibase-20DB2669,,,"Mexico = Valle Real fide Hellmayr, Nov. Zool, 20, 1913, p. 255.","Characters of the Genera and Species of the Family Ramphastidae, Vig..",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/135881#page/31/mode/1up,Pteroglossus prasinus
10109,subspecies,Piciformes,Ramphastidae,Toucans,Aulacorhynchus prasinus wagleri,"(Sturm, JHCF; Sturm, JW, 1841)","J. Gould's Monographie der Ramphastiden oder Tukanartigen Voegel. Aus dem Englischen übersetzt, mit Zusätzen und einigen neuen Arten vermehrt pl.16,text",,,,,,Sierra Madre del Sur of southwestern Mexico (Guerrero and southwestern Oaxaca),,,,emetou3,,avibase-8A785F55,,,No locality =: Mexico.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/135881#page/71/mode/1up,Pteroglossus wagleri
