10478,genus,Piciformes,Picidae,Woodpeckers,Mulleripicus,"Bonaparte, CLJL, 1854",Ateneo Italiano 2 p.122,,,,804,"Taxa lineatus, pileatus, and schulzii are placed in Dryocopus based on available evidence. Sometimes separated in the genus Hylatomus based on putative paraphyly; however, mitochondrial DNA (Winkler et al. 2014) and multilocus data (Fuchs et al. 2006; Shakya et al. 2017) indicate a deep unresolved polytomy between Dryocopus, Mulleripicus, and species assigned to Hylatomus. Pending further research to determine generic limits, the more traditional two-genus arrangement, Dryocopus and the distinctive Mulleripicus, is adopted.",,,,,,,,M,"Picus pulverulentus [Temminck, 1826]; type by monotypy",,,,Mulleripicus
