10581,species,Piciformes,Picidae,Woodpeckers,Colaptes rubiginosus,"(Swainson, WJ, 1820)","Zoological Illustrations ser.1, vol.1, no.3 pl.14,text",Golden-olive Woodpecker,Golden-olive Woodpecker,,791,"Taxon aeruginosus is treated as a subspecies of Colaptes rubiginosus pending further research. The C. rubiginosus complex is paraphyletic with deep mitochondrial DNA divergences (Moore et al. 2011; Dufort 2016) indicating the presence of multiple species, but the phenotypically and vocally distinct aeruginosus has not yet been sampled. An integrative study of genetic, vocal, and phenotypic variation in this complex is needed before making any splits.",,,NE,,goowoo1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/goowoo1/,avibase-1161239F,,,"'Spanish Main' = Caracas, Venezuela, by designation of Hellmayr, Verb. Orn. Ges. Bayern, 13, 1918, p. 315, note.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/92614#page/99/mode/1up,Picus rubiginosus
