11280,genus,Psittaciformes,Strigopidae,New Zealand Parrots,Strigops,"Gray, GR, 1845","The genera of birds: comprising their generic characters, a notice of the habits of each genus, and an extensive list of species referred to their several genera 2 p.426 pl.CV",,,,,,,,,,,,,F,"Strigops habroptilus [Gray, GR, 1845]; type by monotypy",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/148321#page/269/mode/1up,Strigops
11281,species,Psittaciformes,Strigopidae,New Zealand Parrots,Strigops habroptilus,"Gray, GR, 1845","The genera of birds: comprising their generic characters, a notice of the habits of each genus, and an extensive list of species referred to their several genera 2 p.427 pl.CV",Kakapo,Kakapo,Kakapo,N-69,"Some practitioners have used ""habroptila"" based on the fact that the gender of Strigops was established as feminine by Direction 26 of the ICZN in 1955, assuming that habroptila is an adjective. However, Greek coinages such as habroptilus/habroptila can variably be interpreted as nouns (""soft feather"") or adjectives (""soft-feathered""), with arguments in favor of either interpretation. In such cases, ICZN Article 31.2.2 stipulates their usage as a noun. Hence, Strigops habroptilus, the name that has had an overwhelming historic usage, is the correct epithet. We follow Savage and Digby (2023) in this decision.","now mostly Codfish Island (=Whenua Hou, west of Stewart Island); formerly North, South, and Stewart islands (New Zealand); extremely rare and intensively managed",,CR,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22685245,kakapo2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/kakapo2/,avibase-16804FAF,,,"'One of the islands in the South Pacific' = New Zealand, restricted to Dusky Sound, South Island by Mathews and Iredale, antea.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/219462#page/262/mode/1up,Strigops habroptilus
