11356,genus,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Psittacus,"Linnaeus, C, 1758","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.96",,,,,,,,,,,,,M,"Psittacus erithacus [Linnaeus, 1758]; type by subsequent designation (Gray, GR, 1840, A List of the Genera of Birds, p. 52).",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/114/mode/1up,Psittacus
11357,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Psittacus timneh,"Fraser, L, 1844","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.12, no.132 p.38",Timneh Parrot,Timneh Parrot,Timneh Parrot,643,"Taxon timneh is treated as a monotypic species separate from Psittacus erithacus (polytypic) based on plumage and genetics. Mitochondrial DNA (Melo & O'Ryan 2007) and genomic data (Smith et al. 2023) support separation of nominate P. timneh, but the placement of subspecies princeps is more controversial. Based on plumage birds on Príncipe align with erithacus, but mtDNA suggest that princeps is better placed with timneh (Melo & O'Ryan 2007). It is possible that both taxa now occur on Príncipe (with erithacus a recent arrival); further research needed.","southern Guinea to Sierra Leone, Liberia, Mali, and western Ivory Coast",,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22736498,grypar10,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/grypar10/,avibase-7D6F6D08,,,Timneh country. Sierra Leone.,Description of three New Species of Birds.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46217#page/50/mode/1up,Psittacus Timneh
11358,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Psittacus erithacus,"Linnaeus, C, 1758","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.99",Grey Parrot,Gray Parrot,Grey Parrot,643,"Taxon timneh is treated as a monotypic species separate from Psittacus erithacus (polytypic) based on plumage and genetics. Mitochondrial DNA (Melo & O'Ryan 2007) and genomic data (Smith et al. 2023) support separation of nominate P. timneh, but the placement of subspecies princeps is more controversial. Based on plumage birds on Príncipe align with erithacus, but mtDNA suggest that princeps is better placed with timneh (Melo & O'Ryan 2007). It is possible that both taxa now occur on Príncipe (with erithacus a recent arrival); further research needed.",,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22724813,grepar,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/grepar/,avibase-A20878F0,,,"Guinea, error, I designate Gold Coast Colony.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/117/mode/1up,Psittacus erithacus
11359,subspecies,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Psittacus erithacus erithacus,"Linnaeus, C, 1758","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.99",,,,,,"Ivory Coast to Kenya, Tanzania, Príncipe, São Tomé, and Bioko",,,,grypar2,,avibase-3DE7F2AD,,,"Guinea, error, I designate Gold Coast Colony.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/117/mode/1up,Psittacus erithacus
11360,subspecies,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Psittacus erithacus princeps,"Alexander, B, 1909",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 23 p.74,,,,643,"Taxon timneh is treated as a monotypic species separate from Psittacus erithacus (polytypic) based on plumage and genetics. Mitochondrial DNA (Melo & O'Ryan 2007) and genomic data (Smith et al. 2023) support separation of nominate P. timneh, but the placement of subspecies princeps is more controversial. Based on plumage birds on Príncipe align with erithacus, but mtDNA suggest that princeps is better placed with timneh (Melo & O'Ryan 2007). It is possible that both taxa now occur on Príncipe (with erithacus a recent arrival); further research needed.",Príncipe Island (Gulf of Guinea),,,,grypar11,,avibase-0EF40EA2,,,Principe Island.,"Description of a new species of Grey Parrot from Princes Island, W. Africa.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/100926#page/446/mode/1up,Psittacus princeps
