11443,genus,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Myiopsitta,"Bonaparte, CLJL, 1854",Revue et Magasin de Zoologie Pure et Appliquée (2) 6 p.150,,,,,,,,,,,,,F,"Psittacus murinus [Gmelin, JF, 1788]; type by subsequent designation (Gray, GR, 1855, Cat. of the Genera and Subgenera of Birds, p. 87). = Psittacus monachus Boddaert, 1783",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/48620#page/160/mode/1up,Myiopsitta
11444,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Myiopsitta luchsi,"(Finsch, FHO, 1868)","Die Papageien, monographisch bearbeitet 2 p.114,121",Cliff Parakeet,,Cliff Parakeet,624,"Myiopsitta luchsi (monotypic) is treated as a species separate from Myiopsitta monachus (polytypic). While mitochondrial DNA (Russello et al. 2008) and genomic data (Smith et al. 2023) suggest low divergence, there is not yet any evidence of hybridization despite their occurrence in parapatry. Myiopsitta luchsi differs significantly in plumage and morphometrics, and also exhibits striking differences in voice and its choice of natural cliffs as a nest substrate, while Myiopsitta monachus prefers trees or man-made substrates. Despite opportunities, there are no known examples that either one of them uses the other taxon's preferred nest substrate, suggesting they are indeed reproductively isolated.",xeric intermontane valleys of central Bolivia,,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/45427286,monpar2,,avibase-FDD9A634,,,Bolivia.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/104319#page/148/mode/1up,Bolborrhynchus Luchsi
11445,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Myiopsitta monachus,"(Boddaert, P, 1783)",Table des planches enluminéez d'histoire naturelle de M. D'Aubenton p.48,Monk Parakeet,,Monk Parakeet,624,"Myiopsitta luchsi (monotypic) is treated as a species separate from Myiopsitta monachus (polytypic). While mitochondrial DNA (Russello et al. 2008) and genomic data (Smith et al. 2023) suggest low divergence, there is not yet any evidence of hybridization despite their occurrence in parapatry. Myiopsitta luchsi differs significantly in plumage and morphometrics, and also exhibits striking differences in voice and its choice of natural cliffs as a nest substrate, while Myiopsitta monachus prefers trees or man-made substrates. Despite opportunities, there are no known examples that either one of them uses the other taxon's preferred nest substrate, suggesting they are indeed reproductively isolated.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/45427277,monpar1,,avibase-35810386,,,"Ex Daubenton, pi. 768, no locality = Montevideo, Uruguay.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/88617#page/70/mode/1up,Psittacus monachus
11446,subspecies,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Myiopsitta monachus cotorra,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1818)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 25 p.362",,,,,,"southeastern Bolivia, Paraguay, southwestern Brazil, and northwestern Argentina (Formosa, Chaco, and Corrientes); the species is widely introduced elsewhere, primarily from nominate monachus, but populations in North America also originated in part from subspecies cotorra",,,,monpar3,,avibase-64388B11,,,"Buenos Aires and Paraguay, restricted to Paraguay by Wetmore, antea, p. 195.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/60121#page/380/mode/1up,Psittacus cotorra
11447,subspecies,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Myiopsitta monachus monachus,"(Boddaert, P, 1783)",Table des planches enluminéez d'histoire naturelle de M. D'Aubenton p.48,,,,,,"southeastern Brazil (Rio Grande do Sul), Uruguay, and northeastern Argentina (Santa Fe to eastern Buenos Aires); species is widely introduced in North America (USA, Mexico, the Bahamas, Cayman Islands, and Puerto Rico), the Canary Islands, in Europe, and in Israel; source of most introduced populations is nominate monachus, but, at least in North America, some also originated from subspecies cotorra",,,,monpar4,,avibase-840A7777,,,"Ex Daubenton, pi. 768, no locality = Montevideo, Uruguay.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/88617#page/70/mode/1up,Psittacus monachus
