11534,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Amazona autumnalis,"(Linnaeus, C, 1758)","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.102",Red-lored Amazon,,Red-lored Amazon,627,"Taxa diadema and lilacina are treated as species separate from Amazona autumnalis based on available evidence. However, plumages in the A. autumnalis sensu lato complex are geographically variable, and genetic data are mostly incomplete and contradictory regarding relationships (Ottens-Wainright et al. 2004; Russello & Amato 2004; Pilgrim 2010; Smith et al. 2023); further research needed to determine species limits in this group.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22728292,relpar10,,avibase-56EC9CA9,,,"West Indies, ex Edwards, pi. 164, error = southern Mexico.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/120/mode/1up,Psittacus autumnalis
