11537,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Amazona lilacina,"Lesson, RP, 1844","L'Écho du Monde Savant (2), 11 no.30 col.394",Lilacine Amazon,,Lilacine Amazon,627,"Taxa diadema and lilacina are treated as species separate from Amazona autumnalis based on available evidence. However, plumages in the A. autumnalis sensu lato complex are geographically variable, and genetic data are mostly incomplete and contradictory regarding relationships (Ottens-Wainright et al. 2004; Russello & Amato 2004; Pilgrim 2010; Smith et al. 2023); further research needed to determine species limits in this group.",southwestern Ecuador (north shore of the Bahia de Caráque in central Manabí southward to El Oro,,CR,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22728296,relpar9,,avibase-1F11D1B1,,,"Vicinity of Guayaquil, Ecuador.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/180990#page/244/mode/1up,Amazona (psittacus) Lilacina
11538,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Amazona diadema,"(Spix, JB, 1824)","Avium species novae, quas in itinere per Brasiliam annis MDCCCXVII-MDCCCXX (etc.) 1 p.43 pl.32",Diademed Amazon,,Diademed Amazon,627,"Taxa diadema and lilacina are treated as species separate from Amazona autumnalis based on available evidence. However, plumages in the A. autumnalis sensu lato complex are geographically variable, and genetic data are mostly incomplete and contradictory regarding relationships (Ottens-Wainright et al. 2004; Russello & Amato 2004; Pilgrim 2010; Smith et al. 2023); further research needed to determine species limits in this group.",northwestern Brazil (lower Rio Negro and north bank of the upper Amazon River),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22731595,relpar4,,avibase-7539A5FF,,,"Rio Solimoes, Brazil.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/128666#page/61/mode/1up,Psittacus diadema
