11625,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Pyrrhura picta,"(Müller, PLS, 1776)",Des Ritters Carl von Linné ... vollständigen Natursystems Supplements- und Register-Band über alle sechs Theile oder Classen des Thierreichs p.75,Painted Parakeet,,Painted Parakeet,642,"The Pyrrhura picta complex is split into four species: P. picta (monotypic); P. emma (monotypic); P. subandina (polytypic, including eisenmanni); and P. caeruleiceps. Although this arrangement is supported by available genomic data (Smith et al. 2023), and although subandina and eisenmanni are likely sisters based on genomic data, further research is needed to determine whether eisenmanni also deserves species status. Unfortunately, subandina has not been reliably observed since 1949, which complicates comparative analyses with eisenmanni.",southeastern Venezuela to the Guianas and northern Amazonian Brazil (Amapá),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/45422115,paipar2,,avibase-BDCBDAC0,,,Cayenne.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/218386#page/95/mode/1up,Psittacus pictus
11626,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Pyrrhura subandina,"Todd, WEC, 1917",Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington 30 p.6,Subandean Parakeet,,,642,"The Pyrrhura picta complex is split into four species: P. picta (monotypic); P. emma (monotypic); P. subandina (polytypic, including eisenmanni); and P. caeruleiceps. Although this arrangement is supported by available genomic data (Smith et al. 2023), and although subandina and eisenmanni are likely sisters based on genomic data, further research is needed to determine whether eisenmanni also deserves species status. Unfortunately, subandina has not been reliably observed since 1949, which complicates comparative analyses with eisenmanni.",,,NE,,,,avibase-6468B74C,,,"Jaraquiel, Bolivar, Colombia.",Preliminary diagnoses of apparently new Birds from Columbia and Bolivia.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22874#page/26/mode/1up,Pyrrhura subandina
11627,subspecies,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Pyrrhura subandina eisenmanni,"Delgado B, FS, 1985",Ornithological Monographs 36 p.17,,,,,,south-central Panama (Azuero Peninsula),,,,paipar3,,avibase-E0425FD0,,,,A new subspecies of the painted parakeet (Pyrrhura picta) from Panama.,,Pyrrhura picta eisenmanni
11628,subspecies,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Pyrrhura subandina subandina,"Todd, WEC, 1917",Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington 30 p.6,,,,,,northwestern Colombia (lower Sinú River Valley); unrecorded since 1949 and possibly extinct,(possibly extinct),,,paipar4,,avibase-FD549DD7,,,"Jaraquiel, Bolivar, Colombia.",Preliminary diagnoses of apparently new Birds from Columbia and Bolivia.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22874#page/26/mode/1up,Pyrrhura subandina
11629,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Pyrrhura caeruleiceps,"Todd, WEC, 1947",Annals of the Carnegie Museum 30 p.337,Perija Parakeet,,Perija Parakeet,642,"The Pyrrhura picta complex is split into four species: P. picta (monotypic); P. emma (monotypic); P. subandina (polytypic, including eisenmanni); and P. caeruleiceps. Although this arrangement is supported by available genomic data (Smith et al. 2023), and although subandina and eisenmanni are likely sisters based on genomic data, further research is needed to determine whether eisenmanni also deserves species status. Unfortunately, subandina has not been reliably observed since 1949, which complicates comparative analyses with eisenmanni.",west slope of eastern Andes of northern Colombia and Sierra de Perijá,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/45422600,paipar5,,avibase-FA4A412F,,,,New South American Parrots.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/216154#page/441/mode/1up,Pyrrhura subandina caeruleiceps
11630,species,Psittaciformes,Psittacidae,African and New World Parrots,Pyrrhura emma,"Salvadori, AT, 1891",Catalogue of the birds in the British Museum 20 p.217 pl.1,Venezuelan Parakeet,,Venezuelan Parakeet,642,"The Pyrrhura picta complex is split into four species: P. picta (monotypic); P. emma (monotypic); P. subandina (polytypic, including eisenmanni); and P. caeruleiceps. Although this arrangement is supported by available genomic data (Smith et al. 2023), and although subandina and eisenmanni are likely sisters based on genomic data, further research is needed to determine whether eisenmanni also deserves species status. Unfortunately, subandina has not been reliably observed since 1949, which complicates comparative analyses with eisenmanni.",coastal northern Venezuela,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/45421217,paipar6,,avibase-070AE2DC,,,"Caracas and Garipe, Venezuela.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/34476#page/239/mode/1up,Pyrrhura emma
