12003,species,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Pezoporus wallicus,"(Kerr, R, 1792)","The Animal Kingdom, or Zoological System, of the celebrated Sir Charles Linnæus 1 pt2 p.581",Ground Parrot,Ground Parrot,Ground Parrot,657,"Taxon flaviventris (monotypic) is treated as a subspecies of Pezoporus wallicus based on available evidence. Although mitochondrial DNA divergence is relatively deep (Joseph et al. 2011a; Murphy et al. 2011), phenotypic differences are slight, and corroborating information from ecology and behavior are lacking. Furthermore, support from nuclear DNA (Joseph et al. 2011) and genomic data (Smith et al. 2023) are interpreted cautiously due to limited taxon sampling and the potential for missing data to bias phylogenetic reconstructions (see Smith et al. 2023).",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22685226,gropar1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gropar1/,avibase-50C8A5CF,,,New South Wales.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/119041#page/613/mode/1up,Psittacus wallicus
