12093,genus,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Psephotellus,"Mathews, GM, 1913","The Austral Avian Record; a scientific journal devoted primarily to the study of the Australian avifauna 2, 1913 p.57.",,,,655,"The genus Psephotellus is recognized for four species (P. varius, P. dissimilis, P. chrysopterygius, and P. pulcherrimus) based on the genomic data of Irestedt et al. (2019) and Smith et al. (2023). Previously placed in Psephotus along with haematonotus, genetic data shows this group to be non-monophyletic, with Northiella and Purpureicephalus embedded within it. Although all genera could be united in Psephotus, the morphological and ecological disparity present in this clade is best accommodated by the four-genus approach.",,,,,,,,M,"Platycercus pulcherrimus [Gould, 1845]; type by original designation and monotypy",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/108185#page/75/mode/1up,Psephotellus
