12128,species,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Loriculus philippensis,"(Müller, PLS, 1776)",Des Ritters Carl von Linné ... vollständigen Natursystems Supplements- und Register-Band über alle sechs Theile oder Classen des Thierreichs p.80,Philippine Hanging Parrot,Philippine Hanging-Parrot,,669,"Taxa camiguinensis and bonapartei are treated as monotypic species separate from Loriculus philippensis (polytypic) based on available evidence. Phenotypically, these are the most distinctive taxa in the philippensis complex (Arndt 2006; Tello et al. 2006; Allen 2020), differing in size and lack of sexual dimorphism (camiguinensis), and bare parts color (bonapartei). A comprehensive genetic and morphological review of the entire philippensis complex is needed, in which additional splits may be warranted.",,,NE,,phihap1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/phihap1/,avibase-DDFD5D91,,,"Philippines, i.e. Luzon, ex Buffon.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/218386#page/100/mode/1up,Psittacus philippensis
