12184,species,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Melopsittacus undulatus,"(Shaw, G, 1805)","The naturalist's miscellany 16, no.10 pl.673",Budgerigar,Budgerigar,Budgerigar,,,"Australia, except southeastern coast and Tasmania",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22685223,budger,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/budger/,avibase-D17D101A,,,New HoUand = New South Wales.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/125377#page/215/mode/1up,Psittacus undulatus
12185,genus,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Oreopsittacus,"Salvadori, AT, 1877",Annali del Museo Civico di Storia Naturale di Genova 10 p.37,,,,670,"A 12-genus arrangement is adopted for the Loriini based mostly on the genetic results of Joseph et al. (2020) and Smith et al. (2020, 2023). Although a 19-genus treatment of the Loriini has previously been adopted, this revised treatment is considered more informative given the recency of the radiation. The generic treatment adopted is: a monospecific Oreopsittacus, with O. arfaki; a monospecific Charminetta, with C. wilhelminae; a polytypic Hypocharmosina, with H. placentis and H. rubronotata; a polytypic Charmosynopsis, with C. pulchella and C. toxopei; a polytypic Charmosyna, with C. multistriata, C. josefinae, C. papou, and C. stellae; a polytypic Vini, with V. margarethae, V. rubrigularis, V. meeki, V. palmarum, V. amabilis, V. solitaria, V. ultramarina, V. stepheni, V. peruviana, and V. kuhlii; a polytypic Neopsittacus, with N. musschenbroekii and N. pullicauda; a polytypic Lorius, with L. garrulus, L. domicella, L. lory, L. hypoinochrous, L. albidinucha, and L. chlorocercus; a polytypic Psitteuteles, with P. versicolor, P. pusillus, and P. porphyrocephalus; a polytypic Chalcopsitta, with C. fuscata, C. cardinalis, C. duivenbodei, C. atra, and C. scintillata; a monospecific Glossoptilus, with G. goldiei; and a polytypic Trichoglossus, with T. johnstoniae, T. iris, T. flavoviridis, T. ornatus, T. reticulatus, T. borneus, T. semilarvatus, T. cyanogenius, T. histrio, and T. squamatus.",,,,,,,,M,"Trichoglossus arfaki [Meyer, AB, 1874]; type by monotypy",,,,Oreopsittacus
12186,species,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Oreopsittacus arfaki,"(Meyer, AB, 1874)",Verhandlungen der Kaiserlich-Königlichen Zoologisch-Botanischen Gesellschaft in Wien 24 p.37,Plum-faced Lorikeet,Plum-faced Lorikeet,Plum-faced Lorikeet,,,,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22684714,plflor1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/plflor1/,avibase-67482255,,,"Arfak Mountains, 3500 feet. New Guinea.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/95525#page/137/mode/1up,Trichoglossus (Charmosyna) Arfaki
12187,subspecies,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Oreopsittacus arfaki arfaki,"(Meyer, AB, 1874)",Verhandlungen der Kaiserlich-Königlichen Zoologisch-Botanischen Gesellschaft in Wien 24 p.37,,,,,,mountains of Bird's Head Peninsula (western New Guinea),,,,plflor2,,avibase-D82167D7,,,"Arfak Mountains, 3500 feet. New Guinea.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/95525#page/137/mode/1up,Trichoglossus (Charmosyna) Arfaki
12188,subspecies,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Oreopsittacus arfaki major,"Ogilvie-Grant, WR, 1914",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 35 p.11,,,,,,Snow Mountains (western New Guinea),,,,plflor3,,avibase-7486D4BB,,,"Utakwa River, 8000 feet, New Guinea.",Description of three new subspecies of Parrots from Dutch New Guinea.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/100962#page/41/mode/1up,Oreopsittacus arfaki major
12189,subspecies,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Oreopsittacus arfaki grandis,"Ogilvie-Grant, WR, 1895",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 5 p.15,,,,,,central mountains of Papua New Guinea,,,,plflor4,,avibase-84B824EF,,,"Owen Stanley Mountains, New Guinea.","[Exhibition of two apparently undescribed birds from the Owen Stanley Mountains, in S.E. New Guinea].",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101092#page/309/mode/1up,Oreopsittacus grandis
12190,genus,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Charminetta,"Iredale, T, 1956",Birds of New Guinea 1. p.160,,,,670,"A 12-genus arrangement is adopted for the Loriini based mostly on the genetic results of Joseph et al. (2020) and Smith et al. (2020, 2023). Although a 19-genus treatment of the Loriini has previously been adopted, this revised treatment is considered more informative given the recency of the radiation. The generic treatment adopted is: a monospecific Oreopsittacus, with O. arfaki; a monospecific Charminetta, with C. wilhelminae; a polytypic Hypocharmosina, with H. placentis and H. rubronotata; a polytypic Charmosynopsis, with C. pulchella and C. toxopei; a polytypic Charmosyna, with C. multistriata, C. josefinae, C. papou, and C. stellae; a polytypic Vini, with V. margarethae, V. rubrigularis, V. meeki, V. palmarum, V. amabilis, V. solitaria, V. ultramarina, V. stepheni, V. peruviana, and V. kuhlii; a polytypic Neopsittacus, with N. musschenbroekii and N. pullicauda; a polytypic Lorius, with L. garrulus, L. domicella, L. lory, L. hypoinochrous, L. albidinucha, and L. chlorocercus; a polytypic Psitteuteles, with P. versicolor, P. pusillus, and P. porphyrocephalus; a polytypic Chalcopsitta, with C. fuscata, C. cardinalis, C. duivenbodei, C. atra, and C. scintillata; a monospecific Glossoptilus, with G. goldiei; and a polytypic Trichoglossus, with T. johnstoniae, T. iris, T. flavoviridis, T. ornatus, T. reticulatus, T. borneus, T. semilarvatus, T. cyanogenius, T. histrio, and T. squamatus.",,,,,,,,F,,,,,Charminetta
12191,species,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Charminetta wilhelminae,"(Meyer, AB, 1874)","Journal für Ornithologie 22, no.125 p.55,56",Pygmy Lorikeet,Pygmy Lorikeet,Pygmy Lorikeet,,,mountains of New Guinea (Bird's Head Peninsula to Owen Stanley Range),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22684680,pyglor1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/pyglor1/,avibase-A2558EE9,,,West coast of Geelvink Bay.,"Ueber Drepanornis Albertisi Scl., Trichoglossus Josefinae Finsch und Trichoglossus Wilhelminae nov. sp..",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101706#page/67/mode/1up,Trichoglossus Wilhelminae
