12231,genus,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Neopsittacus,"Salvadori, AT, 1875",Annali del Museo Civico di Storia Naturale di Genova 7 p.761,,,,670,"A 12-genus arrangement is adopted for the Loriini based mostly on the genetic results of Joseph et al. (2020) and Smith et al. (2020, 2023). Although a 19-genus treatment of the Loriini has previously been adopted, this revised treatment is considered more informative given the recency of the radiation. The generic treatment adopted is: a monospecific Oreopsittacus, with O. arfaki; a monospecific Charminetta, with C. wilhelminae; a polytypic Hypocharmosina, with H. placentis and H. rubronotata; a polytypic Charmosynopsis, with C. pulchella and C. toxopei; a polytypic Charmosyna, with C. multistriata, C. josefinae, C. papou, and C. stellae; a polytypic Vini, with V. margarethae, V. rubrigularis, V. meeki, V. palmarum, V. amabilis, V. solitaria, V. ultramarina, V. stepheni, V. peruviana, and V. kuhlii; a polytypic Neopsittacus, with N. musschenbroekii and N. pullicauda; a polytypic Lorius, with L. garrulus, L. domicella, L. lory, L. hypoinochrous, L. albidinucha, and L. chlorocercus; a polytypic Psitteuteles, with P. versicolor, P. pusillus, and P. porphyrocephalus; a polytypic Chalcopsitta, with C. fuscata, C. cardinalis, C. duivenbodei, C. atra, and C. scintillata; a monospecific Glossoptilus, with G. goldiei; and a polytypic Trichoglossus, with T. johnstoniae, T. iris, T. flavoviridis, T. ornatus, T. reticulatus, T. borneus, T. semilarvatus, T. cyanogenius, T. histrio, and T. squamatus.",,,,,,,,M,"Nanodes musschenbroekii [Schlegel, 1871]; type by monotypy",,,,Neopsittacus
12232,species,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Neopsittacus musschenbroekii,"(Schlegel, H, 1871)",Nederlandsch Tijdschrift voor de Dierkunde 4 p.34,Yellow-billed Lorikeet,Yellow-billed Lorikeet,Yellow-billed Lorikeet,,,"mid-montane New Guinea, including Vogelkop and Huon Peninsula",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22684717,yeblor2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/yeblor2/,avibase-4B8D4F6C,,,"Interior of the northern peninsula of New Guinea = Hatam, Arfak, New Guinea.",Observations zoologiques V.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/193078#page/46/mode/1up,Nanodes Musschenbroekii
12233,species,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Neopsittacus pullicauda,"Hartert, EJO, 1896",Novitates Zoologicae 3 p.17,Orange-billed Lorikeet,Orange-billed Lorikeet,Orange-billed Lorikeet,,,"high montane west-central to southeastern New Guinea, including Huon Peninsula",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22684720,orblor1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/orblor1/,avibase-7A03D2D9,,,"Mt. Victoria, Victoria district, Owen Stanley Range, New Guinea.","Contributions to the ornithology of the Papuan Islands. I. List of three small collections from British New Guinea, mostly brought together in the Owen Stanley Mountains.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22554#page/35/mode/1up,Neopsittacus pullicauda
12234,genus,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Lorius,"Vigors, NA, 1825","The Zoological Journal 2, no.7 p.400",,,,670,"A 12-genus arrangement is adopted for the Loriini based mostly on the genetic results of Joseph et al. (2020) and Smith et al. (2020, 2023). Although a 19-genus treatment of the Loriini has previously been adopted, this revised treatment is considered more informative given the recency of the radiation. The generic treatment adopted is: a monospecific Oreopsittacus, with O. arfaki; a monospecific Charminetta, with C. wilhelminae; a polytypic Hypocharmosina, with H. placentis and H. rubronotata; a polytypic Charmosynopsis, with C. pulchella and C. toxopei; a polytypic Charmosyna, with C. multistriata, C. josefinae, C. papou, and C. stellae; a polytypic Vini, with V. margarethae, V. rubrigularis, V. meeki, V. palmarum, V. amabilis, V. solitaria, V. ultramarina, V. stepheni, V. peruviana, and V. kuhlii; a polytypic Neopsittacus, with N. musschenbroekii and N. pullicauda; a polytypic Lorius, with L. garrulus, L. domicella, L. lory, L. hypoinochrous, L. albidinucha, and L. chlorocercus; a polytypic Psitteuteles, with P. versicolor, P. pusillus, and P. porphyrocephalus; a polytypic Chalcopsitta, with C. fuscata, C. cardinalis, C. duivenbodei, C. atra, and C. scintillata; a monospecific Glossoptilus, with G. goldiei; and a polytypic Trichoglossus, with T. johnstoniae, T. iris, T. flavoviridis, T. ornatus, T. reticulatus, T. borneus, T. semilarvatus, T. cyanogenius, T. histrio, and T. squamatus.",,,,,,,,M,"Psittacus domicella [Linnaeus, 1758]; type by original designation",,"Sketches in ornithology; or, observations on the leading affinities of some of the more extensive groups of birds.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/87917#page/428/mode/1up,Lorius
