12308,species,Psittaciformes,Psittaculidae,Old World Parrots,Trichoglossus rosenbergii,"Schlegel, H, 1871",Nederlandsch Tijdschrift voor de Dierkunde 4 p.9,Biak Lorikeet,Biak Lorikeet,Biak Lorikeet,664,"Taxon rosenbergii is treated as a monotypic species separate from Trichoglossus haematodus (polytypic) based on plumage and genetics. Phenotypically, rosenbergii is one of the most distinctive members of the complex and is deeply diverged from nominate haematodus based on genomic DNA (Smith et al. 2020, 2023). However, rosenbergii shares mitochondrial DNA with subspecies massena and deplanchii of the T. haematodus sensu stricto complex (Braun et al. 2017); further research needed to clarify species limits across the entire T. haematodus sensu lato complex.","Biak (Cenderawasih Bay, off northwestern New Guinea)",,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22726315,railor6,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/railor6/,avibase-6B4D5B3C,,,Biak.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/193078#page/21/mode/1up,Trichoglossus Rosenbergii
