12417,species,Passeriformes,Pittidae,Pittas,Erythropitta kochi,"(Brüggemann, F, 1876)",Abhandlungen herausgegeben vom Naturwissenschaftlichen Verein zu Bremen 5 p.65 pl.3 fig.6,Whiskered Pitta,Whiskered Pitta,Whiskered Pitta,,,mountains of northern Luzon (northern Philippines),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22698648,whipit1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/whipit1/,avibase-4922C1E5,,,Luzon.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/104684#page/73/mode/1up,Pitta Kochi
12418,species,Passeriformes,Pittidae,Pittas,Erythropitta erythrogaster,"(Temminck, CJ, 1823)","Nouveau recueil de planches coloriées d'oiseaux, pour servir de suite et de complément aux planches enluminées de Buffon livr.36, vol.2 pl.212",Philippine Pitta,Philippine Pitta,,881,"The Erythropitta erythrogaster complex is treated as 8 species based on a combination of morphological (Collar et al. 2015) and genetic evidence, mostly from mitochondrial DNA data (Irestedt et al. 2013). Six polytypic species are recognized: E. erythrogaster (including inspeculata, propinqua, yairocho, and thompsoni); E. celebensis (including caeruleitorques and palliceps); E. rufiventris (including cyanonota, bernsteini, and obiensis); E. rubrinucha (including piroensis); E. macklotii (including digglesi, oblita, loriae, finschii, and habenichti); and E. novaehibernicae (including gazellae, splendida, and extima), with the remaining two species being the monotypic E. dohertyi and E. meeki. Species delimitation in this complex remains open to change, and future additions of genomic and phenotypic datasets may lead to further splits or lumps.",,,NE,,rebpit1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rebpit1/,avibase-4194FFF5,,,"Manila, Luzon, Philippine Islands.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/109469#page/445/mode/1up,Pitta erythrogaster
