12964,family,Passeriformes,Onychorhynchidae,Royal Flycatchers and Allies,Onychorhynchidae,,,,,,1178,"Oxyruncus is placed in the family Oxyruncidae based on genomic DNA evidence (Harvey et al. 2020). Sometimes subsumed into Tityridae, or recognized as a separate family that also includes Onychorhynchus, Myiobius, and Terenotriccus. However, recognition of Oxyruncidae is supported by the lack of a sister relationship with the Tityridae (Harvey et al. 2020), combined with the deep separation of Oxyruncus from Onychorhynchus, Myiobius, and Terenotriccus, and the lack of morphological or behavioral characters uniting them; the latter three genera are placed in the family Onychorhynchidae.",,,,,,,,,,,,,
12965,genus,Passeriformes,Onychorhynchidae,Royal Flycatchers and Allies,Onychorhynchus,"Fischer von Waldheim, G, 1810",Description d'objets rares du Musée d'Histoire Naturelle de l'Université Impériale de Moscou 1 p.1 pl.,,,,,,,,,,,,,M,"Todus regius [Gmelin, JF, 1788]; type by monotypy = Muscicapa coronata Statius Muller, 1776",,,,Onychorhynchus
12966,species,Passeriformes,Onychorhynchidae,Royal Flycatchers and Allies,Onychorhynchus swainsoni,"(Pelzeln, A, 1858)",Sitzungsberichte der Kaiserlichen Akademie der Wissenschaften. Mathematisch-Naturwissenschaftliche Classe 31 p.325,Atlantic Royal Flycatcher,Atlantic Royal Flycatcher,Atlantic Royal Flycatcher,835,"Taxon swainsoni is treated as a species separate from Onychorhynchus coronatus based on consistent differences in vocalizations, plumage, and genetics (Harvey et al. 2020; Reyes et al. 2023). Although O. coronatus sensu lato is sometimes split into four species, vocal differences among coronatus, mexicanus, and occidentalis are weak, despite obvious differences in plumage and a relatively deep genomic divergence between coronatus and the mexicanus/occidentalis clade (Harvey et al. 2020); further research on species limits in this complex is warranted.","southeastern Brazil (Minas Gerais, Rio de Janeiro, São Paulo, and Paraná)",,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22699659,royfly5,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/royfly5/,avibase-D12A2E74,,,"Juan Fernandez; error, restricted to Rio de Janeiro, Brazil by Hellmayr, 1927, Field Mus. Nat. Hist., Zool. Ser., 13, pt. 5, p. 260.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/30227#page/360/mode/1up,Muscivora Swainsoni
12967,species,Passeriformes,Onychorhynchidae,Royal Flycatchers and Allies,Onychorhynchus coronatus,"(Müller, PLS, 1776)",Des Ritters Carl von Linné ... vollständigen Natursystems Supplements- und Register-Band über alle sechs Theile oder Classen des Thierreichs p.168,Tropical Royal Flycatcher,Tropical Royal Flycatcher,,835,"Taxon swainsoni is treated as a species separate from Onychorhynchus coronatus based on consistent differences in vocalizations, plumage, and genetics (Harvey et al. 2020; Reyes et al. 2023). Although O. coronatus sensu lato is sometimes split into four species, vocal differences among coronatus, mexicanus, and occidentalis are weak, despite obvious differences in plumage and a relatively deep genomic divergence between coronatus and the mexicanus/occidentalis clade (Harvey et al. 2020); further research on species limits in this complex is warranted.",,,NE,,royfly1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/royfly1/,avibase-2A931A37,,,Cayenne.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/218386#page/188/mode/1up,Muscicapa coronata
