13085,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Leptopogon superciliaris,"Tschudi, JJ, 1844",Archiv für Naturgeschichte 10 p.275,Slaty-capped Flycatcher,Slaty-capped Flycatcher,,439,"Taxon albidiventer is retained as a subspecies of Leptopogon superciliaris pending further research on species limits in this complex. Genomic data show albidiventer to be embedded within L. superciliaris (Harvey et al. 2020), but multiple species may be represented in this group. Vocal differences (Ridgely & Greenfield 2001; Schulenberg et al. 2007; Boesman 2016fff) also point to multiple species within the L. superciliaris complex. Further clarification of plumage distinctions, analysis of vocalizations, and broader genomic sampling is required.",,,NE,,slcfly1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/slcfly1/,avibase-16C172E1,,,"Peru; restricted to Montaiia of Vitoc by Hellmayr, 1918, Verb. Ornith. Ges. Bayern, 13, p. 306.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/48694#page/289/mode/1up,L[eptopogon] superciliaris
