13418,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Stigmatura napensis,"Chapman, FM, 1926",American Museum Novitates no.231 p.3,Lesser Wagtail-Tyrant,Lesser Wagtail-Tyrant,Lesser Wagtail-tyrant,443,"Taxon bahiae is split from Stigmatura napensis based on genetics. Genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) did not recover S. napensis as monophyletic, instead aligning bahiae with S. budytoides. Vocalizations also differ between napensis and bahiae, although no quantitative comparisons have been made to other taxa in this complex. Further revisions are necessary, as S. budytoides (polytypic) and S. bahiae (monotypic) were not recovered as reciprocally monophyletic (Harvey et al. 2020).","along larger rivers of western and central Amazonia from eastern Ecuador (Napo River) and eastern Peru (Río Napo, Río Ucayali, and Amazon River) eastward to central Brazil (to the lower Río Tapajós); also a population (possibly an undescribed taxon) in Río Orinoco drainages in far eastern Colombia (Vichada) and southwestern Venezuela (western Amazonas)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103681041,lewtyr1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/lewtyr1/,avibase-7D568545,,,"junction of Curaray and Napo rivers, Peru.","Descriptions of new birds from Bolivia, Peru, Ecuador, and Brazil.",https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/4112/,Stigmatura budytoides napensis
13419,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Stigmatura bahiae,"Chapman, FM, 1926",American Museum Novitates no.231 p.4,Bahia Wagtail-Tyrant,Bahia Wagtail-Tyrant,Bahia Wagtail-tyrant,443,"Taxon bahiae is split from Stigmatura napensis based on genetics. Genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) did not recover S. napensis as monophyletic, instead aligning bahiae with S. budytoides. Vocalizations also differ between napensis and bahiae, although no quantitative comparisons have been made to other taxa in this complex. Further revisions are necessary, as S. budytoides (polytypic) and S. bahiae (monotypic) were not recovered as reciprocally monophyletic (Harvey et al. 2020).",northeastern Brazil (Ceará and Rio Grande do Norte southward to southern Bahia),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22731687,leswat2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/leswat2/,avibase-99C6BEEA,,,"Joazeiro [Juazeiro] , northern Bahia, Brazil.","Descriptions of new birds from Bolivia, Peru, Ecuador, and Brazil.",https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/4112/,Stigmatura budytoides bahiae
