13440,genus,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Acrochordopus,"Berlepsch, HHCL; Hellmayr, CE, 1905","Journal für Ornithologie 53, no.1 p.26.",,,,1198,"Acrochordopus (polytypic, including burmeisteri and zeledoni) and Tyranniscus (polytypic, including nigrocapillus, cinereiceps and uropygialis) are recognized as distinct genera based on genomic DNA evidence (Harvey et al. 2020) that Phyllomyias sensu lato is polyphyletic, supported by morphological and genomic differences that separate Acrochordopus from other species placed in Tyranniscus.",,,,,,,,M,Phyllomyias subviridis [Pelzeln]; type by original designation,,Studien über wenig bekannte Typen neotropischer Vögel,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/107488#page/38/mode/1up,Acrochordopus
13441,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Acrochordopus burmeisteri,"(Cabanis, JL; Heine, F, 1860)",Museum Heineanum. Verzeichniss der orithologischen Sammlung des Oberamtmann Ferdinand Heine 2 p.57,Rough-legged Tyrannulet,Rough-legged Tyrannulet,Rough-legged Tyrannulet,458,Taxon zeledoni (polytypic) is split from Acrochordopus burmeisteri (monotypic) based on genetics and vocalizations. Genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) show a deep split between zeledoni (ssp. leucogenys) and burmeisteri; vocal analyses also support the existence of two groups (Parra-Hernández et al. 2020; Parra-Hernández & Arias-Moreno 2020). Further research on genetic and vocal differentiation within zeledoni is desirable.,"east slope of Andes of eastern Bolivia, northern Argentina, eastern Paraguay, and southeastern Brazil",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22699081,roltyr3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/roltyr3/,avibase-F61CF239,,,"Brazil; restricted Rio de Janeiro by Pinto, 1944, Cat. Aves Brasil (Publ. Dept. ZooL, Sao Paulo), pt. 2, p. 298.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/196137#page/65/mode/1up,P[hyllomyias] Burmeisteri
13442,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Acrochordopus zeledoni,"(Lawrence, GN, 1869)",Annals of the Lyceum of Natural History of New York 9(1870) p.144,White-fronted Tyrannulet,White-fronted Tyrannulet,White-fronted Tyrannulet,458,Taxon zeledoni (polytypic) is split from Acrochordopus burmeisteri (monotypic) based on genetics and vocalizations. Genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) show a deep split between zeledoni (ssp. leucogenys) and burmeisteri; vocal analyses also support the existence of two groups (Parra-Hernández et al. 2020; Parra-Hernández & Arias-Moreno 2020). Further research on genetic and vocal differentiation within zeledoni is desirable.,,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22699075,roltyr1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/roltyr1/,avibase-DEDA2050,,,"Dota and Barranca, Costa Rica; restricted to Dota (J. T. Z.).",A catalogue of the birds found in Costa Rica.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22948#page/160/mode/1up,Pogonotriccus (?) zeledoni
