13596,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Nesotriccus maranonicus,"(Zimmer, JT, 1941)",American Museum Novitates no.1109 p.8,Maranon Tyrannulet,Marañon Tyrannulet,,457,"Taxon tumbezanus (polytypic, including inflavus) and maranonicus are treated as species separate from Nesotriccus murinus based on genomic DNA evidence (Zucker et al. 2016), supported by vocalizations. Previously placed in Phaeomyias, Zucker et al. (2016) recovered the distinctive insular N. ridgwayi as embedded within Phaeomyias, necessitating a change of genus name. Further splits may be warranted in the N. murinus group and uncertainty over the type locality of tumbezanus may have nomenclatural consequences that require resolution.","west slope of the Andes of southwestern Ecuador (Loja) and northwestern Peru (Piura and Cajamarca), and the arid tropical Marañón Valley in far southern Ecuador and northern Peru",,NE,,moctyr4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/moctyr4/,avibase-6B61BE45,,,"Jaen, 2,400 ft., Rio Marahon, northern Peru.","Studies of Peruvian birds. No. 37, The genera Sublegatus, Phaeomyias[,] Camptostoma, Xanthomyias, Phyllomyias, and Tyranniscus.",https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/4794/,Phaeomyias murina maranonica
