13968,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Ochthoeca salvini,"Taczanowski, W, 1877","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1877, pt.2 p.324",Tumbes Tyrant,Tumbes Chat-Tyrant,Tumbes Tyrant,463,"The genus Ochthoeca is restricted to ten species (including salvini) based on genetic evidence (Tello et al. 2009; Harvey et al. 2020), with Silvicultrix used for frontalis, pulchella, diadema, and jelskii as proposed by Lanyon (1986), and Colorhamphus parvirostris retained as a monotypic genus. An earlier study based on short segments of mitochondrial DNA (García-Moreno et al. 1998) lacked sufficient resolution to be informative.",arid northwestern Peru (Tumbes to La Libertad),,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22699951,tumtyr2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/tumtyr2/,avibase-38AAAD74,,,"Tumbes, Peru.",Liste des Oiseaux recueillis en 1876 au nord du Pérou occidental par MM. Jelski et Stolzmann.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/90436#page/422/mode/1up,Ochthoeca salvini
13969,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Ochthoeca cinnamomeiventris,"(de Lafresnaye, NFAA, 1843)","Revue Zoologique, par la Société Cuvierienne 6 p.291",Slaty-backed Chat-Tyrant,Chestnut-bellied Chat-Tyrant,Slaty-backed Chat-tyrant,461,"Ochthoeca cinnamomeiventris is split into three species based on genetics, plumages, and vocalizations: O. cinnamomeiventris (monotypic); O. nigrita (monotypic); and O. thoracica (polytypic, including angustifasciata). Genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) support recognition of three species; the split of thoracica is also supported by mitochondrial DNA (García-Moreno et al. 1998) and vocal data (Farnsworth & Langham 2020). Vocal data for nigrita is limited and further vocal studies are warranted.","Andes of Colombia, Ecuador (entire east slope, southward on the west slope to Chimborazo), and far northern Peru (east slope, north and west of the Marañón Valley)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103682781,slbcht2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/slbcht2/,avibase-5E381EA4,,,"Colombia; restricted to 'Bogota' by Hellmayr, 1927, Field Mus. Nat. Hist., Zool. Ser., 13, pt. 5, p. 50.",Oiseaux nouveaux de Colombie.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/19446#page/299/mode/1up,Muscicapa cinnamomeiventris
