14030,genus,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Pyrocephalus,"Gould, J, 1838","The zoology of the voyage of H.M.S. Beagle, under the command of Captain FitzRoy, R.N., during the years 1832 to 1836 3 pt3 p.44",,,,,,,,,,,,,M,"Muscicapa coronata [auct. = J.F. Gmelin, 1789]; type by subsequent designation (Gray, GR, 1840, A List of the Genera of Birds, p. 30). = Muscicapa rubinus Boddaert, 1783  ",,,,Pyrocephalus
14031,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Pyrocephalus nanus,"Gould, J, 1838","The zoology of the voyage of H.M.S. Beagle, under the command of Captain FitzRoy, R.N., during the years 1832 to 1836 pt9 p.45 pl.7",Brujo Flycatcher,Brujo Flycatcher,,467,"Two species are recognized in Pyrocephalus: P. nanus (polytypic, including dubius) and P. rubinus (polytypic) based on genetics and vocalizations. Variously considered to comprise 2, 3 or 4 species, mitochondrial DNA data (Carmi et al. 2016) recovered multiple clades, with a deep divergence separating the two Galapagos Island taxa (nanus and dubius) from all continental forms. Further research is needed to define species limits within P. rubinus sensu stricto, as preliminary genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) conflict with some aspects of the mtDNA topology in Carmi et al. (2016); further revisions are likely, especially if a comprehensive review of vocalizations can be combined with more complete sampling at the genomic level.",,,NE,,brufly1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/brufly1/,avibase-F7667798,,,"Galapagos Archipelago; type from James Island [= San Salvador] , fide Ridgway, 1894, Proc. U. S. Nat. Mus., 17, p. 365.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/124547#page/85/mode/1up,Pyrocephalus nanus
14032,subspecies,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Pyrocephalus nanus nanus,"Gould, J, 1838","The zoology of the voyage of H.M.S. Beagle, under the command of Captain FitzRoy, R.N., during the years 1832 to 1836 pt9 p.45 pl.7",,,,,,Galapagos (except San Cristóbal),,,,verfly3,,avibase-55BCD678,,,"Galapagos Archipelago; type from James Island [= San Salvador] , fide Ridgway, 1894, Proc. U. S. Nat. Mus., 17, p. 365.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/124547#page/85/mode/1up,Pyrocephalus nanus
14033,subspecies,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Pyrocephalus nanus dubius,"Gould, J; Gray, GR, 1839","The zoology of the voyage of H.M.S. Beagle, under the command of Captain FitzRoy, R.N., during the years 1832 to 1836 pt9 p.46",,,,,,"formerly San Cristóbal Island (Galapagos); extinct, last reported 1987",Extinct,,,verfly8,,avibase-D5C9273F,,,Galapagos (Colon) Islands [= Chatham Island (Isla San Cristobal)] .,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/124547#page/86/mode/1up,Pyrocephalus dubius
14034,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Pyrocephalus rubinus,"(Boddaert, P, 1783)",Table des planches enluminéez d'histoire naturelle de M. D'Aubenton p.42,Vermilion Flycatcher,Vermilion Flycatcher,Common Vermilion Flycatcher,467,"Two species are recognized in Pyrocephalus: P. nanus (polytypic, including dubius) and P. rubinus (polytypic) based on genetics and vocalizations. Variously considered to comprise 2, 3 or 4 species, mitochondrial DNA data (Carmi et al. 2016) recovered multiple clades, with a deep divergence separating the two Galapagos Island taxa (nanus and dubius) from all continental forms. Further research is needed to define species limits within P. rubinus sensu stricto, as preliminary genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) conflict with some aspects of the mtDNA topology in Carmi et al. (2016); further revisions are likely, especially if a comprehensive review of vocalizations can be combined with more complete sampling at the genomic level.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103682912,verfly,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/verfly/,avibase-1456993D,,,"restricted to Teffe, Brazil by Zimmer, 1941, Amer. Mus. Novit., no. 1126, p. 16.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/88617#page/64/mode/1up,Muscicapa rubinus
