14251,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Knipolegus hudsoni,"Sclater, PL, 1872","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1872, pt.1 p.541 pl.31,text",Hudson's Black Tyrant,Hudson's Black-Tyrant,Hudson's Black-tyrant,,,"central Argentina; winters to Bolivia, southwestern Brazil, and southeastern Peru",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22700223,hubtyr1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/hubtyr1/,avibase-5CA4674C,,,"Rio Negro, Patagonia.",On the Birds of the Rio Negro of Patagonia. With Notes by P. L. Sclater.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/90880#page/625/mode/1up,Cnipolegus hudsoni
14252,genus,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Cnemarchus,"Ridgway, R, 1905",Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington 18 p.208,,,,471,"Genus-level changes in the fluvicoline tyrant flycatchers are based on a combination of genetic (summarised by Chesser et al. 2020b; Ohlson et al. 2020), phenotypic, and behavioral data. The classification recognizes: Syrtidicola fluviatilis based on deep genetic divergence from Muscisaxicola (Chesser et al. 2020b), as well as morphological and ecological differences; Cnemarchus rufipennis based on common themes in plumage, vocalizations and ecology with C. erythropygius; Pyrope pyrope based on deep genetic divergence within the Xolmis sensu lato clade (Chesser et al. 2020b; Ohlson et al. 2020); monospecific Nengetus (N. cinereus) based on deep genetic divergence, and its distinctive plumage and ecology; Neoxolmis restricted to four species (N. rufiventris, N. rubetra, N. salinarum, and N. coronatus) which form a cohesive group based on plumage and ecology to the exclusion of cinereus; Xolmis restricted to X. irupero and X. velatus based on genetics; and Heteroxolmis dominicanus, as genetic data show it to be outside the Xolmiini and sister to Alectrurus (Chesser et al. 2020b; Ohlson et al. 2020) a placement also supported by osteological characters.",,,,,,,,M,"Taenioptera erythropygia [Sclater, PL, 1853]; type by original designation",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/19435#page/228/mode/1up,Cnemarchus
14253,species,Passeriformes,Tyrannidae,Tyrant Flycatchers and Allies,Cnemarchus erythropygius,"(Sclater, PL, 1853)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.19, no.231 p.193 pl.41",Red-rumped Bush Tyrant,Red-rumped Bush-Tyrant,Red-rumped Bush-tyrant,,,,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22699978,rrbtyr1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rrbtyr1/,avibase-3BB9E319,,,"Ecuador; restricted to Verdecocha, Pichincha (J. T. Z.).",On two new species of Birds of the genus Taenioptera.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/96443#page/239/mode/1up,Taenioptera erythropygia
