14368,genus,Passeriformes,Thamnophilidae,"Antbirds, Antshrikes, Antwrens, and Antvireos",Thamnistes,"Sclater, PL; Salvin, O, 1860","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.28, no.2 p.299",,,,,,,,,,,,,M,"Thamnistes anabatinus [Sclater, PL & Salvin, 1860]; type by monotypy",,Characters of Eleven New Species of Birds discovered by Osbert Salvin in Guatemala.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46225#page/381/mode/1up,Thamnistes
14369,species,Passeriformes,Thamnophilidae,"Antbirds, Antshrikes, Antwrens, and Antvireos",Thamnistes rufescens,"Cabanis, JL, 1873","Journal für Ornithologie 21, no.121 p.65",Rufescent Antshrike,Rufescent Antshrike,,828,"Taxa aequatorialis and gularis are treated as subspecies of Thamnistes anabatinus pending further research. Both taxa are sometimes placed in a polytypic T. aequatorialis, along with the vocally distinct rufescens. While vocalizations (Isler & Whitney 2017), size, apparent parapatry, and mitochondrial DNA data (Weir 2009) are suggestive of species-level divergence for aequatorialis, genetic data for gularis and rufescens are lacking; further research is needed to determine taxonomic affinities across the entire complex.",eastern Peru south of the Rio Marañón (Amazonas) to western Bolivia,,NE,,rufant12,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rufant12/,avibase-7882DDB3,,,"Monterico, Peru.",[Über die ornithologischen Entdeckungen des Herrn Constantin Jelski im westlichen Peru].,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101685#page/77/mode/1up,Thamnistes rufescens
14370,species,Passeriformes,Thamnophilidae,"Antbirds, Antshrikes, Antwrens, and Antvireos",Thamnistes anabatinus,"Sclater, PL; Salvin, O, 1860","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.28, no.2 p.299",Russet Antshrike,Russet Antshrike,,828,"Taxa aequatorialis and gularis are treated as subspecies of Thamnistes anabatinus pending further research. Both taxa are sometimes placed in a polytypic T. aequatorialis, along with the vocally distinct rufescens. While vocalizations (Isler & Whitney 2017), size, apparent parapatry, and mitochondrial DNA data (Weir 2009) are suggestive of species-level divergence for aequatorialis, genetic data for gularis and rufescens are lacking; further research is needed to determine taxonomic affinities across the entire complex.",,,NE,,rusant1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rusant1/,avibase-EE472B65,,,"Vera Paz, Guatemala.",Characters of Eleven New Species of Birds discovered by Osbert Salvin in Guatemala.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46225#page/381/mode/1up,Thamnistes anabatinus
