15223,species,Passeriformes,Grallariidae,Antpittas,Grallaria alticola,"Todd, WEC, 1919",Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington 32 p.115,Boyaca Antpitta,Boyaca Antpitta,Boyaca Antpitta,747,"The Grallaria quitensis sensu lato complex is treated as three monotypic species based on differences in vocalizations, supported by modest plumage differences (Krabbe & Schulenberg 2003; Boesman 2016ii): G. alticola; G. atuensis; and G. quitensis. While mitochondrial DNA and genomic data (Winger et al. 2015) support recognition of G. alticola, taxon atuensis was not included in the analysis.",eastern Andes of Colombia,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103660427,tawant2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/tawant2/,avibase-0416064D,,,"Lagunillas, Boyaca, Colombia.",Descriptions of apparently new Colombian birds.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22875#page/141/mode/1up,Grallaria alticola
15224,species,Passeriformes,Grallariidae,Antpittas,Grallaria quitensis,"Lesson, RP, 1844","L'Écho du Monde Savant (2), 11 no.49 col.848",Tawny Antpitta,Tawny Antpitta,Tawny Antpitta,747,"The Grallaria quitensis sensu lato complex is treated as three monotypic species based on differences in vocalizations, supported by modest plumage differences (Krabbe & Schulenberg 2003; Boesman 2016ii): G. alticola; G. atuensis; and G. quitensis. While mitochondrial DNA and genomic data (Winger et al. 2015) support recognition of G. alticola, taxon atuensis was not included in the analysis.","central Andes of Colombia, Ecuador, and far northern Peru",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103660417,tawant3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/tawant3/,avibase-356BAAED,,,"vicinity of Quito, Ecuador.",Révision du genre grallaria.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/180990#page/396/mode/1up,Grallaria quitensis
15225,species,Passeriformes,Grallariidae,Antpittas,Grallaria atuensis,"Carriker, MA, 1933",Proceedings of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Philadelphia 85 p.22,Atuen Antpitta,Atuen Antpitta,Atuen Antpitta,747,"The Grallaria quitensis sensu lato complex is treated as three monotypic species based on differences in vocalizations, supported by modest plumage differences (Krabbe & Schulenberg 2003; Boesman 2016ii): G. alticola; G. atuensis; and G. quitensis. While mitochondrial DNA and genomic data (Winger et al. 2015) support recognition of G. alticola, taxon atuensis was not included in the analysis.",Andes of northern Peru (southern Amazonas and eastern La Libertad),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103660431,tawant4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/tawant4/,avibase-4ECE7CED,,,"Atuen, 12,000 feet, Amazonas, Peru.","Descriptions of new Birds from Peru, with notes on other little-known species.",https://www.jstor.org/stable/4064167,Grallaria quitensis atuensis
15226,species,Passeriformes,Grallariidae,Antpittas,Grallaria urraoensis,"Carantón-Ayala, D; Certuche-Cubillos, K, 2010",Ornitología Colombiana,Urrao Antpitta,Urrao Antpitta,Urrao Antpitta,397,"The name Grallaria urraoensis is adopted for the Urrao Antpitta, as the type material of G. fenwickorum is considered inadequate. The photos of G. fenwickorum that form part of the type material are not comprehensive in showing the features of the species, and can be readily altered, and the feathers were not lodged in an organized natural history collection (Peterson 2013), such that their ultimate fate is subject to question.",northern part of western Andes of Colombia (Antioquia),,CR,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22736345,antant1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/antant1/,avibase-722C29AB,,,"Reserva Natural Colibrí del Sol, sur del Páramo de Frontino, vereda El Chuscal, 17 Km. al norte del Poblado de Urrao, 06 26' N, 76 05'W, Antioquia, Colombia.",A new species of antpitta (Grallariidae: Grallaria) from the northern sector of the western Andes of Colombia,https://asociacioncolombianadeornitologia.org/wp-content/uploads/revista/oc9/MS1004-Caranton.pdf,Grallaria urraoensis
