15508,subspecies,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Deconychura typica minor,"Todd, WEC, 1919",Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington 30 p.116,,,,,,tropical northern Colombia,,,,lotwoo8,,avibase-FA3DBB07,,,"El Tambor, Santander, Colombia.",Descriptions of apparently new Colombian birds.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22875#page/142/mode/1up,Deconychura typica minor
15509,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Deconychura longicauda,"(Pelzeln, A, 1868)","Zur Ornithologie Brasiliens. Resultate von Johann Natterers Reisen in den Jahren 1817 bis 1835 Abth.1 p.42,60",Whistling Long-tailed Woodcreeper,Whistling Woodcreeper,Northern Long-tailed Woodcreeper,715,"Three species are recognized in the Deconychura longicauda complex based on a combination of mitochondrial DNA (Barbosa 2010) and vocal (Boesman 2016mm) evidence: polytypic D. typica (typica, darienensis, and minor); nominate D. longicauda (monotypic); and polytypic D. pallida (pallida, connectens, and zimmeri). Both vocal and mtDNA data indicate the presence of an unnamed taxon in the Andean foothills (Barbosa 2010; Boesman 2016mm; see also Schulenberg et al. 2010) that probably represents a fourth species; formal nomenclatural description of this taxon is underway.",the Guianas and Brazil north of the Amazon River (from Rio Negro eastward to Amapá),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103661261,lotwoo4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/lotwoo4/,avibase-15B327AC,,,"Borba, Marabitanas, Barra do Rio Negro = Manaus.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/21811#page/70/mode/1up,Dendrocincla longicauda
15510,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Deconychura pallida,"Zimmer, JT, 1929","Field Museum of Natural History Publication, Zoological Series Ser., 17 p.6",Mournful Long-tailed Woodcreeper,Mournful Woodcreeper,Southern Long-tailed Woodcreeper,715,"Three species are recognized in the Deconychura longicauda complex based on a combination of mitochondrial DNA (Barbosa 2010) and vocal (Boesman 2016mm) evidence: polytypic D. typica (typica, darienensis, and minor); nominate D. longicauda (monotypic); and polytypic D. pallida (pallida, connectens, and zimmeri). Both vocal and mtDNA data indicate the presence of an unnamed taxon in the Andean foothills (Barbosa 2010; Boesman 2016mm; see also Schulenberg et al. 2010) that probably represents a fourth species; formal nomenclatural description of this taxon is underway.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103661265,lotwoo5,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/lotwoo5/,avibase-3B21E1E3,,,"Hyutanahan, Rio Purvis, Brazil.",The Birds of the Neotropical genus Deconychura.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/21064#page/14/mode/1up,Deconychura longicauda pallida
