15693,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Xiphorhynchus erythropygius,"(Sclater, PL, 1860)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.27, no.3 p.366",Spotted Woodcreeper,Spotted Woodcreeper,,719,"Taxon aequatorialis (polytypic, including punctigula and insolitus) is treated as conspecific with Xiphorhynchus erythropygius pending further research. Sometimes split as a separate species based on vocal (Boesman 2016oo) and plumage differences; however, vocalizations are variable within taxa and formal bioacoustic and playback experiments are lacking. Furthermore, Johnson & Mason (2022) suggested that there may be three vocal groups in the complex; further research needed to determine species limits.",,,NE,,spowoo1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/spowoo1/,avibase-9FBAF868,,,"Veracruz and Oaxaca; type from Jalapa, Veracruz, Mexico.","On a Series of Birds collected in the vicinity of Jalapa, in Southern Mexico.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/156166#page/458/mode/1up,Dendrornis erythropygia
