15996,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Automolus melanopezus,"(Sclater, PL, 1858)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.26, no.350 p.61",Brown-rumped Foliage-gleaner,Brown-rumped Foliage-gleaner,Brown-rumped Foliage-gleaner,,,"southeastern Colombia to southeastern Peru, far northwestern Bolivia, and western Amazonian Brazil",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22702938,brfgle1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/brfgle1/,avibase-A1CCBC5B,,,"Rio Napo, Ecuador.",Notes on a Collection of Birds received by M. Verreaux of Paris from the Rio Napo in the Republic of Ecuador.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/100585#page/95/mode/1up,Anabates melanopezus
15997,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Automolus cervinigularis,"(Sclater, PL, 1857)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.24, no.318 p.288",Fawn-throated Foliage-gleaner,Fawn-throated Foliage-gleaner,Fawn-throated Foliage-gleaner,734,"The Automolus ochrolaemus complex is treated as three species based on genetics, supported by vocalizations: monotypic A. exsertus; polytypic A. cervinigularis (including hypophaeus); and polytypic A. ochrolaemus (all other subspecies). Although A. exsertus has sometimes been recognized based on vocal discrimination experiments with allopatric hypophaeus (Freeman & Montgomery 2017), a comprehensive analysis of vocalizations in this complex is lacking. Mitochondrial DNA data (Smith et al. 2014) recovered exsertus as a deeply diverged sister lineage to a clade composed of other Middle American taxa (cervinigularis and hypophaeus), and both are deeply diverged from other members of the A. ochrolaemus complex, supporting a three-way split.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/244681681,butfog9,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/butfog9/,avibase-82B02D55,,,"Cordoba, Veracruz, Mexico.","Catalogue of the Birds collected by M. Auguste Sallé in Southern Mexico, with Descriptions of New Species.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46214#page/346/mode/1up,Anabates cervinigularis
