16000,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Automolus exsertus,"Bangs, O, 1901","The Auk 18, no.4 p.367",Chiriqui Foliage-gleaner,Chiriqui Foliage-gleaner,Chiriqui Foliage-gleaner,734,"The Automolus ochrolaemus complex is treated as three species based on genetics, supported by vocalizations: monotypic A. exsertus; polytypic A. cervinigularis (including hypophaeus); and polytypic A. ochrolaemus (all other subspecies). Although A. exsertus has sometimes been recognized based on vocal discrimination experiments with allopatric hypophaeus (Freeman & Montgomery 2017), a comprehensive analysis of vocalizations in this complex is lacking. Mitochondrial DNA data (Smith et al. 2014) recovered exsertus as a deeply diverged sister lineage to a clade composed of other Middle American taxa (cervinigularis and hypophaeus), and both are deeply diverged from other members of the A. ochrolaemus complex, supporting a three-way split.",Pacific slope of southwestern Costa Rica to western Panama (Chiriquí),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/232777577,butfog4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/butfog4/,avibase-3083EA83,,,"Divala, Chiriqui.","On a collection of birds made by W. W. Brown, Jr., at David and Divala, Chiriqui.",https://sora.unm.edu/sites/default/files/journals/auk/v018n04/p0355-p0370.pdf,Automolus exsertus
16001,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Automolus ochrolaemus,"(Tschudi, JJ, 1844)",Archiv für Naturgeschichte 10 p.295,Ochre-throated Foliage-gleaner,Ochre-throated Foliage-gleaner,Ochre-throated Foliage-gleaner,734,"The Automolus ochrolaemus complex is treated as three species based on genetics, supported by vocalizations: monotypic A. exsertus; polytypic A. cervinigularis (including hypophaeus); and polytypic A. ochrolaemus (all other subspecies). Although A. exsertus has sometimes been recognized based on vocal discrimination experiments with allopatric hypophaeus (Freeman & Montgomery 2017), a comprehensive analysis of vocalizations in this complex is lacking. Mitochondrial DNA data (Smith et al. 2014) recovered exsertus as a deeply diverged sister lineage to a clade composed of other Middle American taxa (cervinigularis and hypophaeus), and both are deeply diverged from other members of the A. ochrolaemus complex, supporting a three-way split.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/232777230,btfgle1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/btfgle1/,avibase-9E699193,,,Peru.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/48694#page/309/mode/1up,Anabates ochrolaemus
