16066,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Furnarius cinnamomeus,"(Lesson, RP, 1844)","Revue Zoologique, par la Société Cuvierienne 7 p.433",Pacific Hornero,Pacific Hornero,Pacific Hornero,730,"Three species are recognized in the Furnarius leucopus complex based on a combination of vocalizations, morphology (including plumage and iris color), supported, in part, by genetic data: polytypic F. leucopus; monotypic F. cinnamomeus; and polytypic F. longirostris (including endoecus). Genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) indicate that the Furnarius leucopus sensu lato complex is paraphyletic with respect to F. torridus, supporting the split of cinnamomeus, however, this study did not include samples of longirostris/endoecus. Evidence of genetic and vocal divergence within the polytypic leucopus sensu stricto clade (Boesman 2016ss; Harvey et al. 2020) suggest that further splits may be warranted.","far southwestern Colombia (Nariño), western Ecuador, and northwestern Peru",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103670862,palhor4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/palhor4/,avibase-09CA444F,,,"Guayaquil, Ecuador.",Oiseaux nouveaux.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/19478#page/441/mode/1up,Picolaptes cinnamomeus
16067,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Furnarius longirostris,"Pelzeln, A, 1856",Sitzungsberichte der Kaiserlichen Akademie der Wissenschaften. Mathematisch-Naturwissenschaftliche Classe 20 p.158 pl.2 fig.2,Caribbean Hornero,Caribbean Hornero,Caribbean Hornero,730,"Three species are recognized in the Furnarius leucopus complex based on a combination of vocalizations, morphology (including plumage and iris color), supported, in part, by genetic data: polytypic F. leucopus; monotypic F. cinnamomeus; and polytypic F. longirostris (including endoecus). Genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) indicate that the Furnarius leucopus sensu lato complex is paraphyletic with respect to F. torridus, supporting the split of cinnamomeus, however, this study did not include samples of longirostris/endoecus. Evidence of genetic and vocal divergence within the polytypic leucopus sensu stricto clade (Boesman 2016ss; Harvey et al. 2020) suggest that further splits may be warranted.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103670838,palhor5,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/palhor5/,avibase-F335951B,,,Venezuela.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/108785#page/172/mode/1up,Furnarius longirostris
