16070,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Furnarius leucopus,"Swainson, WJ, 1838",Animals in Menageries. In: The Cabinet Cyclopædia conducted by the Rev. Dionysius Lardner p.325 fig.67a no.133,Pale-legged Hornero,Pale-legged Hornero,Pale-legged Hornero,730,"Three species are recognized in the Furnarius leucopus complex based on a combination of vocalizations, morphology (including plumage and iris color), supported, in part, by genetic data: polytypic F. leucopus; monotypic F. cinnamomeus; and polytypic F. longirostris (including endoecus). Genomic data (Harvey et al. 2020) indicate that the Furnarius leucopus sensu lato complex is paraphyletic with respect to F. torridus, supporting the split of cinnamomeus, however, this study did not include samples of longirostris/endoecus. Evidence of genetic and vocal divergence within the polytypic leucopus sensu stricto clade (Boesman 2016ss; Harvey et al. 2020) suggest that further splits may be warranted.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103670881,palhor3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/palhor3/,avibase-71B6E38F,,,Guiana i.e. British Guiana.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/92073#page/337/mode/1up,Furnarius leucopus
