16141,subspecies,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Aphrastura spinicauda subantarctica,"Rozzi, R; Quilodrán, CS; Botero-Delgadillo, E; Crego, RD; Napolitano, C; Barroso, O; Torres-Mura, JC; Vásquez, RA, 2022",Scientific Reports 12 13957,,,,,,Diego Ramirez Archipelago (south of Chile),,,,thtray5,,avibase-0C415001,,,,"The Subantarctic Rayadito (Aphrastura subantarctica), a new bird species on the southernmost islands of the Americas",https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-022-17985-4,Aphrastura subantarctica
16142,genus,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Sylviorthorhynchus,"Gay, C, 1845",Historia física y política de Chile 1 p.315,,,,,,,,,,,,,M,"Sylviorthorhynchus desmurii [Gay, 1845]; type by monotypy",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/130100#page/319/mode/1up,Sylviorthorhynchus
16143,species,Passeriformes,Furnariidae,Ovenbirds and Woodcreepers,Sylviorthorhynchus desmurii,"Gay, C, 1845",Historia física y política de Chile 1 p.316 Atlas 2 Orn. pl.[3],Des Murs's Wiretail,Des Murs's Wiretail,Des Murs's Wiretail,N-33,"Sylviorthorhynchus desmursii has also been used. The spelling desmurii is the original one, and there are strong indications that it was not an inadvertent error, as it was used multiple times by Oeillet Des Murs himself. The spelling desmursii is an incorrect subsequent spelling predominantly propagated by Peters’ Checklist. There is much controversy over whether this incorrect subsequent spelling is in prevailing usage. The Code's interpretation is strictly tied to the definition of terms in its Glossary, where prevailing usage is defined as the usage by ""authors"" in their ""work"". The Glossary has no official definition of ""author"". However, its definition of ""work"" includes ""any text or illustration, whether published, unpublished, or carrying a disclaimer"". So clearly, the usage in sources other than peer-reviewed papers also counts towards ""prevailing usage"" and a conventional Google search could be viewed as providing a fair arbitration on current usage. At the time of assessment, the usage of desmursii on Google Scholar was more than 2 orders of magnitude higher than that of the original spelling, but on conventional Google, it was used more frequently at only less than one order of magnitude, with a rising trend for the use of desmurii following the discovery that it had been the intended spelling. Hence, a narrow majority of our community felt that the incorrect spelling desmursii had not obtained sufficient prevailing usage (or had lost a sufficient part of it in recent years) to warrant its perpetuation as ""in prevailing usage"", resulting in the re-acceptance of the original spelling desmurii.",central and southern Chile and adjacent Argentina,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22702150,demwir1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/demwir1/,avibase-37179E49,,,"Province of Valdivia, particularly near Corral, Chile.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/130100#page/320/mode/1up,Sylviorthorhynchus Desmurii
