16599,subspecies,Passeriformes,Maluridae,"Grasswrens, Fairywrens, and Emu-wrens",Amytornis barbatus diamantina,"Schodde, R; Christidis, L, 1987",The Emu 87 p.188-192,,,,,,"floodplains of east-central Australia (lower Bulloo River, southwestern Queensland, and adjacent northwestern New South Wales)",,,,grygra3,,avibase-CAC7BA78,,,,Genetic differentiation and subspeciation in the Grey Grasswren Amytornis barbatus (Maluridae).,https://doi.org/10.1071/MU9870188,Amytornis barbatus diamantina
16600,species,Passeriformes,Maluridae,"Grasswrens, Fairywrens, and Emu-wrens",Amytornis whitei,"Mathews, GM, 1910",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 25 p.34,Pilbara Grasswren,Pilbara Grasswren,,988,"The Amytornis striatus sensu lato complex is treated as four species based on a combination of genetic, plumage, and ecological differences following Christidis et al. (2010, 2013): A. whitei; A. oweni; A. striatus; and A. rowleyi. Sometimes treated as three species (Black et al. 2020) based on a lack of mitochondrial DNA divergence between whitei and oweni, strong ecological differences between these relatively cryptic taxa suggest that they are better treated as species pending further research. A genomic DNA perspective is needed to confirm species and subspecies limits in this complex.",,,NE,,strgra4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/strgra4/,avibase-E3A8871E,,,"Coongan River, midwestern Australia.",On a new subspecies (sic) of Grass-Wren.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/120095#page/302/mode/1up,Amytornis whitei
