16606,species,Passeriformes,Maluridae,"Grasswrens, Fairywrens, and Emu-wrens",Amytornis rowleyi,"Schodde, R; Mason, IJ, 1999",Directory of Australian birds. Passerines p.1-851,Opalton Grasswren,Opalton Grasswren,,988,"The Amytornis striatus sensu lato complex is treated as four species based on a combination of genetic, plumage, and ecological differences following Christidis et al. (2010, 2013): A. whitei; A. oweni; A. striatus; and A. rowleyi. Sometimes treated as three species (Black et al. 2020) based on a lack of mitochondrial DNA divergence between whitei and oweni, strong ecological differences between these relatively cryptic taxa suggest that they are better treated as species pending further research. A genomic DNA perspective is needed to confirm species and subspecies limits in this complex.","east-central Australia (Forsyth Range, central Queensland)",,NE,,rusgra1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rusgra1/,avibase-0BCEFC8F,,,,,https://books.google.ca/books?id=XXbJoaGF36YC&pg=PT146,Amytornis striatus rowleyi
16607,species,Passeriformes,Maluridae,"Grasswrens, Fairywrens, and Emu-wrens",Amytornis striatus,"(Gould, J, 1840)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.7, no.82 p.143",Striated Grasswren,Striated Grasswren,,988,"The Amytornis striatus sensu lato complex is treated as four species based on a combination of genetic, plumage, and ecological differences following Christidis et al. (2010, 2013): A. whitei; A. oweni; A. striatus; and A. rowleyi. Sometimes treated as three species (Black et al. 2020) based on a lack of mitochondrial DNA divergence between whitei and oweni, strong ecological differences between these relatively cryptic taxa suggest that they are better treated as species pending further research. A genomic DNA perspective is needed to confirm species and subspecies limits in this complex.",,,NE,,strgra2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/strgra2/,avibase-A860A9AA,,,"lower Namoi River, New South Wales.","Letter from Van Diemen's Land, accompanied with descriptions of some new Australian Birds.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/96163#page/673/mode/1up,Dasyornis striatus
