16927,species,Passeriformes,Acanthizidae,"Gerygones, Thornbills, Scrubwrens, and Allies",Sericornis frontalis,"(Vigors, NA; Horsfield, T, 1827)","Transactions of the Linnean Society of London 15, pt.1 p.226",White-browed Scrubwren,White-browed Scrubwren,,234,Taxon maculatus (polytypic) is treated as a species separate from Sericornis frontalis (polytypic) on the basis of plumage and genetics following Norman et al. (2018). Differences in eye color (Cake 2019) largely support this split except that subspecies ashbyi aligns with the frontalis group; genomic data would be informative.,,,NE,,whbscr1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/whbscr1/,avibase-28FE48D9,,,"no locality = Sydney, New South Wales, fide Mathews, 1922, Birds Australia, 10, p. 7.",A Description of the Australian Birds in the Collection of the Linnean Society ; with an Attempt at arranging them according to their natural Affinities'.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/13694#page/235/mode/1up,Acanthiza frontalis
