17069,genus,Passeriformes,Meliphagidae,Honeyeaters,Sugomel,"Mathews, GM, 1922",The Austral Avian Record; a scientific journal devoted primarily to the study of the Australian avifauna 5 p.7.,,,,,,,,,,,,,N,"Myzomela nigra ashbyi [Mathews, 1912]; type by original designation = Myzomela nigra Gould, 1838",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/111060#page/9/mode/1up,Sugomel
17070,species,Passeriformes,Meliphagidae,Honeyeaters,Sugomel nigrum,"(Gould, J, 1838)",The birds of Australia and the adjacent islands pt2 pl.8,Black Honeyeater,Black Honeyeater,Black Honeyeater,N-38,"Sugomel niger has also been used. According to ICZN Code Article 30.1.3, ""…a genus-group name that is or ends in a Latin word takes the gender given for that word in standard Latin dictionaries."" ""Mel"" is a neuter nominative singular Latin noun, meaning ""honey"". It is inconsequential that Mathews (in 1924) applied a masculine species name to a genus established by Mathews (in 1922). The correct gender needs to be established in the original publication. Hence Article 30.1.1 applies, and Sugomel must be neuter.",western and central Australia (central Western Australia eastward to southwestern Queensland and northwestern Victoria),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22703919,blahon1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/blahon1/,avibase-772E19B8,,,New South Wales.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/177775#page/100/mode/1up,Myzomela nigra
