17085,species,Passeriformes,Meliphagidae,Honeyeaters,Myzomela cineracea,"Sclater, PL, 1879","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1879, pt.3 p.448 pl.37 fig.1",Ashy Myzomela,Ashy Myzomela,Ashy Myzomela,,,New Britain and Umboi Island (southeastern Bismarck Archipelago),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103686550,ashmyz1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/ashmyz1/,avibase-E98DDFE9,,,New Britain.,"On a Fourth Collection of Birds made by the Rev. G. Brown, C.M.Z.S., on Duke-of-York Island and in its vicinity.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/90455#page/198/mode/1up,Myzomela cineracea
17086,species,Passeriformes,Meliphagidae,Honeyeaters,Myzomela simplex,"Gray, GR, 1861","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.28, no.3 p.349",Moluccan Myzomela,Moluccan Myzomela,Moluccan Myzomela,969,"The Myzomela obscura sensu lato complex is treated as four species based on a combination of genetics, plumage, and vocalizations: M. obscura (polytypic); M. simplex (polytypic); M. rubrotincta (monotypic); and M. rubrobrunnea (monotypic). Mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Marki et al. 2017) indicate that M. obscura sensu lato is paraphyletic, with rubrotincta recovered as a deeply divergent lineage from Australian obscura. Subsequent re-evaluation of plumage and vocal differences suggests that the other reddish-tinted members of the M. obscura sensu lato complex, simplex and rubrobrunnea, also warrant separation as species. Nevertheless, a comprehensive morphological, bioacoustic, and genetic review is needed to confirm proposed species limits in this complex.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103686603,dusmyz4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/dusmyz4/,avibase-9A3DA80E,,,Batjan Island.,"List of Birds collected by Mr. Wallace at the Molucca Islands, with Descriptions of New Species, etc..",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46225#page/447/mode/1up,Myzomela simplex
