17088,subspecies,Passeriformes,Meliphagidae,Honeyeaters,Myzomela simplex simplex,"Gray, GR, 1861","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.28, no.3 p.349",,,,,,"northern Moluccas (Halmahera, Damar, Ternate, Tidore, and Bacan)",,,,dusmyz6,,avibase-4286EF68,,,Batjan Island.,"List of Birds collected by Mr. Wallace at the Molucca Islands, with Descriptions of New Species, etc..",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46225#page/447/mode/1up,Myzomela simplex
17089,species,Passeriformes,Meliphagidae,Honeyeaters,Myzomela rubrotincta,"Salvadori, AT, 1878",Annali del Museo Civico di Storia Naturale di Genova 12 p.334,Red-tinged Myzomela,Red-tinged Myzomela,Obi Myzomela,969,"The Myzomela obscura sensu lato complex is treated as four species based on a combination of genetics, plumage, and vocalizations: M. obscura (polytypic); M. simplex (polytypic); M. rubrotincta (monotypic); and M. rubrobrunnea (monotypic). Mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Marki et al. 2017) indicate that M. obscura sensu lato is paraphyletic, with rubrotincta recovered as a deeply divergent lineage from Australian obscura. Subsequent re-evaluation of plumage and vocal differences suggests that the other reddish-tinted members of the M. obscura sensu lato complex, simplex and rubrobrunnea, also warrant separation as species. Nevertheless, a comprehensive morphological, bioacoustic, and genetic review is needed to confirm proposed species limits in this complex.",northern Moluccas (Obi and Bisa),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103686620,dusmyz3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/dusmyz3/,avibase-F1708B0F,,,Obi Island.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/95545#page/348/mode/1up,Myzomela rubrotincta
17090,species,Passeriformes,Meliphagidae,Honeyeaters,Myzomela rubrobrunnea,"Meyer, AB, 1874",Sitzungsberichte der Kaiserlichen Akademie der Wissenschaften. Mathematisch-Naturwissenschaftliche Classe 70 p.203,Biak Myzomela,Biak Myzomela,Red-brown Myzomela,969,"The Myzomela obscura sensu lato complex is treated as four species based on a combination of genetics, plumage, and vocalizations: M. obscura (polytypic); M. simplex (polytypic); M. rubrotincta (monotypic); and M. rubrobrunnea (monotypic). Mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Marki et al. 2017) indicate that M. obscura sensu lato is paraphyletic, with rubrotincta recovered as a deeply divergent lineage from Australian obscura. Subsequent re-evaluation of plumage and vocal differences suggests that the other reddish-tinted members of the M. obscura sensu lato complex, simplex and rubrobrunnea, also warrant separation as species. Nevertheless, a comprehensive morphological, bioacoustic, and genetic review is needed to confirm proposed species limits in this complex.","Biak (Cenderawasih Bay, off northwestern New Guinea)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103686589,dusmyz2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/dusmyz2/,avibase-5E3027B3,,,Mysore [= Biak] Island.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/35269#page/221/mode/1up,Myzomela rubrobrunnea
