17306,species,Passeriformes,Meliphagidae,Honeyeaters,Melithreptus gularis,"(Gould, J, 1837)","A synopsis of the birds of Australia, and the adjacent islands pt1 pl.17 fig.3",Black-chinned Honeyeater,Black-chinned Honeyeater,,976,"Taxon laetior is treated as a subspecies of Melithreptus gularis based on available evidence. Despite differences in plumage and vocalizations, there is a broad zone of intergradation between laetior and gularis, and genetic divergence is consistent with subspecific differentiation based on mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Toon et al. 2010).",,,NE,,blchon2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/blchon2/,avibase-A64689F9,,,interior of New South Wales.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/182460#page/77/mode/1up,Haematops gularis
