17818,species,Passeriformes,Campephagidae,Cuckooshrikes,Edolisoma holopolium,"(Sharpe, RB, 1888)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1888, pt.2 p.184",Solomons Cicadabird,Solomons Cicadabird,,1085,"Taxon tricolor is treated as a species separate from Edolisoma holopolium based on mitochondrial DNA divergence (Pedersen et al. 2018), supported by differences in plumage and possibly voice. Taxon pygmaeum, sometimes split as a monotypic species, is treated as a subspecies of E. holopolium, as its plumage divergence appears less pronounced, vocal differences require further corroboration, and genetic data are lacking; further research needed.",,,NE,,,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/soicus1/,avibase-4D6FC74F,,,Guadalcanal.,"Descriptions of some new Species of Birds from the Island of Guadalcanar in the Solomon Archipelago, discovered by Mr. C. M. Woodford.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/91192#page/230/mode/1up,Graucalus holopolius
