18084,genus,Passeriformes,Malaconotidae,Bushshrikes and Allies,Rhodophoneus,"Heuglin, MT, 1871","Ornithologie Nordost-Afrika's, der Nilquellen- und Küsten-Gebiete des Rothen Meeres und des nördlichen Somal-Landes 1 p.462",,,,498,"Taxon cruentus is retained in the monotypic genus Rhodophoneus based on morphology, ecology, and genetics. A combined analysis of nuclear and mitochondrial DNA placed R. cruentus as a divergent sister lineage to a polytypic Telophorus (only nominate zeylonus and dohertyi included) (Fuchs et al. 2012b). Differences in morphology, proportions, and ecology (e.g., Harris & Franklin 2000), are also considered sufficient to warrant generic recognition.",,,,,,,,M,"Lanius cruentus [Hemprich & Ehrenberg, 1828]; type by monotypy",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/105306#page/54/mode/1up,Rhodophoneus
18085,species,Passeriformes,Malaconotidae,Bushshrikes and Allies,Rhodophoneus cruentus,"(Hemprich, WF; Ehrenberg, CG, 1828)","Symbolae physicae seu icones et descriptiones corporum naturalium novorum aut minus cognitorum quae ex itineribus per Libyam Aegyptum Nubiam Dongolam Syrian Arabiam et Habessianiam publico institutis (etc.) sig.c p.9, pl.3",Rosy-patched Bushshrike,Rosy-patched Bushshrike,Rosy-patched Bushshrike,498,"Taxon cruentus is retained in the monotypic genus Rhodophoneus based on morphology, ecology, and genetics. A combined analysis of nuclear and mitochondrial DNA placed R. cruentus as a divergent sister lineage to a polytypic Telophorus (only nominate zeylonus and dohertyi included) (Fuchs et al. 2012b). Differences in morphology, proportions, and ecology (e.g., Harris & Franklin 2000), are also considered sufficient to warrant generic recognition.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22707623,ropbus1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/ropbus1/,avibase-8B8AC14A,,,"Arkiko near Massawa, Abyssinia",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/189249#page/19/mode/1up,Lanius cruentus
