18204,species,Passeriformes,Platysteiridae,Wattle-eyes and Batises,Batis capensis,"(Linnaeus, C, 1766)",Systema Naturæ. Editio duodecima reformata. Tomus I [part 1] p.327,Cape Batis,Cape Batis,Cape Batis,509,"Taxon dimorpha (polytypic, including sola) is treated as a species separate from Batis capensis (polytypic) based on differences in plumage, bill length, vocalizations, and genetics (Fjeldså et al. 2006; Fjeldså & Bowie 2021). In addition, both species occur in Malawi, with B. c. erythrophthalma identified from the Zomba Plateau, indicating parapatry or sympatry.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22731056,capbat10,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/capbat10/,avibase-9E17E8D0,,,Cape of Good Hope.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/137337#page/331/mode/1up,Muscicapa capensis
