18381,species,Passeriformes,Psophodidae,Whipbirds and Wedgebills,Psophodes nigrogularis,"Gould, J, 1844",The birds of Australia pt15,Western Whipbird,Western Whipbird,Western Whipbird,242,"Taxon leucogaster (polytypic, including lashmari) is treated as conspecific with Psophodes nigrogularis based on available evidence. Although mtDNA data (Burbidge et al. 2017) identified two clades with moderate divergence, vocalizations are similar, and the genetic break does not align with geographic patterns in plumage or morphometrics (Schodde & Mason 1999; Burbidge et al. 2017). Given the potential for mtDNA capture between parapatric taxa, further research based on nuclear or genomic DNA data would be informative.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22705330,weswhi1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/weswhi1/,avibase-D57E208D,,,Western Australia.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/187975#page/73/mode/1up,Psophodes nigrogularis
