18897,species,Passeriformes,Pachycephalidae,Whistlers and Allies,Pachycephala graeffii,"Hartlaub, KJG, 1866","Ibis ser.2, vol.2, no.6 p.172",Yellow-throated Fiji Whistler,Yellow-throated Fiji Whistler,,1207,"The yellow-throated graeffii group is treated as a species separate from the white-throated Pachycephala vitiensis group based on a combination of plumage, vocalizations, and genetics. Mitochondrial DNA data (Andersen et al. 2014) recovered P. vitiensis as polyphyletic, with some deep divergences suggesting there may be multiple species in this complex. Most members of the graeffii group formed a well-supported clade, and this split is also supported by major vocal differences between graeffii and kandavensis. However, comprehensive genetic and bioacoustic analyses are lacking and further research is needed to determine species limits in this complex; in particular the placement of torquata, which was not recovered as part of the graeffii group based on mtDNA (Andersen et al. 2014), and the status of taxa lauana and kandavensis, which were recovered as divergent lineages within the P. vitiensis complex (Andersen et al. 2014).",,,NE,,fijwhi1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/fijwhi1/,avibase-C5A3350D,,,"Viti Levu, Fiji.",On Five New Species of Birds from the Feejee Islands.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/258424#page/204/mode/1up,Pachycephala graeffii
