19151,species,Passeriformes,Rhipiduridae,Fantails and Silktails,Rhipidura semicollaris,"Müller, S, 1843","Verhandelingen over de natuurlijke geschiedenis der Nederlandsche overzeesche bezittingen, Zoologie Land-Volk. p.184, note",Supertramp Fantail,Supertramp Fantail,,857,"The Rufous Fantail complex (comprising the highly polytypic Rhipidura rufifrons, and R. dryas) is divided into eight species based on a combination of genomic data (Klicka et al. 2023b), plumage differences, and vocalizations: Rhipidura dryas (polytypic) centred in northwestern Australia; R. semicollaris (polytypic) mostly from smaller islands of southeastern Indonesia; R. torrida (monotypic) from the northern Moluccas; R. rufifrons (polytypic) centred in northeastern Australia; R. louisiadensis (monotypic) from the Louisiades and D’Entrecasteaux islands; R. melanolaema from the Santa Cruz Is. (polytypic, including agilis from Nendo); R. versicolor (polytypic) from various Micronesian islands; and R. rufofronta (polytypic) from the main Solomon Islands. Additional splits may be warranted in the R. rufofronta, R. semicollaris, and R. melanolaema complexes; further research needed.",,,NE,,arafan2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/arafan2/,avibase-A8281232,,,Timor.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/258134#page/200/mode/1up,Rhipidura semicollaris
