19302,species,Passeriformes,Dicruridae,Drongos,Dicrurus sharpei,"Oustalet, J-FÉ, 1879","Nouvelles Archives du Muséum d'Histoire Naturelle de Paris, Bulletin ser.2, vol.2, fasc.1 p.97",Sharpe's Drongo,Sharpe's Drongo,Sharpe's Drongo,698,"Taxon sharpei (polytypic, including occidentalis) is treated as a species separate from Dicrurus ludwigii based on analysis of plumage, proportions, and vocalizations (Fishpool et al. 2021), and genetics. Mitochondrial DNA data (Fuchs et al. 2017b, 2018b) do not recover D. ludwigii sensu lato as monophyletic, with sharpei being more closely aligned to D. atripennis. Although a relatively deep mtDNA divergence separates sharpei and occidentalis (Fuchs et al. 2018b) they are treated as conspecific pending further research.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/229725407,shadro2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/shadro2/,avibase-84249EE3,,,"Upper Ogowe River, Gabon.",Catalogue méthodique des oiseaux recueillis par M. Marche dans son voyage sur l'Ogôoué avec description d'espèces nouvelles.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/113476#page/109/mode/1up,Dicrurus sharpei
