19535,species,Passeriformes,Monarchidae,"Monarch Flycatchers, Paradise Flycatchers, and Shrikebills",Myiagra hebetior,"(Hartert, EJO, 1924)",Novitates Zoologicae 31 p.270,Mussau Flycatcher,Mussau Flycatcher,Mussau Flycatcher,1050,"Taxon eichhorni (polytypic, including cervinicolor) is treated as a species separate from Myiagra hebetior based on a combination of plumage, vocalizations, behavior, and genetics. Although cervinicolor is sometimes split as a species, multilocus DNA data (Andersen et al. 2015b) show it to be closely related to eichhorni. As genetic data for nominate hebetior is lacking, a more thorough genetic review of the complex is warranted.",St. Matthias Group (north-central Bismarck Archipelago),,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103711371,dulfly2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/dulfly2/,avibase-F33032D8,,,St. Matthias (= Mussau) Island.,The Birds of St. Matthias Island (nr. New Hanover).,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/105790#page/366/mode/1up,Monarcha hebetior
19536,species,Passeriformes,Monarchidae,"Monarch Flycatchers, Paradise Flycatchers, and Shrikebills",Myiagra eichhorni,"(Hartert, EJO, 1924)",Novitates Zoologicae 31 p.271,Velvet Flycatcher,Velvet Flycatcher,,1050,"Taxon eichhorni (polytypic, including cervinicolor) is treated as a species separate from Myiagra hebetior based on a combination of plumage, vocalizations, behavior, and genetics. Although cervinicolor is sometimes split as a species, multilocus DNA data (Andersen et al. 2015b) show it to be closely related to eichhorni. As genetic data for nominate hebetior is lacking, a more thorough genetic review of the complex is warranted.",,,NE,,,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/velfly1/,avibase-13696ACB,,,New Hanover.,The Birds of St. Matthias Island (nr. New Hanover).,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/105790#page/367/mode/1up,Monarcha hebetior eichhorni
