19627,species,Passeriformes,Monarchidae,"Monarch Flycatchers, Paradise Flycatchers, and Shrikebills",Pomarea nigra,"(Sparrman, A, 1786)","Museum Carlsonianum, in quo novas et selectas aves, coloribus ad vivum brevique descriptione illustratas (etc.) fasc.1 no.xxiii pl.23",Tahiti Monarch,Tahiti Monarch,Tahiti Monarch,1059,"Taxon rugensis is placed in the monospecific genus Metabolus, while taxa takatsukasae and godeffroyi are placed in Monarcha. Mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Andersen et al. 2015b) recovered these species, along with Pomarea nigra and P. dimidiata, as an unresolved polytomy at the base of the main Monarcha assemblage. Given the nomenclatural issues that arise due to paraphyly of Pomarea, and lack of statistical support for alternative generic arrangements among these 5 species, the IOC 13.2 classification has been adopted pending a comprehensive genomic review of the complex.",highlands of Tahiti (Society Islands),,CR,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22707178,tahmon2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/tahmon2/,avibase-3B79D946,,,"Society Islands = Tahiti, fide Mathews, 1930, Syst. Avium Australasianarum, p. 525.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/128098#page/105/mode/1up,Muscicapa nigra
19628,species,Passeriformes,Monarchidae,"Monarch Flycatchers, Paradise Flycatchers, and Shrikebills",Pomarea maupitiensis,"(Garnot, P, 1829)","Voyage autour du Monde exécuté par ordre du Roi, sur la Corvette de Sa Majesté, La Coquille, pendant les années 1822, 1823, 1824 et 1825 (etc.). Zoologie 1, pt.2 p.592",Maupiti Monarch,Maupiti Monarch,Maupiti Monarch,N-68,"Dickinson et al. (2019b) lectotypified the specific names pomarea and maupitiensis in a way that the former refers to Tahiti birds and the latter to those from Maupiti. Hence, Pomarea maupitiensis is the correct name for Maupiti Monarch.",formerly highlands of Maupiti Island (Society Islands); extinct,Extinct,EX,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22724444,maumon1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/maumon1/,avibase-57570D50,,,,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/119032#page/242/mode/1up,Muscicapa maupitiensis
19629,species,Passeriformes,Monarchidae,"Monarch Flycatchers, Paradise Flycatchers, and Shrikebills",Pomarea dimidiata,"(Hartlaub, KJG; Finsch, FHO, 1871)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1871, pt.2 p.28",Rarotonga Monarch,Rarotonga Monarch,Rarotonga Monarch,1059,"Taxon rugensis is placed in the monospecific genus Metabolus, while taxa takatsukasae and godeffroyi are placed in Monarcha. Mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Andersen et al. 2015b) recovered these species, along with Pomarea nigra and P. dimidiata, as an unresolved polytomy at the base of the main Monarcha assemblage. Given the nomenclatural issues that arise due to paraphyly of Pomarea, and lack of statistical support for alternative generic arrangements among these 5 species, the IOC 13.2 classification has been adopted pending a comprehensive genomic review of the complex.",forest undergrowth of Rarotonga (southwestern Cook Islands),,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22707172,rarmon1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rarmon1/,avibase-B494521A,,,"Rarotonga, Cook Islands.",On a Collection of Birds from Savai and Rarotonga Islands in the Pacific.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/90542#page/58/mode/1up,Monarches dimidiatus
