19860,species,Passeriformes,Laniidae,Shrikes,Lanius humeralis,"Stanley, ES, 1814","A voyage to Abyssinia, and travels into the interior of that country, executed under the orders of the British government, in the years 1809 and 1810 (etc.) App. IV p.li",Northern Fiscal,Northern Fiscal,,313,"Taxon humeralis (polytypic, including smithii and capelli) is split from Lanius collaris (polytypic) based on genetics. Mitochondrial DNA data (Fuchs et al. 2011, 2019) identified a deep divergence between the northern humeralis group and the southern collaris group. Furthermore, L. collaris sensu lato was not recovered as monophyletic, with L. souzae embedded within the complex. A more comprehensive review incorporating vocal, morphological, and genomic data is needed.",,,NE,,norfis1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/norfis1/,avibase-5792867A,,,"Chelicut, Abyssinia (p. 45 of Salt's Voy. . . .).",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/183286#page/651/mode/1up,Lanius humeralis
