20033,species,Passeriformes,Corvidae,"Crows, Jays, and Magpies",Cyanolyca armillata,"(Gray, GR, 1845)","The genera of birds: comprising their generic characters, a notice of the habits of each genus, and an extensive list of species referred to their several genera 2, pt.11 p.307, pl.74",Black-collared Jay,Black-collared Jay,,1096,"Taxon quindiuna is treated as a subspecies of Cyanolyca armillata pending further research. Although quindiuna differs in coloration and structure, mitochondrial DNA divergence is modest (Bonaccorso 2009), and vocal differences are not discernible. Pending a more comprehensive review incorporating genomic DNA data and assessment of clinality in phenotypic traits, these differences are better treated as subspecific.",,,NE,,blcjay2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/blcjay2/,avibase-423B3BE4,,,"no type locality given; type specimen from 'Bogota', Colombia.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/219462#page/21/mode/1up,Cyanocorax armillatus
