20295,species,Passeriformes,Corvidae,"Crows, Jays, and Magpies",Corvus philippinus,"(Bonaparte, CLJL, 1853)","Comptes Rendus Hebdomadaires des Séances de l'Académie des Sciences 37, no.23 p.830, note",Philippine Jungle Crow,Philippine Jungle Crow,,1070,"Taxon philippinus is treated as a species separate from other members of the Corvus macrorhynchos complex based on mitochondrial DNA paraphyly (Jønsson et al. 2012), supported by vocalizations. Although taxa levaillantii and culminatus are sometimes split from C. macrorhynchos there is insufficient evidence to confirm this split. Future genomic analysis, supplemented by bioacoustic and morphological evidence, will be needed to determine species limits within the C. macrorhynchos species complex.",Philippines including Palawan and Sulu groups,,NE,,labcro15,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/labcro15/,avibase-AC7128AC,,,Philippines.,"Notes sur les collections rapportées en 1853, par M. A. Delattre, de son voyage en Californie et dans le Nicaragua. Seconde communication : Passereaux cultrirostres.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/16564#page/840/mode/1up,Cornix philippinus
