20312,species,Passeriformes,Corvidae,"Crows, Jays, and Magpies",Corvus sierramadrensis,"Rand, AL; Rabor, DS, 1961",Fieldiana Zoology 39 p.577,Sierra Madre Crow,Sierra Madre Crow,,1077,"The Slender-billed Crow Corvus enca complex is divided into 5 species based on a combination of bioacoustic, morphological, and mitochondrial DNA data (Jønsson et al. 2012; Eaton et al. 2021): Sulawesi Crow (C. celebensis, polytypic, including mangoli); Sunda Crow (C. enca, polytypic including compilator); Palawan Crow (C. pusillus, monotypic); Samar Crow (C. samarensis, monotypic); Sierra Madre Crow (C. sierramadrensis, monotypic). Further research is needed to corroborate the division of C. samarensis and C. sierramadrensis, and to assess the depth of divergence of the two subspecies within C. enca sensu stricto.",northern Philippines (Sierra Madre mountains of Luzon),,NE,,slbcro5,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/slbcro5/,avibase-5E184D07,,,"San Pascua, Gonzaga, Cagayan Prov., Sierra Madre, Luzon.","A new race of Crow, Corvus enca, from the Philippines.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/21620#page/7/mode/1up,Corvus enca sierramadrensis
