20647,subspecies,Passeriformes,Remizidae,Penduline Tits,Remiz coronatus stoliczkae,"(Hume, AO, 1874)","Stray Feathers 2, no.6 p.521-522",,,,,,"breeds eastern Kazakhstan, southern Russia (from Altai eastward to Chita, in southern Transbaikalia), northwestern and central Mongolia, and northwestern and northern China (from Xinjiang eastward, excluding Ili Valley, to Ürümqi; northern Ningxia); winter range of migratory populations poorly known",,,,whcpet3,,avibase-03269D5B,,,"no locality; Bora, south of Yarkand, eastern Turkestan, designated by Hartert, 1905, Vogel pal. Fauna, 1, p. 391.",Novelties.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/94439#page/545/mode/1up,Aegithalus Stoliczkae
20648,species,Passeriformes,Remizidae,Penduline Tits,Remiz pendulinus,"(Linnaeus, C, 1758)","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.189",Eurasian Penduline Tit,Eurasian Penduline-Tit,,673,"Remiz macronyx (polytypic) is treated as a species separate from Remiz pendulinus based on comparatively strong plumage differences (Stepanyan 1978; Rasmussen & Anderton 2005). It is known to hybridize with R. pendulinus in the field, which explains the lack of deep mitochondrial divergence between the two despite significant nuclear divergence (Barani-Beiranvand et al. 2017). However, their hybridization is spatially limited, consistent with current interpretations of biological species boundaries. Genome-wide data are required to assess their gene flow interactions and confirm their taxonomic status.",,,NE,,euptit1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/euptit1/,avibase-F81EB049,,,"Poland, Lithuania, Hungary, and Italy.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/209/mode/1up,Motacilla pendulinus
