21008,species,Passeriformes,Alaudidae,Larks,Chersomanes beesleyi,"Benson, CW, 1966","Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 86, no.4 p.77",Beesley's Lark,Beesley's Lark,,212,"Taxon beesleyi is treated as a monotypic species separate from Chersomanes albofasciata based on available evidence. Limited mitochondrial DNA data (Alström et al. 2013, 2023; Miller et al. 2021) indicate a deep divergence between beesleyi and some other members of this complex; however, geographically intermediate populations have not been sampled and there is some overlap in phenotypic and behavioral traits (Donald & Collar 2011); further research would be informative.","northern Tanzania (near Kingerete, Arusha, just north of Mount Meru)",,NE,,beelar1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/beelar1/,avibase-9BEA5037,,,,The Spike-heeled Lark Chersomanes albofasciata in East Africa.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/126843#page/111/mode/1up,Chersomanes albofasciata beesleyi
