21238,species,Passeriformes,Alaudidae,Larks,Corypha hypermetra,"(Reichenow, A, 1879)",Ornithologisches Centralblatt 4 p.155,Red-winged Lark,Red-winged Lark,,1204,"Five new polytypic species are recognized in the genus Corypha based on integrative analysis of morphology (including plumage), vocalizations, and genetics (Alström et al. 2023, 2024): C. kidepoensis (including kathangorensis) is treated as a species separate from C. hypermetra (polytypic, including gallarum); C. athi (including harterti), C. nigrescens (including nyikae), C. kabalii (including irwini and malbranti), and C. kurrae (including bamendae, batesi, henrici, and stresemanni) are treated as species separate from C. africana. Taxon irwinii is poorly known, and sometimes synonymized with C. africana gomesi. However, based on analysis of specimens (n=2) there are clear differences from a specimen of gomesi (and the type description), and the one irwinii that has been analysed genetically was found to be very closely related to kabalii and malbranti (although gomesi has yet to be analysed genetically).",,,NE,,,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rewlar1/,avibase-5F213A7D,,,"Kibaradja [Tana River, Kenya Colony].",Neue Vögel aus Ostafrika,https://www.zobodat.at/pdf/Ornith-Centralblatt_4_0155.pdf,Spilocorydon hypermetrus
