21649,species,Passeriformes,Cisticolidae,Cisticolas and Allies,Camaroptera brachyura,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1820)",Tableau encyclopédique et méthodique des trois règnes de la nature. Ornithologie. 2nd ed. 2 p.459,Bleating Camaroptera,Green-backed Camaroptera,Bleating Camaroptera,492,"The polytypic brevicaudata group is retained in Camaroptera brachyura based on present evidence. Sometimes split based on plumage and habitat differences, the grey-backed brevicaudata group and green-backed brachyura group are vocally similar (Dowsett & Dowsett-Lemaire 1980), and hybridize in areas of contact (White 1962; Zimmerman et al. 2001). Available mitochondrial DNA data (Nguembock et al. 2007) identified deep divergences between brevicaudata, harterti, and brachyura, but further research is needed to define species limits in this group.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103774592,grbcam1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/grbcam1/,avibase-DC456636,,,Cape of Good Hope.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/208154#page/67/mode/1up,Sylvia brachyura
