21944,species,Passeriformes,Cisticolidae,Cisticolas and Allies,Scepomycter winifredae,"(Moreau, RE, 1938)",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 58 p.139,Winifred's Warbler,Mrs. Moreau's Warbler,Winifred's Warbler,477,"Taxon rubehoensis is retained as a subspecies of Scepomycter winifredae, as differences in plumage are subtle and mitochondrial DNA divergences relatively low (Bowie et al. 2009). However, more comprehensive genomic studies are warranted, as nuclear DNA data mostly assorts into two groups corresponding to rubehoensis and winifredae.",,,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22714578,mrmwar1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/mrmwar1/,avibase-31FB812A,,,"Kinole forest, northern Uluguru, Tanganyika.",Description of a new Artisornis.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/125354#page/177/mode/1up,Artisornis winifredae
