22047,species,Passeriformes,Cisticolidae,Cisticolas and Allies,Cisticola distinctus,"Lynes, H, 1930","Ibis ser.12, vol.6, Cisticola Suppl. p.240",Lynes's Cisticola,Lynes's Cisticola,,476,"Taxon distinctus is treated as a monotypic species separate from Cisticola lais on the basis of divergence in mitochondrial DNA, with distinctus recovered as sister to C. subruficapilla (Davies 2014). Apparent differences in plumage, song, and habitat have been reported, but the two taxa are very similar in plumage and reports of vocal differences are conflicting (Dowsett & Dowsett-Lemaire 1993; Zimmerman et al. 2001; Stevenson & Fanshawe 2020); further research needed to confirm this split.",highlands of eastern Uganda and central Kenya,,NE,,waicis2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/waicis2/,avibase-52B4F230,,,"Kidong (= Nkidong) valley, Kenya.",Review of the genus Cisticola.,https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1474-919X.1930.tb08343.x,Cisticola distincta
22048,species,Passeriformes,Cisticolidae,Cisticolas and Allies,Cisticola lais,"(Hartlaub, KJG; Finsch, FHO, 1870)",Die Vögel Ost-Afrikas p.237,Wailing Cisticola,Wailing Cisticola,,476,"Taxon distinctus is treated as a monotypic species separate from Cisticola lais on the basis of divergence in mitochondrial DNA, with distinctus recovered as sister to C. subruficapilla (Davies 2014). Apparent differences in plumage, song, and habitat have been reported, but the two taxa are very similar in plumage and reports of vocal differences are conflicting (Dowsett & Dowsett-Lemaire 1993; Zimmerman et al. 2001; Stevenson & Fanshawe 2020); further research needed to confirm this split.",,,NE,,waicis3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/waicis1/,avibase-5FD10562,,,Natal.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/49512#page/259/mode/1up,Drymoica lais
