22903,species,Passeriformes,Aegithalidae,"Tit-warblers, Bushtits, and Long-tailed Tit",Aegithalos concinnus,"(Gould, J, 1855)",The birds of Asia 2 pt7 pl.65,Black-throated Bushtit,Black-throated Tit,,550,"Taxa iredalei (polytypic, including rubricapillus) and annamensis (monotypic) are treated as conspecific with Aegithalos concinnus pending further research. Sometimes treated as separate species based on plumage and vocalizations, deep mitochondrial DNA divergences and paraphyly with A. exilis (Johansson et al. 2016) also indicate the presence of multiple species (Päckert et al. 2010; Dai et al. 2011; Dai et al. 2013). However, as not all relevant taxa have been studied, and extensive gene flow has been documented between some taxa (Dai et al. 2017), a taxonomic revision of this complex is deferred pending completion of a comprehensive genome-wide analysis.",,,NE,,blttit2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/blttit2/,avibase-94C5E135,,,"Chusan, Chekiang, China.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/118636#page/269/mode/1up,Psaltria concinna
