23197,species,Passeriformes,Phylloscopidae,Leaf Warblers,Phylloscopus grammiceps,"(Strickland, HE, 1849)",Contributions to ornithology 2 p.124 pl.34 fig.1,Sunda Warbler,Sunda Warbler,,320,"Taxon sumatrensis (monotypic) is treated as a subspecies of Phylloscopus grammiceps based on vocal and genetic data. Sometimes considered to be separate species based on call notes and plumage differences, the songs of sumatrensis and grammiceps are indistinguishable (Eaton et al. 2016, 2021) and mitochondrial DNA divergence is low (Alström et al. 2018b). More extensive genomic and bioacoustic research on the P. grammiceps-montis-castaniceps complex is required.",,,NE,,sunwar1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/sunwar1/,avibase-D3BF3262,,,"no locality; Asia, fide Bonaparte, 1850, Consp. Gen. Avium, 1, p. 324; Java, fide G. R. Gray, 1869, Hand-list Gen. Sp. Birds, 1, p. 323.",Illustrations of Ornithology.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/211381#page/269/mode/1up,Pycnosphrys grammiceps
