23305,species,Passeriformes,Pycnonotidae,Bulbuls,Arizelocichla masukuensis,"(Shelley, GE, 1897)","Ibis ser.7, vol.3, no.12 p.534",Shelley's Greenbul,Shelley's Greenbul,Shelley's Greenbul,1012,"Taxon kakamegae (polytypic, including kungwensis) is treated as conspecific with Arizelocichla masukuensis based on available evidence. Plumage differences are slight and vocal differences are poorly documented. Although divergence in mitochondrial DNA is evident (Shakya & Sheldon 2017; De Santis et al. 2018), further research with broader geographic and genetic sampling is needed.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22712760,shegre1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/shegre1/,avibase-6FC57210,,,"Masuku Range, 7,000 feet.","On the Birds collected by Mr. Alexander Whyte, F.Z.S., during his Expedition to the Nyika Plateau in North Nyasaland. With an Introduction by P. L. Sclater.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/54800#page/596/mode/1up,Andropadus masukuensis
