23318,species,Passeriformes,Pycnonotidae,Bulbuls,Arizelocichla fusciceps,"(Shelley, GE, 1893)","Ibis ser.6, vol.5, no.17 p.13",Black-browed Mountain Greenbul,Black-browed Mountain Greenbul,Black-browed Mountain Greenbul,,,"mountains of southwestern Tanzania, northeastern Zambia, Malawi, and northeastern Mozambique",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103818240,easmog4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/easmog4/,avibase-1F66AE1E,,,"Milanji Plateau, 4,000-5,000 feet, Nyasaland.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/85192#page/43/mode/1up,Xenocichla fusciceps
23319,species,Passeriformes,Pycnonotidae,Bulbuls,Arizelocichla striifacies,"(Reichenow, A; Neumann, OR, 1895)",Ornithologische Monatsberichte 3 no.5 p.74,Olive-headed Greenbul,Olive-headed Greenbul,Olive-headed Bulbul,1015,"Taxon striifacies (polytypic, including olivaceiceps) is treated as a species separate from Arizelocichla milanjensis based on available evidence. Sometimes split into 3 species (A. milanjensis, A. striifacies and A. olivaceiceps) but plumage differences support a 2-species treatment with milanjensis, the most distinctive taxon, separated at the species level. Genetic data are fragmentary but mitochondrial DNA (Shakya & Sheldon 2017) supports separation of striifacies from milanjensis. Nevertheless, a comprehensive genetic study and investigation of contact zones is needed to confirm species limits in this group.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22712821,,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/stfgre1/,avibase-9A80B57C,,,"Marangu, Kilimanjaro.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/35473#page/90/mode/1up,Xenocichla striifacies
