23412,species,Passeriformes,Pycnonotidae,Bulbuls,Phyllastrephus cabanisi,"(Sharpe, RB, 1882)",Catalogue of the birds in the British Museum 6 p.83,Cabanis's Greenbul,Cabanis's Greenbul,Cabanis's Greenbul,1016,"Taxon placidus is treated as a subspecies of Phyllastrephus cabanisi (polytypic, including sucosus) based on available evidence. Sometimes treated as separate species based on morphology (Dowsett 1972), taxon sucosus has been shown to be intermediate in size between the two (Dowsett-Lemaire 1990; Dowsett & Dowsett-Lemaire 1993), and they lack significant vocal, behavioral, and ecological differences. Genetic data are fragmentary (Johansson et al. 2007; De Santis et al. 2018), and largely uninformative; further research needed.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22712890,cabgre1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/cabgre1/,avibase-24F71192,,,"Phuket, Thailand.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/34311#page/101/mode/1up,Criniger cabanisi
