23433,species,Passeriformes,Pycnonotidae,Bulbuls,Microtarsus priocephalus,"(Jerdon, TC, 1839)","Madras Journal of Literature and Science 10, no.25 p.246",Grey-headed Bulbul,Gray-headed Bulbul,Grey-headed Bulbul,761a,"The genus Microtarsus is recognized for seven taxa previously included under an expanded Pycnonotus. Five taxa (eutilotus, melanoleucos, urostictus, priocephalus, and melanocephalos) are included in Microtarsus based on the genetic analysis of Shakya & Sheldon (2017) with fuscoflavescens and nieuwenhuisii also placed here based on morphology.",southwestern peninsular India (southern Maharashtra and Goa to western Mysore and Kerala),,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22712619,gyhbul1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gyhbul1/,avibase-D370538F,,,"near the foot of the Perya Pass, Malabar District, Madras.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/176770#page/270/mode/1up,B[rachypus] priocephalus
23434,species,Passeriformes,Pycnonotidae,Bulbuls,Microtarsus melanocephalos,"(Gmelin, JF, 1788)","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I [pars I] p.309",Black-headed Bulbul,Black-headed Bulbul,Black-headed Bulbul,"761a, N-65","((761a: The genus Microtarsus is recognized for seven taxa previously included under an expanded Pycnonotus. Five taxa (eutilotus, melanoleucos, urostictus, priocephalus, and melanocephalos) are included in Microtarsus based on the genetic analysis of Shakya & Sheldon (2017), with fuscoflavescens and nieuwenhuisii also placed here based on morphology.((N-65: The correct species epithet for Black-headed Bulbul is Brachypodius melanocephalos, first published as Lanius melanocephalos Gmelin, 1788. The usage of the name Brachypodius atriceps, based on Turdus atriceps Temminck, 1822, is based on the belief that Brachypodius melanocephalos (Gmelin, 1788) is a junior synonym of Lanius collurio, var. ε melanocephalus Gmelin, 1788 (a name of a subspecies of Red-backed Shrike). However, the latter two names differ by one letter (ICZN Article 57.6), and are therefore not homonyms. Even if they were to be considered homonyms, the name for the bulbul would take precedence because of its higher rank in the original work by Gmelin (1788) (ICZN Article 24.1).",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103836079,blhbul1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/blhbul1/,avibase-C72EC8C8,,,"Sandwich Islands, error; type locality corrected to Sumatra, by Oberholser, 1912, Smiths. Misc. Coll., 60, no. 7, p. 10, footnote 1.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10285#page/321/mode/1up,Lanius melanocephalos
