23439,species,Passeriformes,Pycnonotidae,Bulbuls,Microtarsus fuscoflavescens,"(Hume, AO, 1873)","Stray Feathers 1, no.2, 3 & 4, A new Genus of the Malurinæ - Blanfordius p.297-298",Andaman Bulbul,Andaman Bulbul,Andaman Bulbul,761a,"The genus Microtarsus is recognized for seven taxa previously included under an expanded Pycnonotus. Five taxa (eutilotus, melanoleucos, urostictus, priocephalus, and melanocephalos) are included in Microtarsus based on the genetic analysis of Shakya & Sheldon (2017) with fuscoflavescens and nieuwenhuisii also placed here based on morphology.",Andaman Islands,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103836280,andbul1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/andbul1/,avibase-78E73320,,,"Port Mouat and Mount Harriet, South Andaman, Andaman Islands.",Novelties.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/94983#page/319/mode/1up,Brachypodius fuscoflavescens
23440,species,Passeriformes,Pycnonotidae,Bulbuls,Microtarsus nieuwenhuisii,"(Finsch, FHO, 1901)",Notes from the Leyden Museum 23 no.2 p.95,Blue-wattled Bulbul,Blue-wattled Bulbul,Blue-wattled Bulbul,"761a, 761b","761a)) The genus Microtarsus is recognized for seven taxa previously included under an expanded Pycnonotus. Five taxa (eutilotus, melanoleucos, urostictus, priocephalus, and melanocephalos) are included in Microtarsus based on the genetic analysis of Shakya & Sheldon (2017), with fuscoflavescens and nieuwenhuisii also placed here based on morphology. 761b)) Taxon nieuwenhuisii is recognized as a species (Microtarsus nieuwenhuisii) pending further research. Sometimes considered a color morph or hybrid (Williams 2002), this hypothesis has not yet been substantiated (Collar 2014), leading to its continued treatment as a species.",,,DD,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22712705,blwbul1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/blwbul1/,avibase-84F1B408,,,"Upper Kayan River, near the source of the Bulongan, Borneo.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/37388#page/119/mode/1up,Poliolophus Nieuwenhuisii
