24806,species,Passeriformes,Pellorneidae,Ground Babblers and Allies,Gypsophila rufipectus,"(Salvadori, AT, 1879)",Annali del Museo Civico di Storia Naturale di Genova 14 p.224,Rusty-breasted Wren-Babbler,Rusty-breasted Wren-Babbler,Rusty-breasted Wren-babbler,N-66,"The name for the Rusty-breasted Wren-Babbler is based on the protonym Turdinus rufipectus Salvadori, 1879 (p.224, Salvadori 1879). The epithet rufipectus must be considered a noun for two reasons: (1) ""pectus"" = breast is a noun in Latin. There is a conventional way to form an adjective of this noun: ""pectoralis"". If Salvadori had had an adjective in mind, he could have named the species ""rufipectoralis"", an epithet that has been coined for other bird species (e.g., Ochthoeca rufipectoralis). (2) Whenever one is in doubt, ICZN Article 31.2.2 stipulates that the name must be regarded as a noun.",montane forest of western Sumatra,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22716040,rbwbab1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rbwbab1/,avibase-3B593D10,,,"Mount Singgalang [lat. 0° 24' S., long. 100° 20' E.], Sumatra.",,,Turdinus rufipectus
