24828,species,Passeriformes,Leiothrichidae,Laughingthrushes and Allies,Alcippe davidi,"Styan, FW, 1896","Ibis ser.7, vol.2, no.7 p.310",David's Fulvetta,David's Fulvetta,,341,"The Alcippe morrisonia complex is treated as four species based on genetics: A. morrisonia (monotypic); A. hueti (polytypic, including rufescentior); A. fratercula (polytypic, including yunnanensis and laotiana); and A. davidi (polytypic, including schaefferi). Relatively deep mitochondrial DNA divergences separate these clades (Zou et al. 2007, 2008; Song et al. 2009), while nominate A. peracensis may be nested within this complex (Cai et al. 2019). More studies, including genomic and vocal data, are needed.",,,NE,,gycful3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gycful3/,avibase-39FE95C7,,,,On some Chinese Species of the Genus Alcippe.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/55020#page/356/mode/1up,Alcippe davidi
