24834,species,Passeriformes,Leiothrichidae,Laughingthrushes and Allies,Alcippe morrisonia,"Swinhoe, R, 1863","Ibis ser.1, vol.5, no.19 p.296",Grey-cheeked Fulvetta,Morrison's Fulvetta,,341,"The Alcippe morrisonia complex is treated as four species based on genetics: A. morrisonia (monotypic); A. hueti (polytypic, including rufescentior); A. fratercula (polytypic, including yunnanensis and laotiana); and A. davidi (polytypic, including schaefferi). Relatively deep mitochondrial DNA divergences separate these clades (Zou et al. 2007, 2008; Song et al. 2009), while nominate A. peracensis may be nested within this complex (Cai et al. 2019). More studies, including genomic and vocal data, are needed.",Taiwan,,NE,,gycful1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gycful1/,avibase-F8788273,,,Formosa.,"The Ornithology of Formosa, or Taiwan. [Continued from p. 219.].",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/240123#page/326/mode/1up,Alcippe morrisonia
24835,species,Passeriformes,Leiothrichidae,Laughingthrushes and Allies,Alcippe fratercula,"Rippon, G, 1900",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 11 p.11,Yunnan Fulvetta,Yunnan Fulvetta,,341,"The Alcippe morrisonia complex is treated as four species based on genetics: A. morrisonia (monotypic); A. hueti (polytypic, including rufescentior); A. fratercula (polytypic, including yunnanensis and laotiana); and A. davidi (polytypic, including schaefferi). Relatively deep mitochondrial DNA divergences separate these clades (Zou et al. 2007, 2008; Song et al. 2009), while nominate A. peracensis may be nested within this complex (Cai et al. 2019). More studies, including genomic and vocal data, are needed.",,,NE,,gycful4,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/gycful4/,avibase-A62C0342,,,"Southern Shan State, Upper Burma.",[Description of new species of birds from the Shan States].,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/114181#page/169/mode/1up,Alcippe fratercula
