26614,species,Passeriformes,Turdidae,Thrushes and Allies,Zoothera dauma,"(Latham, J, 1790)","Index ornithologicus, sive systema ornithologiæ; complectens avium divisionem in classes, ordines, genera, species, ipsarumque varietates: adjectis synonymis, locis, descriptionibus, &c. 1 p.362",Scaly Thrush,Scaly Thrush,,104,"The Zoothera dauma sensu lato complex is treated as five species based on a combination of morphology, vocalizations (Weir 2018), and biogeography: Z. dauma (polytypic, including iriomotensis and horsfieldi); Z. aurea (polytypic, including toratugumi); Z. neilgherriensis; Z. imbricata; and Z. major. Analyses of fragmentary genetic data (Klicka et al. 2005; Sangster et al. 2010; Price et al. 2014; Robin et al. 2015) indicate the presence of multiple species within this complex but a more comprehensive review including all taxa is required.",,,NE,,scathr8,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/scathr8/,avibase-F58200CE,,,"India; restricted to Kashmir by Baker, 1921, Journ. Bombay Nat. Hist. Soc, 27, p. 720.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/226470#page/384/mode/1up,Turdus Dauma
