26618,species,Passeriformes,Turdidae,Thrushes and Allies,Zoothera major,"(Ogawa, M, 1905)",Annotationes Zoologicae Japonenses 5 p.178,Amami Thrush,Amami Thrush,Amami Thrush,104,"The Zoothera dauma sensu lato complex is treated as five species based on a combination of morphology, vocalizations (Weir 2018), and biogeography: Z. dauma (polytypic, including iriomotensis and horsfieldi); Z. aurea (polytypic, including toratugumi); Z. neilgherriensis; Z. imbricata; and Z. major. Analyses of fragmentary genetic data (Klicka et al. 2005; Sangster et al. 2010; Price et al. 2014; Robin et al. 2015) indicate the presence of multiple species within this complex but a more comprehensive review including all taxa is required.","Amami Ōshima (northern Ryukyu Islands, southern Japan)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22708496,scathr6,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/scathr6/,avibase-8BAD426A,,,Amami-0-Shima.,Notes on Mr. Alan Owston's collection of birds from the islands lying between Kinsin and Formosa.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/152505#page/200/mode/1up,Geocichla major
