26973,species,Passeriformes,Turdidae,Thrushes and Allies,Turdus ardosiaceus,"Vieillot, LJP, 1822",Tableau encyclopédique et méthodique des trois règnes de la nature. Ornithologie. 2nd ed. 1 p.646-647,Eastern Red-legged Thrush,,Eastern Red-legged Thrush,90,"The Turdus plumbeus complex is treated as two species based on plumage and genetics: T. ardosiaceus (polytypic, including albiventris) and T. plumbeus (polytypic). Genomic (Batista et al. 2020) and mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Nylander et al. 2008; Ricklefs & Bermingham 2008; Batista et al. 2020) support recognition of T. ardosiaceus. However, taxon rubripes, sometimes split as a separate species, is treated as conspecific with T. plumbeus based on the presence of intermediate phenotypes between rubripes and schistaceus along their contact zone.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103891946,relthr3,,avibase-6B75CDBA,,,Santo Domingo.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/208154#page/254/mode/1up,Turdus ardosiaceus
