26982,species,Passeriformes,Turdidae,Thrushes and Allies,Turdus migratorius,"Linnaeus, C, 1766",Systema Naturæ. Editio duodecima reformata. Tomus I [part 1] p.292,American Robin,American Robin,,89,"Taxon confinis is treated as a subspecies of Turdus migratorius based on available evidence. There is considerable ecogeographic variation in size and plumage within T. migratorius sensu lato (Aldrich & James 1991), and formal bioacoustic analyses are lacking. Although mitochondrial DNA and genomic data (Batista et al. 2020) indicate that T. migratorius sensu lato forms a complex with T. rufitorques, taxonomic sampling is incomplete; further research needed.",,,NE,,amerob,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/amerob/,avibase-D77E4B41,,,in America septentrionali.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/137337#page/296/mode/1up,[Turdus] migratorius
