27036,species,Passeriformes,Turdidae,Thrushes and Allies,Turdus subalaris,"(Seebohm, H, 1887)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.3, no.37 p.557",Blacksmith Thrush,Blacksmith Thrush,Eastern Slaty Thrush,95,"Taxon subalaris is treated as a species separate from Turdus nigriceps based on plumage, vocalizations, and genetics. Mitochondrial DNA divergence between these species is deep, and they do not form a monophyletic clade (Cerqueira et al. 2016; Batista et al. 2020).","breeds southernmost Brazil (north to Paraná), northeastern Argentina, and southeastern Paraguay; winters northward to south-central Brazil (northward to Mato Grosso and Goiás)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22708863,slathr3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/slathr3/,avibase-89E3147F,,,"Jutuba, presumably in the valley of the Rio Grande, Province of Sao Paulo, Brazil [= Jatuba, western Goias, vide Hellmayr, 1934, Field Mus. Nat. Hist. Publ., Zool. Ser., 13, pt. 7, p. 411].",Description of a supposed new Species of the Genus Merula from South America.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/91212#page/691/mode/1up,Merula subalaris
