27044,species,Passeriformes,Turdidae,Thrushes and Allies,Turdus amaurochalinus,"Cabanis, JL, 1851",Museum Heineanum. Verzeichniss der orithologischen Sammlung des Oberamtmann Ferdinand Heine 1 p.5,Creamy-bellied Thrush,Creamy-bellied Thrush,Creamy-bellied Thrush,,,"eastern Peru to central Argentina, Paraguay, Uruguay, and Brazil",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22708891,crbthr1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/crbthr1/,avibase-17FCF7A0,,,"Brazil ; restricted to Rio Grande do Sul by Pinto, 1944, Cat. Aves Brasil (Publ. Dept. Zool., Sao Paulo), pt. 2, p. 370.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/196124#page/21/mode/1up,T[urdus] amaurochalinus
27045,species,Passeriformes,Turdidae,Thrushes and Allies,Turdus arthuri,"(Chubb, C, 1914)",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 33 p.131,Campina Thrush,Campina Thrush,Campina Thrush,87,"The Turdus ignobilis sensu lato complex is treated as three species based on a combination of plumage, ecological, and genetic evidence: T. ignobilis (polytypic); T. arthuri (monotypic); and T. murinus (monotypic). Although taxon coverage across genetic studies is incomplete, both mitochondrial DNA (Cerqueira et al. 2016; Avendaño et al. 2017; Batista et al. 2020) and genomic data (Batista et al. 2020) indicate that T. ignobilis sensu lato is not monophyletic, with T. maranonicus, and possibly other species, embedded within it. More comprehensive genetic studies and formal bioacoustic analyses would be informative and further splits may be warranted.","eastern Colombia eastward to southern Venezuela and Guyana, southward locally to central Amazonian Brazil, from the east bank of the Río Madeira to the east bank of the Río Tapajós",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103891016,bkbthr3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkbthr3/,avibase-F28463EA,,,"Abary River, British Guiana.",Exhibition and description of two new species of birds from British Guiana.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101093#page/173/mode/1up,Planesticus arthuri
27046,species,Passeriformes,Turdidae,Thrushes and Allies,Turdus maranonicus,"Taczanowski, W, 1880","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1880, pt.2 p.189 pl.20",Maranon Thrush,Marañon Thrush,Maranon Thrush,,,northern Peru (upper Marañón Valley) and adjacent Ecuador,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22708875,marthr2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/marthr2/,avibase-1F4DAD80,,,"Callacate, northern Peru.","Liste des Oiseaux recueillis au Nord du Pérou par M. Stolzman, pendant les derniers mois de 1878 et dans la première moitié de 1879.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/90456#page/261/mode/1up,Turdus maranonicus
27047,species,Passeriformes,Turdidae,Thrushes and Allies,Turdus ignobilis,"Sclater, PL, 1858","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.25, no.344 p.273",Black-billed Thrush,Black-billed Thrush,,87,"The Turdus ignobilis sensu lato complex is treated as three species based on a combination of plumage, ecological, and genetic evidence: T. ignobilis (polytypic); T. arthuri (monotypic); and T. murinus (monotypic). Although taxon coverage across genetic studies is incomplete, both mitochondrial DNA (Cerqueira et al. 2016; Avendaño et al. 2017; Batista et al. 2020) and genomic data (Batista et al. 2020) indicate that T. ignobilis sensu lato is not monophyletic, with T. maranonicus, and possibly other species, embedded within it. More comprehensive genetic studies and formal bioacoustic analyses would be informative and further splits may be warranted.",,,NE,,blbthr1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/blbthr1/,avibase-F2FC64EA,,,Nova Grenada [= Bogota] .,Description of Eleven New Species of Birds from Tropical America.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/100996#page/285/mode/1up,Turdus ignobilis
