27237,genus,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Fraseria,"Bonaparte, CLJL, 1854","Comptes Rendus Hebdomadaires des Séances de l'Académie des Sciences 38 p.536,note",,,,189,"A broad Fraseria comprising eight species is recognized (olivascens, lendu, tessmanni, caerulescens, griseigularis, plumbea, ocreata, and cinerascens), with comitatus placed in the genus Bradornis. Species included in Fraseria form a monophyletic group with strong support, based on a combined analysis of nuclear and mitochondrial DNA (Voelker et al. 2016). However, Bradornis (including comitatus) is non-monophyletic (Voelker et al. 2016); further research required.",,,,,,,,F,"Tephrodornis ocreatus [Strickland, 1844]; type by monotypy",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/16563#page/546/mode/1up,Fraseria
