27296,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Myopornis boehmi,"(Reichenow, A, 1884)","Journal für Ornithologie 32, no.166 p.253",Böhm's Flycatcher,Böhm's Flycatcher,Böhm's Flycatcher,157,"Taxa fuliginosus and ussheri are placed in Artomyias, and taxon boehmi is placed in Myopornis based on genetics. Sometimes placed in Bradornis or Muscicapa, mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Voelker et al. 2016) show these three species to be deeply diverged from both genera. As support for monophyly of the three species is weak and ecological differences with boehmi pronounced, a two-genus treatment is preferred.","Angola to Democratic Republic of the Congo, Zambia, southwestern Tanzania, and northern Mozambique",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22709234,boefly1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/boefly1/,avibase-D5629ECA,,,"Kakoma, Tanganyika.",[Über Bradyornis Böhmi Rchw.].,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101693#page/265/mode/1up,Bradyornis Böhmi
27297,genus,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Artomyias,"Verreaux, JP; Verreaux, JBÉ, 1855","Journal für Ornithologie 3, no.13 p.103",,,,,,,,,,,,,F,Artomyias fuliginosa [J. and E. Verreaux]; type by monotypy,,Oiseaux nouveaux du Gabon,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/49380#page/115/mode/1up,Artomyias
27298,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Artomyias ussheri,"Sharpe, RB, 1871","Ibis ser.3, vol.1, no.4 p.416",Ussher's Flycatcher,Ussher's Flycatcher,Ussher's Flycatcher,157,"Taxa fuliginosa and ussheri are placed in Artomyias, and taxon boehmi is placed in Myopornis based on genetics. Sometimes placed in Bradornis or Muscicapa, mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Voelker et al. 2016) show these three species to be deeply diverged from both genera. As support for monophyly of the three species is weak and ecological differences with boehmi pronounced, a two-genus treatment is preferred.",Sierra Leone to Ghana and Nigeria,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22709226,ussfly1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/ussfly1/,avibase-79993B33,,,"Abrobonko, Fantee (= Fanti), Gold Coast.",On Seven new or lately described Species of African Birds.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/35065#page/460/mode/1up,Artomyias ussheri
27299,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Artomyias fuliginosa,"Verreaux, JP; Verreaux, JBÉ, 1855","Journal für Ornithologie 3, no.14 p.104",Sooty Flycatcher,Sooty Flycatcher,Sooty Flycatcher,157,"Taxa fuliginosa and ussheri are placed in Artomyias, and taxon boehmi is placed in Myopornis based on genetics. Sometimes placed in Bradornis or Muscicapa, mitochondrial-dominated DNA data (Voelker et al. 2016) show these three species to be deeply diverged from both genera. As support for monophyly of the three species is weak and ecological differences with boehmi pronounced, a two-genus treatment is preferred.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22709230,soofly1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/soofly1/,avibase-AD9EBAC2,,,Gabon.,Oiseaux nouveaux du Gabon.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/49380#page/116/mode/1up,Artomyias fuliginosa
