27301,subspecies,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Artomyias fuliginosa minuscula,"Grote, H, 1922",Anzeiger der Ornithologische Gesellschaft in Bayern Band1 no.7 p.58,,,,,,"northeastern Democratic Republic of the Congo to Uganda, northwestern Zambia, and northern Tanzania",,,,soofly3,,avibase-158D59D5,,,"Beni, Semliki valley, Belgian Congo.",Eine neue mittelafrikanische Fliegenschnäpperform.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/137794#page/70/mode/1up,Artomyias fuliginosa minuscula
27302,genus,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Bradornis,"Smith, A, 1847","Illustrations of the zoology of South Africa; consisting chiefly of figures and descriptions of the objects of natural history collected during an expedition into the interior of South Africa, in the years 1834, 1835, and 1836 pt.26 pl.113,text",,,,"189, 190","189)) A broad Fraseria comprising eight species is recognized (olivascens, lendu, tessmanni, caerulescens, griseigularis, plumbea, ocreata, and cinerascens) with comitatus placed in the genus Bradornis. Species included in Fraseria form a monophyletic group with strong support based on a combined analysis of nuclear and mitochondrial DNA (Voelker et al. 2016). However, Bradornis (including comitatus) is non-monophyletic (Voelker et al. 2016); further research required. 190)) Taxa pallidus and infuscatus are placed in the genus Agricola, while taxa mariquensis and microrhynchus are placed in Bradornis based on Voelker et al. (2016). Despite morphological and behavioral similarities, these clades were not recovered as monophyletic based on analysis of nuclear and mitochondrial DNA data (Voelker et al. 2016); further research needed.",,,,,,,,M,"Bradornis mariquensis [Smith, A, 1847]; type by original designation",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/210547#page/493/mode/1up,Bradornis
27303,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Bradornis comitatus,"(Cassin, J, 1857)",Proceedings of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Philadelphia 9 p.35,Dusky-blue Flycatcher,Dusky-blue Flycatcher,Dusky-blue Flycatcher,189,"A broad Fraseria comprising eight species is recognized (olivascens, lendu, tessmanni, caerulescens, griseigularis, plumbea, ocreata, and cinerascens), with comitatus placed in the genus Bradornis. Species included in Fraseria form a monophyletic group with strong support, based on a combined analysis of nuclear and mitochondrial DNA (Voelker et al. 2016). However, Bradornis (including comitatus) is non-monophyletic (Voelker et al. 2016); further research required.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22709271,dubfly2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/dubfly2/,avibase-F21A8321,,,"Muni River, Western Africa = Gabon.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/30013#page/49/mode/1up,Butalis comitatus
