27404,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Eumyias oscillans,"(Hartert, EJO, 1897)",Novitates Zoologicae 4 p.170,Flores Jungle Flycatcher,Flores Jungle Flycatcher,Russet-backed Warbling-flycatcher,"191, 205","191)) Taxon stresemanni is treated as a monotypic species separate from Eumyias oscillans based on differences in plumage, morphometrics, and vocalizations (Garg et al. 2024). 205)) Taxa stresemanni, oscillans, hoevelli, hyacinthinus, sanfordi, and additus are placed in Eumyias based on bioacoustic and genomic data (Garg et al. 2024). The inclusion of additus is supported by mitochondrial and nuclear DNA data (Sangster et al. 2010; Zhao et al. 2023).
