27541,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Stiphrornis pyrrholaemus,"Schmidt, BK; Angehr, GR, 2008",Zootaxa 1850 27-42,Olive-backed Forest Robin,Olive-backed Forest Robin,Olive-backed Forest-robin,200,"Taxa pyrrholaemus (monotypic) and mabirae (polytypic, including sanghensis) are treated as species separate from Stiphrornis erythrothorax (polytypic, including gabonensis, dahomeyensis, inexpectatus, and xanthogaster) based on plumage and genetics (Beresford & Cracraft 1999; Schmidt et al. 2008; Voelker et al. 2013, 2017). Sometimes treated as five species, mitochondrial-dominated DNA data have revealed three deeply diverged lineages within this complex (Voelker et al. 2017) consistent with a 3-species treatment. Further bioacoustic and genetic research is needed to better define distributional and taxonomic limits within this complex.","not well known, but reported in southwestern Gabon south of the Ogooué River and, in northeastern Gabon, north of the Ogooué River",,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22735640,forrob6,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/forrob6/,avibase-E3760281,,,,A new species of African Forest Robin from Gabon (Passeriformes: Muscicapidae: Stiphrornis),http://www.mapress.com/zootaxa/2008/f/zt01850p042.pdf,Stiphrornis pyrrholaemus
27542,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Stiphrornis erythrothorax,"Hartlaub, KJG, 1855","Journal für Ornithologie 3, no.17 p.355",Orange-breasted Forest Robin,Orange-breasted Forest Robin,,200,"Taxa pyrrholaemus (monotypic) and mabirae (polytypic, including sanghensis) are treated as species separate from Stiphrornis erythrothorax (polytypic, including gabonensis, dahomeyensis, inexpectatus, and xanthogaster) based on plumage and genetics (Beresford & Cracraft 1999; Schmidt et al. 2008; Voelker et al. 2013, 2017). Sometimes treated as five species, mitochondrial-dominated DNA data have revealed three deeply diverged lineages within this complex (Voelker et al. 2017) consistent with a 3-species treatment. Further bioacoustic and genetic research is needed to better define distributional and taxonomic limits within this complex.",,,NE,,obfrob1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/obfrob1/,avibase-0DD78D2A,,,Dabocrom.,"Beschreibung einiger neuen, von Herrn H. S. Pel, höllandischem Residenten an der Goldküste, dasselbst gesammelten Vögelarten.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/49380#page/367/mode/1up,Stiphrornis erythrothorax
