27763,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Larvivora akahige,"(Temminck, CJ, 1835)","Nouveau recueil de planches coloriées d'oiseaux, pour servir de suite et de complément aux planches enluminées de Buffon livr.96, vol.3 pl.571",Japanese Robin,Japanese Robin,Japanese Robin,197,"Taxon tanensis is treated as a monotypic species separate from Larvivora akahige (monotypic) based on plumage, vocalizations (Zhao et al. 2016), and genetics. While mitochondrial DNA data show evidence of extensive introgression (Seki et al. 2012; Seki 2023), nuclear microsatellites mostly assort along taxonomic lines (Seki 2023), supporting the split.","breeds on southern Sakhalin Island, the southern Kuril Islands, and Japan; winters in southeastern China (northwestern Fujian southward to Guangdong and Guangxi)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103767606,japrob2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/japrob2/,avibase-76E2708C,,,"Riu Kius, south of Japan ; corrected to Hondo by",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/112979#page/338/mode/1up,Sylvia akahige
27764,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Larvivora tanensis,"(Kuroda, Nm, 1923)",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 43 p.106,Izu Robin,Izu Robin,Izu Robin,197,"Taxon tanensis is treated as a monotypic species separate from Larvivora akahige (monotypic) based on plumage, vocalizations (Zhao et al. 2016), and genetics. While mitochondrial DNA data show evidence of extensive introgression (Seki et al. 2012; Seki 2023), nuclear microsatellites mostly assort along taxonomic lines (Seki 2023), supporting the split.","Izu, Tanegashima, and Yakushima islands (southern Japan)",,VU,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103767625,japrob3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/japrob3/,avibase-20940C94,,,"Nishino-omote, Tanegashima, south of Kiu Siu (sic).",Description of new subspecies from Japan.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/100930#page/512/mode/1up,Erithacus akahige tanensis
27765,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Larvivora komadori,"(Temminck, CJ, 1835)","Nouveau recueil de planches coloriées d'oiseaux, pour servir de suite et de complément aux planches enluminées de Buffon livr.96, vol.3 pl.570",Ryukyu Robin,Ryukyu Robin,Ryukyu Robin,198,"Taxon namiyei is treated as a monotypic species separate from Larvivora komadori (monotypic) based on clear differences in plumage, and genetics, with minor vocal differences also reported. Although these species are separated by a deep mitochondrial DNA divergence (Saitoh et al. 2015), genomic data and a formal bioacoustic analysis would be informative.","breeds Danjo Islands (off southwestern Kyushu) and northern Ryukyu Islands (Tanegashima southward to Tokunoshima); winters southward to the southern Ryukyu Islands (mainly Miyako, Ishigaki, Iriomote, and Yonakuni, southern Japan)",,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103767667,ryurob2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/ryurob2/,avibase-69346554,,,"Korea ; corrected to northern Riu Kius and Tanegashima by Kuroda, 1923, op. cit., p. 106.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/112979#page/337/mode/1up,Sylvia komadori
27766,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Larvivora namiyei,"(Stejneger, LH, 1887)","Proceedings of the United States National Museum 9, no.597 p.644",Okinawa Robin,Okinawa Robin,Okinawa Robin,198,"Taxon namiyei is treated as a monotypic species separate from Larvivora komadori (monotypic) based on clear differences in plumage, and genetics, with minor vocal differences also reported. Although these species are separated by a deep mitochondrial DNA divergence (Saitoh et al. 2015), genomic data and a formal bioacoustic analysis would be informative.","Okinawa (central Ryukyu Islands, southern Japan)",,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103767739,ryurob3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/ryurob3/,avibase-742C395C,,,"Okinawa, Riu Kiu Islands.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/32555#page/658/mode/1up,Icoturus namiyei
