27780,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Brachypteryx poliogyna,"Ogilvie-Grant, WR, 1895",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 4 p.40,Philippine Shortwing,Philippine Shortwing,Philippine Shortwing,203,"The Brachypteryx montana sensu lato complex is treated as five species based on differences in plumage, vocalizations, and genetics: monotypic montana; monotypic erythrogyna; monotypic saturata; monotypic floris; and polytypic poliogyna. Available mitochondrial DNA evidence indicates deep divergences between some of these taxa (Kyriazis et al. 2018; Shakya et al. 2020) but a comprehensive genetic review of the complex is lacking.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103866625,whbsho7,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/whbsho7/,avibase-BCB949A5,,,"mountains of Lepanto, northern Luzon.",New species from Northern Luzon.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101092#page/266/mode/1up,Brachypteryx poliogyna
