27788,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Brachypteryx erythrogyna,"Sharpe, RB, 1888","Ibis ser.5, vol.6, no.24 p.389-390, pl. X",Bornean Shortwing,Bornean Shortwing,Bornean Shortwing,203,"The Brachypteryx montana sensu lato complex is treated as five species based on differences in plumage, vocalizations, and genetics: monotypic montana; monotypic erythrogyna; monotypic saturata; monotypic floris; and polytypic poliogyna. Available mitochondrial DNA evidence indicates deep divergences between some of these taxa (Kyriazis et al. 2018; Shakya et al. 2020) but a comprehensive genetic review of the complex is lacking.",mountains of northern Borneo,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103866633,whbsho8,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/whbsho8/,avibase-1599A511,,,Kina Balu.,"Further Descriptions of new Species of Birds discovered by Mr. John Whitehead on the Mountain of Kina Balu, Northern Borneo.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/55018#page/417/mode/1up,Brachypteryx erythrogyna
27789,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Brachypteryx saturata,"Salvadori, AT, 1879",Annali del Museo Civico di Storia Naturale di Genova 13 p.225,Sumatran Shortwing,Sumatran Shortwing,Sumatran Shortwing,203,"The Brachypteryx montana sensu lato complex is treated as five species based on differences in plumage, vocalizations, and genetics: monotypic montana; monotypic erythrogyna; monotypic saturata; monotypic floris; and polytypic poliogyna. Available mitochondrial DNA evidence indicates deep divergences between some of these taxa (Kyriazis et al. 2018; Shakya et al. 2020) but a comprehensive genetic review of the complex is lacking.",mountains of Sumatra,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103866639,whbsho9,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/whbsho9/,avibase-EED638F3,,,"Padang Highlands, Sumatra.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/36347#page/231/mode/1up,Brachypteryx saturata
27790,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Brachypteryx montana,"Horsfield, T, 1821","Transactions of the Linnean Society of London 13, pt.1 p.157",Javan Shortwing,Javan Shortwing,Javan Shortwing,203,"The Brachypteryx montana sensu lato complex is treated as five species based on differences in plumage, vocalizations, and genetics: monotypic montana; monotypic erythrogyna; monotypic saturata; monotypic floris; and polytypic poliogyna. Available mitochondrial DNA evidence indicates deep divergences between some of these taxa (Kyriazis et al. 2018; Shakya et al. 2020) but a comprehensive genetic review of the complex is lacking.",mountains of Java,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103866595,whbsho10,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/whbsho10/,avibase-98AF741E,,,Java.,Systematic Arrangement and Description of Birds from the Island of Java.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/13692#page/176/mode/1up,Brachypteryx montana
27791,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Brachypteryx floris,"Hartert, EJO, 1897","Novitates Zoologicae 4, no.1 p.170",Flores Shortwing,Flores Shortwing,Flores Shortwing,203,"The Brachypteryx montana sensu lato complex is treated as five species based on differences in plumage, vocalizations, and genetics: monotypic montana; monotypic erythrogyna; monotypic saturata; monotypic floris; and polytypic poliogyna. Available mitochondrial DNA evidence indicates deep divergences between some of these taxa (Kyriazis et al. 2018; Shakya et al. 2020) but a comprehensive genetic review of the complex is lacking.",mountains of Flores (western Lesser Sundas),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103866688,whbsho11,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/whbsho11/,avibase-3353BA88,,,South Flores.,"Descriptions of seven new species of birds and one new subspecies from Flores, and of one new subspecies from Djampea, all collected by Mr. Alfred Everett.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22555#page/188/mode/1up,Brachypteryx floris
