28078,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe hispanica,"(Linnaeus, C, 1758)","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.186",Western Black-eared Wheatear,Western Black-eared Wheatear,,162,"Oenanthe lugens sensu lato is treated as three polytypic species based on differences in plumage and morphometrics (Shirihai & Svensson 2018), and genetics (Förschler et al. 2010; Aliabadian et al. 2012; Schweizer & Shirihai 2013; Schweizer et al. 2019): O. lugens; O. lugubris; and O. lugentoides. Mitochondrial DNA data (Schweizer & Shirihai 2013) revealed three deeply divergent clades consistent with a 3-species treatment, while genomic data (Schweizer et al. 2019) also demonstrate non-monophyly of the O. lugens sensu lato complex. Further research is required to determine if additional splits are warranted.",breeds southwestern Europe (Spain and Portugal eastward to Italy and northern Croatia) and northwestern Africa (eastward to northwestern Libya); winters in the western Sahel (eastward to Niger and northern Nigeria),,NE,,bkewhe1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkewhe1/,avibase-CBB94183,,,"Hispania [= Gibraltar, vide Hartert, 1910, Vog. pal. Fauna, 1, p. 685].",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/205/mode/1up,Motacilla hispanica
28079,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe pleschanka,"(Lepekhin, II, 1770)",Novi Commentarii Academiae Scientiarum Imperialis Petropolitanae 14 p.503 pl.14 fig.2,Pied Wheatear,Pied Wheatear,Pied Wheatear,,,"breeds stony south-central Eurasia; winters to Arabia, Iran, and northeastern Africa",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22710308,piewhe1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/piewhe1/,avibase-2FB34D83,,,"Saratov, lower Volga.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/113648#page/567/mode/1up,Motacilla pleschanka
28080,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe melanoleuca,"(Güldenstädt, JA, 1775)",Novi Commentarii Academiae Scientiarum Imperialis Petropolitanae 14 p.468,Eastern Black-eared Wheatear,Eastern Black-eared Wheatear,,162,"Oenanthe lugens sensu lato is treated as three polytypic species based on differences in plumage and morphometrics (Shirihai & Svensson 2018), and genetics (Förschler et al. 2010; Aliabadian et al. 2012; Schweizer & Shirihai 2013; Schweizer et al. 2019): O. lugens; O. lugubris; and O. lugentoides. Mitochondrial DNA data (Schweizer & Shirihai 2013) revealed three deeply divergent clades consistent with a 3-species treatment, while genomic data (Schweizer et al. 2019) also demonstrate non-monophyly of the O. lugens sensu lato complex. Further research is required to determine if additional splits are warranted.","breeds southeastern Europe (eastward from southern Italy and Croatia), Türkiye, and the Levant eastward to southwestern Kazakhstan and western Iran; winters in the central and eastern Sahel, eastward to the southern Red Sea",,NE,,bkewhe2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/bkewhe2/,avibase-DF26171F,,,"Tiflis, Georgia, Caucasus.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/113774#page/554/mode/1up,Muscicapa melanoleuca
28081,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe cypriaca,"(Homeyer, EF, 1885)",Zeitschrift für die gesammte Ornithologie 1 p.397,Cyprus Wheatear,Cyprus Wheatear,Cyprus Wheatear,,,breeds stony areas of Cyprus; winters in northeastern Africa,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22710312,cypwhe1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/cypwhe1/,avibase-A3148129,,,Cyprus.,"Beschreibung eines neuen Steinschmätzers Saxicola cypriaca, nov. sp..",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/127788#page/407/mode/1up,Saxicola cypriaca
28082,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe seebohmi,"(Dixon, C, 1882)","Ibis ser.4, vol.6, no.24 p.563-564, pl. XIV",Atlas Wheatear,Atlas Wheatear,Atlas Wheatear,163,"Taxon seebohmi (monotypic) is treated as a species separate from Oenanthe oenanthe (polytypic) based on pronounced differences in plumage and ecology (Shirihai & Svensson 2018). However, mitochondrial DNA divergence is negligible (Aliabadian et al. 2007; Wang et al. 2020), possibly due to recent introgression; insights from genomic data are needed.",Morocco to northeastern Algeria; winters to Mauritania,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103773966,norwhe3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/norwhe3/,avibase-3983013B,,,"Djebel Mahmel, Algeria.","Notes on the Birds of the Province of Constantine, Algeria.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/35128#page/621/mode/1up,Saxicola seebohmi
28083,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe oenanthe,"(Linnaeus, C, 1758)","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.186",Northern Wheatear,Northern Wheatear,Northern Wheatear,163,"Taxon seebohmi (monotypic) is treated as a species separate from Oenanthe oenanthe (polytypic) based on pronounced differences in plumage and ecology (Shirihai & Svensson 2018). However, mitochondrial DNA divergence is negligible (Aliabadian et al. 2007; Wang et al. 2020), possibly due to recent introgression; insights from genomic data are needed.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103773898,norwhe,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/norwhe/,avibase-DF526047,,,"in Europae apricis lapidosis [= Sweden, fide Hartert, 1910, Vog. pal. Fauna, p. 679].",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/205/mode/1up,Motacilla oenanthe
