28091,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe bottae,"(Bonaparte, CLJL, 1854)",Comptes Rendus Hebdomadaires des Séances de l'Académie des Sciences 38 p.7,Buff-breasted Wheatear,Buff-breasted Wheatear,Buff-breasted Wheatear,161,"Taxon frenata is treated as a monotypic species separate from Oenanthe bottae (monotypic) based on modest plumage differences. Forming a complex with O. heuglinii and O. isabellina (Zhao et al. 2023), plumage differences among African species are relatively weak and mitochondrial DNA divergence is modest (Zhao et al. 2023). Although genetic data for O. bottae are lacking, its plumage is considered the most distinct, prompting recognition of frenata as a separate species. Further research is needed and may result in a taxonomic revision of this complex.",highlands of southwestern Arabia (Mecca to Yemen),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103774053,rebwhe2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rebwhe2/,avibase-DB59BA9E,,,"no locality ; Yemen designated by Sclater, 1930, Syst. Av. Aethiop., p. 455.","Notes sur les collections rapportées en 1853, par M. A. Delattre, de son voyage en Californie et dans le Nicaragua. Quatrième communication : Chanteurs subulirostres.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/16563#page/17/mode/1up,Campicola bottae
28092,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe frenata,"(Heuglin, MT, 1869)","Journal für Ornithologie 17, no.99 p.158-159",Rusty-breasted Wheatear,Rusty-breasted Wheatear,Rusty-breasted Wheatear,161,"Taxon frenata is treated as a monotypic species separate from Oenanthe bottae (monotypic) based on modest plumage differences. Forming a complex with O. heuglinii and O. isabellina (Zhao et al. 2023), plumage differences among African species are relatively weak and mitochondrial DNA divergence is modest (Zhao et al. 2023). Although genetic data for O. bottae are lacking, its plumage is considered the most distinct, prompting recognition of frenata as a separate species. Further research is needed and may result in a taxonomic revision of this complex.",highlands of Eritrea and Ethiopia,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103774137,rebwhe3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/rebwhe3/,avibase-19ADEF8A,,,"Mensa, Abyssinian highlands.","Synopsis der Vögel Nord-Ost-Afrikas, des Nilquellengebietes un der Küstenländer des Rothen Meeres. (Schluss ; s. Januar-Heft 1869, S. 1-18.)'.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/102837#page/170/mode/1up,Saxicola frenata
28093,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe isabellina,"(Temminck, CJ, 1829)","Nouveau recueil de planches coloriées d'oiseaux, pour servir de suite et de complément aux planches enluminées de Buffon livr.79, vol.3 pl.472 fig.1",Isabelline Wheatear,Isabelline Wheatear,Isabelline Wheatear,,,"breeds south-central Eurasia; winters to northeastern Africa, Arabia, and India",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22710333,isawhe1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/isawhe1/,avibase-E6C6F746,,,Nubia.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/112979#page/437/mode/1up,Saxicola isabellina
28094,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe heuglinii,"(Heuglin, MT, 1869)","Ornithologie Nordost-Afrika's, der Nilquellen- und Küsten-Gebiete des Rothen Meeres und des nördlichen Somal-Landes p.259",Heuglin's Wheatear,Heuglin's Wheatear,Heuglin's Wheatear,"161, N-30","161)) Taxon frenata is treated as a monotypic species separate from Oenanthe bottae (monotypic) based on modest plumage differences. Forming a complex with O. heuglinii and O. isabellina (Zhao et al. 2023), plumage differences among African species are relatively weak and mitochondrial DNA divergence is modest (Zhao et al. 2023). Although genetic data for O. bottae are lacking, its plumage is considered the most distinct, prompting recognition of frenata as a separate species. Further research is needed and may result in a taxonomic revision of this complex. N-30)) The earliest mention of the name has the spelling heuglinii, attributed to a work by von Heuglin (1869: 346-7), wherein the latter author credited Hartlaub & Finsch for the description.","Mauritania to Mali, Cameroon, Sudan, Ethiopia, and northwestern Kenya",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22710348,heuwhe1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/heuwhe1/,avibase-6ADB636C,,,"'Gondar' [errore ; Sudan suggested by Sclater, 1930, Syst. Av. Aethiop., p. 455].",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/49512#page/281/mode/1up,Saxicola Heuglini
