28144,species,Passeriformes,Muscicapidae,"Chats, Old World Flycatchers, and Allies",Oenanthe lugentoides,"(Seebohm, H, 1881)",Catalogue of the birds in the British Museum 5 p.371,Arabian Wheatear,Arabian Wheatear,Arabian Wheatear,169,"Oenanthe lugens is treated as three polytypic species based on differences in plumage and morphometrics (Shirihai & Svensson 2018), and genetics (Förschler et al. 2010; Schweizer & Shirihai 2013; Schweizer et al. 2020b): O. lugens; O. lugubris; and O. lugentoides. Mitochondrial DNA data (Schweizer & Shirihai 2013) revealed three deeply divergent clades consistent with a 3-species treatment, while genomic data (Schweizer et al. 2019) also demonstrates non-monophyly of the O. lugens sensu lato complex. Further research is required to determine if additional splits are warranted.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22710284,mouwhe5,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/mouwhe5/,avibase-3CA06BE3,,,"Sennaar, northeast Africa {_errore = Yemen, vide Sclater, 1930, Syst. Av. Aethiop., p. 445].",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/34309#page/393/mode/1up,Saxicola lugentoides
