28183,genus,Passeriformes,Dicaeidae,Flowerpeckers,Pachyglossa,"Blyth, E, 1843","Journal of the Asiatic Society of Bengal 12, pt.2, no.143 p.1009",,,,1197,"The genus Pachyglossa is resurrected for seven species of flowerpecker: P. propria; P. chrysorrhea; P. vincens; P. melanozantha; P. agilis; and P. everetti are transferred from Dicaeum; and P. olivacea is transferred to Pachyglossa from Prionochilus, based on the mitochondrial-dominated DNA data of Saucier et al. (2019) and Fjeldså et al. (2020). However, basal relationships in this complex remain poorly resolved, and P. olivacea may warrant recognition as a monotypic genus; further research needed.",,,,,,,,F,Pachyglossa melanoxantha [Blyth]; type by original designation,,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/123810#page/525/mode/1up,Pachyglossa
28184,species,Passeriformes,Dicaeidae,Flowerpeckers,Pachyglossa olivacea,"(Tweeddale, A, 1877)","The Annals and Magazine of Natural History including Zoology, Botany, and Geology ser.4, vol.20, no.120 p.536",Olive-backed Flowerpecker,Olive-backed Flowerpecker,Olive-backed Flowerpecker,1197,"The genus Pachyglossa is resurrected for seven species of flowerpecker: P. propria; P. chrysorrhea; P. vincens; P. melanozantha; P. agilis; and P. everetti are transferred from Dicaeum; and P. olivacea is transferred to Pachyglossa from Prionochilus, based on the mitochondrial-dominated DNA data of Saucier et al. (2019) and Fjeldså et al. (2020). However, basal relationships in this complex remain poorly resolved, and P. olivacea may warrant recognition as a monotypic genus; further research needed.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22717451,olbflo1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/olbflo1/,avibase-27665659,,,"Dinagat, Philippine Islands.",LXVII. Descriptions of some new Species of Birds.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/53474#page/550/mode/1up,Prionochilus olivaceus
