28345,species,Passeriformes,Nectariniidae,Spiderhunters and Sunbirds,Kurochkinegramma hypogrammicum,"(Müller, S, 1843)","Verhandelingen over de natuurlijke geschiedenis der Nederlandsche overzeesche bezittingen, Zoologie Land-Volk. pt6,7or8 p.173,note",Purple-naped Spiderhunter,Purple-naped Spiderhunter,Purple-naped Spiderhunter,N-67,"The suffix ""-gramma"" in Kurochkinegramma has the same derivation as in Hypogramma: namely the neuter Greek noun ""gramma"" (=drawing, writing). The species epithet hypogrammicum is an adjectivization, and has been used as such ever since the original coinage of Hypogramma hypogrammicum. Therefore, it should retain its usage as an adjective (and therefore its ending) under the new genus.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22717680,punsun1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/punsun1/,avibase-7700E7E6,,,Sumatra and Borneo.,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/258134#page/189/mode/1up,Nectarinia hypogrammica
