29253,species,Passeriformes,Estrildidae,"Munias, Parrotfinches, Waxbills, and Allies",Taeniopygia guttata,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1817)","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 12 p.233",Zebra Finch,Zebra Finch,,562,"Taxon castanotis (monotypic) is treated as a subspecies of Taeniopygia guttata based on modest differences in plumage, size, vocalizations (Clayton 1990a), and genetics that encompasses both nuclear and mitochondrial DNA data (Balakrishnan & Edwards 2009; Newhouse & Balakrishnan 2015; Olsson & Alström 2020). Although assortative mating has been observed in captivity (e.g., Clayton 1990b), it could have occurred in response to external factors (Burley et al. 1982), or the evolution of local song dialects (Wang et al. 2022), and is not considered evidence of species status.",,,NE,,zebfin2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/zebfin2/,avibase-C532D642,,,Moluccas [= Timor] .,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/60160#page/249/mode/1up,Fringilla guttata
