29361,species,Passeriformes,Estrildidae,"Munias, Parrotfinches, Waxbills, and Allies",Lonchura hunsteini,"(Finsch, FHO, 1886)","Ibis ser.5, vol.4, no.13 p.1 pl.1",Mottled Mannikin,Mottled Munia,,560,"Taxon nigerrima is treated as a monotypic species separate from Lonchura hunsteini based on available evidence. Genomic data demonstrate that this group has radiated recently and rapidly (Stryjewski & Sorenson 2017) and may represent a hybrid swarm. Based on detectable but weak genomic divergence, combined with evidence of geographic replacement amongst other species in this complex, it seems most likely that L. nigerrima is also specifically distinct. However, no data on vocalizations, biometrics, or ecology exist to support this split; further research needed.",New Ireland (northeastern Bismarck Archipelago),,NE,,motmun1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/motmun1/,avibase-9107A335,,,New Ireland.,On two new Species of Birds from New Ireland.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/271312#page/35/mode/1up,Donacicola hunsteini
29362,species,Passeriformes,Estrildidae,"Munias, Parrotfinches, Waxbills, and Allies",Lonchura nigerrima,"(Rothschild, LW; Hartert, EJO, 1899)",Ornithologische Monatsberichte 7 p.139,New Hanover Mannikin,New Hanover Munia,,560,"Taxon nigerrima is treated as a monotypic species separate from Lonchura hunsteini based on available evidence. Genomic data demonstrate that this group has radiated recently and rapidly (Stryjewski & Sorenson 2017) and may represent a hybrid swarm. Based on detectable but weak genomic divergence, combined with evidence of geographic replacement amongst other species in this complex, it seems most likely that L. nigerrima is also specifically distinct. However, no data on vocalizations, biometrics, or ecology exist to support this split; further research needed.",New Hanover (northeastern Bismarck Archipelago),,NE,,nehmun1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/nehmun1/,avibase-84A01BC8,,,New Hanover.,Ein kleiner Beitrag zur ferneren Kenntnis der Ornis von Neu-Hannover.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101400#page/155/mode/1up,Munia nigerrima
