29878,species,Passeriformes,Motacillidae,Wagtails and Pipits,Macronyx sharpei,"Jackson, FJ, 1904",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 14 p.74,Sharpe's Longclaw,Sharpe's Longclaw,Sharpe's Longclaw,549,"Taxon ruficollis is transferred from Madanga to Anthus (Anthus ruficollis) based on analysis of multilocus DNA data and morphology (Alström et al. 2015b), while taxon bocagii is transferred from Amaurocichla to Motacilla (as Motacilla bocagii) based on multilocus DNA (Alström et al. 2015b) and genome-wide (Harris et al. 2018b) genetic evidence. For reasons of taxonomic stability, taxon chloris is placed in Hemimacronyx pending further research. Mitochondrial-dominated DNA data suggest that chloris is closely related to Macronyx croceus and M. capensis (Pietersen et al. 2019), which are embedded within Anthus. Similarly, taxon sharpei is placed in Macronyx instead of Hemimacronyx, pending further research. A comprehensive genetic review of genera Anthus, Macronyx, Hemimacronyx, and Tmetothylacus is needed.",grassy highlands of Kenya,,EN,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22718436,shalon1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/shalon1/,avibase-FED54E53,,,Mau plateau.,A new species of Macronyx.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/114181#page/560/mode/1up,Macronyx sharpei
