29937,species,Passeriformes,Motacillidae,Wagtails and Pipits,Anthus novaeseelandiae,"(Gmelin, JF, 1789)","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I. Pars II 1 pt2 p.799",New Zealand Pipit,New Zealand Pipit,,546,"Taxon australis (polytypic) is treated as a species separate from Anthus novaeseelandiae (polytypic) on the basis of differences in size, wing-tip structure, and plumage as detailed by Schodde & Mason (1999). However, genetic divergence and vocal differences, if any, have yet to be elucidated and further work is needed to confirm this split.",,,NE,,auspip3,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/auspip3/,avibase-74C96ABE,,,"Queen Charlotte's Sound, South Island, New Zealand.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10286#page/300/mode/1up,Alauda novae Seelandiae
