29942,species,Passeriformes,Motacillidae,Wagtails and Pipits,Anthus australis,"Vieillot, LJP, 1818","Nouveau dictionnaire d'histoire naturelle, appliquée aux arts, à l'agriculture, à l'économie rurale et domestique, à la médecine, etc. Nouvelle édition 26 p.501",Australian Pipit,Australian Pipit,,546,"Taxon australis (polytypic) is treated as a species separate from Anthus novaeseelandiae (polytypic) on the basis of differences in size, wing-tip structure, and plumage as detailed by Schodde & Mason (1999). However, genetic divergence and vocal differences, if any, have yet to be elucidated and further work is needed to confirm this split.",,,NE,,auspip2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/auspip2/,avibase-E353F8BD,,,"Sydney, New South Wales.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/60126#page/523/mode/1up,Anthus australis
