30604,species,Passeriformes,Fringillidae,"Finches, Euphonias, and Allies",Loxia sinesciuris,"Benkman, CW, 2009",The Condor 111 169-176,Cassia Crossbill,Cassia Crossbill,,1107,"Taxon sinesciuris is treated as a species separate from Loxia curvirostra based on evidence of assortative mating and near-complete reproductive isolation (Smith & Benkman 2007; Benkman et al. 2009), supported, in part, by genetics. Although sinesciuris forms a separate clade based on analysis of genome-wide data (Parchman et al. 2016), divergence is extremely shallow and renders L. curvirostra paraphyletic; further research needed.",South Hills and Albion Mountains of south-central Idaho (northwestern USA),,NE,,redcro9,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/redcro9/,avibase-5627C990,,,,A New Species of the Red Crossbill (Fringillidae: Loxia) from Idaho,https://academic.oup.com/condor/article/111/1/169/5152452,Loxia sinesciuris
