31349,species,Passeriformes,Passerellidae,New World Sparrows,Melozone leucotis,"Cabanis, JL, 1861","Journal für Ornithologie 8, no.48 p.413",White-eared Ground Sparrow,,White-eared Ground-sparrow,840,"Taxon occipitalis is treated as a species separate from Melozone leucotis based on differences in plumage and vocalizations (Sandoval et al. 2017a), and a consistent pattern of divergence in nuclear and mitochondrial DNA (Sandoval et al. 2017b). Additional investigation of the geographically and phenotypically intermediate subspecies nigrior would provide further insights. After AviList voted on this issue, NACC (issue 2023-C-12) opted not to split occpipitalis, and the issue will likely be reevaluated in a future version of AviList.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103776706,whegrs2,,avibase-10596E74,,,Costa Rica.,Uebersicht der im Berliner Museum befindlichen Vögel von Costa Rica. (Fortsetz. s. S. 321-336.).,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101709#page/425/mode/1up,Melozone leucotis
