31352,species,Passeriformes,Passerellidae,New World Sparrows,Melozone occipitalis,"(Salvin, O, 1878)","Ibis ser.4, vol.2, no.8 p.446-447",Grey-crowned Ground Sparrow,,Grey-crowned Ground-sparrow,840,"Taxon occipitalis is treated as a species separate from Melozone leucotis based on differences in plumage and vocalizations (Sandoval et al. 2017a), and a consistent pattern of divergence in nuclear and mitochondrial DNA (Sandoval et al. 2017b). Additional investigation of the geographically and phenotypically intermediate subspecies nigrior would provide further insights. After AviList voted on this issue, NACC (issue 2023-C-12) opted not to split occpipitalis, and the issue will likely be reevaluated in a future version of AviList.",highlands of southern Mexico (Chiapas) to Guatemala and El Salvador,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103776727,whegrs1,,avibase-A93FF062,,,"Volcan de Fuego, Guatemala.","Descriptions of two new Species of Birds from Central America, and one from South America.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/34861#page/492/mode/1up,Pyrgisoma occipitale
