31435,species,Passeriformes,Passerellidae,New World Sparrows,Atlapetes crassus,"Bangs, O, 1908",Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington 21 p.161,Choco Brushfinch,Choco Brushfinch,Choco Brushfinch,1121,"Taxon crassus is treated as a species separate from Atlapetes tricolor based on plumage and vocalizations (Sánchez-González et al. 2015), supported by elevational niche differences and mitochondrial DNA data from separate studies (Klicka et al. 2014; Sánchez-González et al. 2015). Although deeply diverged, crassus is represented by a short DNA sequence.",Andes of western Colombia and Ecuador (Pichincha and El Oro),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103774244,tribrf1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/tribrf1/,avibase-14D41E23,,,"San Antonio, 5,800 ft., Valle, Colombia.",Notes on birds from Western Colombia.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22870#page/205/mode/1up,Atlapetes crassus
31436,species,Passeriformes,Passerellidae,New World Sparrows,Atlapetes tricolor,"(Taczanowski, W, 1875)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1874, pt.4 p.516 pl.65",Tricolored Brushfinch,Golden-crowned Brushfinch,Tricolored Brushfinch,1121,"Taxon crassus is treated as a species separate from Atlapetes tricolor based on plumage and vocalizations (Sánchez-González et al. 2015), supported by elevational niche differences and mitochondrial DNA data from separate studies (Klicka et al. 2014; Sánchez-González et al. 2015). Although deeply diverged, crassus is represented by a short DNA sequence.","east slope of Andes of central Peru (San Martín southward to western Cusco in the Apurímac Valley), also local on outlying ridges (Cordillera Azul, southwestern Loreto; Cerros del Sira, Huánuco)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103774148,tribrf2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/tribrf2/,avibase-7FE52D63,,,"Chilpes, Paltaypampa, Ninabamba, Pumarca, and 'Tempobata,' Junin, Peru; restricted to Chilpes by Berlepsch, 1912, Verh. V. Intern. Ornith. Kongr. Berlin, p. 1100.",Liste des Oiseaux recueillis par M. Constantin Jelski dans la partie centrale du Pérou occidental.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/90419#page/674/mode/1up,Buarremon tricolor
31437,species,Passeriformes,Passerellidae,New World Sparrows,Atlapetes schistaceus,"(Boissonneau, A, 1840)","Revue Zoologique, par la Société Cuvierienne 3 p.69",Slaty Brushfinch,Northern Slaty Brushfinch,Slaty Brushfinch,1114,"Taxon taczanowskii is treated as a monotypic species separate from Atlapetes schistaceus based on genetics, plumage, and vocalizations. Although modest, mitochondrial DNA divergence (Sánchez-González et al. 2015) is greater than some other species pairs in this complex, and support for their monophyly is weak; further research would be informative.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103774619,slabru1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/slabru1/,avibase-7A6A8753,,,"Santa Fe de Bogota, Colombia.",Oiseaux nouveaux de Santa-Fé de Bogota.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/48713#page/79/mode/1up,Tanagra (Arremon) schistaceus
