31601,species,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus koepckeae,"Lowery, GH; O'Neill, JP, 1965","Occasional Papers of the Museum of Zoology, Louisiana State University no.33 p.1",Selva Cacique,Selva Cacique,Selva Cacique,,,southeastern Peru (known from 3 localities),,NT,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22724043,selcac1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/selcac1/,avibase-7354E7B8,,,"Balta, lat. 10° 08' S., long. 71° 13' W., ca. 300 m., Loreto, Peru.",A new species of Cacicus (Aves: Icteridae).,https://sites01.lsu.edu/wp/mnspapers/files/2017/08/Occasional-Paper-33_updated.pdf,Cacicus koepckeae
31602,species,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus uropygialis,"de Lafresnaye, NFAA, 1843","Revue Zoologique, par la Société Cuvierienne 6 p.290",Scarlet-rumped Cacique,Scarlet-rumped Cacique,,588,"Monotypic taxa pacificus and microrhynchus are treated as conspecific with Cacicus uropygialis pending further research. Sometimes treated as two or three species based on plumage, vocalizations, macro-ecology, or genetics; however, the available data are contradictory regarding relationships. Overall, the three taxa are similar in plumage but mitochondrial DNA data (Powell et al. 2014) recovered uropygialis and pacificus as sister taxa, and deeply diverged from microrhynchus, whereas macro-ecological data align lowland microrhynchus with pacificus (e.g., Ridgely & Greenfield 2001). Formal analyses of vocalizations and assessment of gene flow among taxa are needed.",,,NE,,scrcac1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/scrcac1/,avibase-73399D4E,,,"Colombia ; type from 'Bogota', fide Bangs, 1930, Bull. Mus. Comp. ZooL, 70, p. 417.",Oiseaux nouveaux de Colombie.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/19446#page/298/mode/1up,Cassicus uropygialis
31603,subspecies,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus uropygialis microrhynchus,"(Sclater, PL; Salvin, O, 1865)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1864, pt.3 p.353",,,,,,far northeastern Honduras to eastern Panama (except Darién),,,,scrcac2,,avibase-3D0A4048,,,Lion Hill Station [?] on the Panama Railway.,Notes on a Collection of Birds from the Isthmus of Panama.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/90417#page/437/mode/1up,Cassiculus microrhynchus
31604,subspecies,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus uropygialis pacificus,"Chapman, FM, 1915",Bulletin of the American Museum of Natural History 34 p.657,,,,,,eastern Panama (Darién) to western Colombia and western Ecuador (El Oro),,,,scrcac3,,avibase-43C2C997,,,"Alto Bonito, Rio Sucio, Choco, Colombia.",Diagnoses of apparently new Colombian Birds. IV.,https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/1752,Cacicus uropygialis pacificus
31605,subspecies,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus uropygialis uropygialis,"de Lafresnaye, NFAA, 1843","Revue Zoologique, par la Société Cuvierienne 6 p.290",,,,,,"Andes of Colombia to northwestern Venezuela, eastern Ecuador, and southeastern Peru",,,,scrcac4,,avibase-BD9FCAA1,,,"Colombia ; type from 'Bogota', fide Bangs, 1930, Bull. Mus. Comp. ZooL, 70, p. 417.",Oiseaux nouveaux de Colombie.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/19446#page/298/mode/1up,Cassicus uropygialis
31606,species,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus cela,"(Linnaeus, C, 1758)","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.191",Yellow-rumped Cacique,Yellow-rumped Cacique,,587,"Taxon flavicrissus (polytypic) is treated as conspecific with Cacicus cela pending further research. Differences in plumage are maintained range-wide including in a zone of near-parapatry, and limited mitochondrial DNA data indicate a deep divergence (Powell et al. 2014) but vocal data are equivocal regarding species status; the vocal repertoire is large and colony-specific (Feekes 1981), confounding identification of homologous vocalizations (Boesman 2016ggg). Broader genetic sampling based on nuclear or genomic DNA, and an in-depth analysis of vocalizations would be informative.",,,NE,,yercac1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/yercac1/,avibase-EC71EBAC,,,"'in Indiis,' error; Surinam substituted by Hellmayr, 1906, Novit. Zool., 13, p. 20.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/211/mode/1up,Parus Cela
31607,subspecies,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus cela vitellinus,"Lawrence, GN, 1864",Proceedings of the Academy of Natural Sciences of Philadelphia 16 p.107,,,,,,tropical eastern Panama (Canal Zone) to northern Colombia,,,,yercac4,,avibase-6B3F3891,,,"New Granada, Isthmus of Panama.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/18264#page/115/mode/1up,Cassicus vitellinus
31608,subspecies,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus cela flavicrissus,"(Sclater, PL, 1860)","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London pt.28, no.2 p.276",,,,,,tropical western Ecuador to far northwestern Peru (Tumbes),,,,yercac5,,avibase-CF299BBA,,,"Babahoyo, Ecuador.","List of Birds collected by Mr. Fraser at Babahoyo in Ecuador, with Descriptions of New Species.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/46225#page/358/mode/1up,Cassiculus flavicrissus
31609,subspecies,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus cela cela,"(Linnaeus, C, 1758)","Systema Naturæ per Regna Tria Naturæ, Secundum Classes, Ordines, Genera, Species, cum Characteribus, Differentiis, Synonymis, Locis. Tomus I. Editio decima, reformata 1 p.191",,,,,,"lowlands east of Andes from Colombia (including Caribbean coast near Santa Marta), most of Venezuela, Trinidad, and the Guianas southward to central Bolivia (Santa Cruz) and southern Brazil (Mato Grosso do Sul); also coastal eastern Brazil (Pernambuco southward to southeastern Bahia)",,,,yercac2,,avibase-5EFA0D83,,,"'in Indiis,' error; Surinam substituted by Hellmayr, 1906, Novit. Zool., 13, p. 20.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10277#page/211/mode/1up,Parus Cela
31610,species,Passeriformes,Icteridae,"New World Blackbirds, Troupials, and Allies",Cacicus chrysonotus,"d'Orbigny, ACVMD; de Lafresnaye, NFAA, 1838","Magasin de Zoologie 8 cl.2 p.3 pl.77,78,79",Mountain Cacique,Mountain Cacique,Mountain Cacique,589,"Taxon leucoramphus (polytypic) is treated as conspecific with Cacicus chrysonotus based on phenotypic evidence of intermediacy (Hosner et al. 2015) and lack of supporting data on vocal differentiation. However, Powell et al. (2014) found relatively deep mitochondrial DNA divergence between representative samples. A formal analysis of vocal differences, including assessment of homologous vocalizations and analysis of intraspecific variation, and assessment of gene flow across contact zones is needed.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/22731284,moucac1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/moucac1/,avibase-4663E94B,,,"Yungas, Bolivia.","Synopsis Avium, in ejus per Americam meridionalem itinere, collectarum et ab ipso viatore necnon.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/114209#page/177/mode/1up,[Cassicus] Chrysonotus
