31930,species,Passeriformes,Parulidae,New World Warblers,Geothlypis velata,"(Vieillot, LJP, 1809)","Histoire naturelle des oiseaux de l'Amérique Septentrionale, depuis Saint Dominique jusqu'à la baie de Hudson; contenant un grand nombre d'espèces décrites ou figurées pour la première fois 2 p.22 pl.74",Southern Yellowthroat,Southern Yellowthroat,,529,"The Geothlypis aequinoctialis complex is split into three species based on deep mitochondrial DNA divergences (Escalante et al. 2009), supported by plumage differences: G. aequinoctialis (monotypic); G. auricularis (polytypic, including peruviana); and G. velata (monotypic). A more comprehensive assessment of genetic divergences (including nuclear DNA) and vocalizations is desirable.","southeastern Peru to Bolivia (except southwestern), Brazil, Paraguay, Uruguay, and northeastern Argentina",,NE,,masyel5,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/masyel5/,avibase-65AD203E,,,"no locality; Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, designated by Naumberg, 1930, Bull. Amer. Mus. Nat. Hist., 60, p. 339.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/180312#page/72/mode/1up,Sylvia velata
31931,species,Passeriformes,Parulidae,New World Warblers,Geothlypis aequinoctialis,"(Gmelin, JF, 1789)","Systema Naturae. Editio decima tertia, aucta, reformata. Cura Jo. Frid. Gmelin (etc.). Tomus I. Pars II 1 pt2 p.972",Masked Yellowthroat,Masked Yellowthroat,,529,"The Geothlypis aequinoctialis complex is split into three species based on deep mitochondrial DNA divergences (Escalante et al. 2009), supported by plumage differences: G. aequinoctialis (monotypic); G. auricularis (polytypic, including peruviana); and G. velata (monotypic). A more comprehensive assessment of genetic divergences (including nuclear DNA) and vocalizations is desirable.","northeastern Colombia to Venezuela, Trinidad, the Guianas, and northern Brazil",,NE,,masyel2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/masyel2/,avibase-0B42CDFF,,,Cayenne [= French Guiana] .,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/10286#page/473/mode/1up,Motacilla aequinoctialis
