32178,species,Passeriformes,Parulidae,New World Warblers,Basileuterus melanotis,"Lawrence, GN, 1868",Annals of the Lyceum of Natural History of New York 9 p.95,Black-eared Warbler,Costa Rican Warbler,Costa Rican Warbler,539,"Basileuterus tristriatus (polytypic) is split into four species based on differences in vocalizations and plumages (Donegan 2014): B. melanotis (monotypic); B. tacarcunae (monotypic); B. punctipectus (polytypic, including inconspicuus and canens); and nominate B. tristriatus. This arrangement is supported by the mitochondrial DNA study of Gutiérrez-Pinto et al. (2012), with B. tristriatus sensu lato recovered as paraphyletic.",mountains of Costa Rica and western Panama,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/232775311,thswar5,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/thswar5/,avibase-1741B8A7,,,,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/22948#page/111/mode/1up,Basileuterus melanotis
32179,species,Passeriformes,Parulidae,New World Warblers,Basileuterus tacarcunae,"Chapman, FM, 1924",American Museum Novitates no.143 p.6,Tacarcuna Warbler,Tacarcuna Warbler,Tacarcuna Warbler,539,"Basileuterus tristriatus (polytypic) is split into four species based on differences in vocalizations and plumages (Donegan 2014): B. melanotis (monotypic); B. tacarcunae (monotypic); B. punctipectus (polytypic, including inconspicuus and canens); and nominate B. tristriatus. This arrangement is supported by the mitochondrial DNA study of Gutiérrez-Pinto et al. (2012), with B. tristriatus sensu lato recovered as paraphyletic.","local in highlands of central Panama (Panamá and Guna Yala), eastern Panama (Cerra Tacarcuna, Darién), and adjacent northwestern Colombia (Chocó)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/232775530,thswar9,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/thswar9/,avibase-5A1D54E9,,,"east slope, Mt. Tacarcuna, 4,600 ft., below Colombia-Panama line, Darien, Panama.","Descriptions of new birds from Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and Bolivia.",https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/3224/,Basileuterus tacarcunae
32180,species,Passeriformes,Parulidae,New World Warblers,Basileuterus tristriatus,"(Tschudi, JJ, 1844)",Archiv für Naturgeschichte 10 p.283,Three-striped Warbler,Three-striped Warbler,Three-striped Warbler,539,"Basileuterus tristriatus (polytypic) is split into four species based on differences in vocalizations and plumages (Donegan 2014): B. melanotis (monotypic); B. tacarcunae (monotypic); B. punctipectus (polytypic, including inconspicuus and canens); and nominate B. tristriatus. This arrangement is supported by the mitochondrial DNA study of Gutiérrez-Pinto et al. (2012), with B. tristriatus sensu lato recovered as paraphyletic.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/232775023,thswar1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/thswar1/,avibase-99E9FFE0,,,"corrected to valley of Vitoc, Junin, by Hellmayr, 1935, Field Mus. Nat. Hist. Publ., Zool. Ser., 13, pt. 8, p. 494.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/48694#page/297/mode/1up,Myiodioctes tristriatus
