32189,species,Passeriformes,Parulidae,New World Warblers,Basileuterus punctipectus,"Chapman, FM, 1924",American Museum Novitates no.143 p.5,Yungas Warbler,Yungas Warbler,Yungas Warbler,539,"Basileuterus tristriatus (polytypic) is split into four species based on differences in vocalizations and plumages (Donegan 2014): B. melanotis (monotypic); B. tacarcunae (monotypic); B. punctipectus (polytypic, including inconspicuus and canens); and nominate B. tristriatus. This arrangement is supported by the mitochondrial DNA study of Gutiérrez-Pinto et al. (2012), with B. tristriatus sensu lato recovered as paraphyletic.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/232775895,thswar2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/thswar2/,avibase-A74E673E,,,"Yungas, 3,600 ft., Cochabamba, Bolivia.","Descriptions of new birds from Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and Bolivia.",https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/3224/,Basileuterus tristriatus punctipectus
