32272,species,Passeriformes,Cardinalidae,Cardinals and Allies,Granatellus pelzelni,"Sclater, PL, 1865","Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London 1864, pt.3 p.606 pl.37 fig.1",Rose-breasted Chat,,Rose-breasted Chat,579,"Taxon paraensis is treated as a species separate from Granatellus pelzelni based primarily on divergence in mitochondrial (Dornas et al. 2022) and genomic DNA data (Scott 2022), supported by minor plumage differences. Although vocalizations appear strikingly different (Boesman 2016r), it is unclear if homologous songs have been compared (i.e., female song of paraensis may have been compared to male song of pelzelni); further research needed. After the AviList vote, SACC considered this split and decided against it; this issue thus may warrant reconsideration for a future version of AviList.","tropical southeastern Venezuela to Guyana, Suriname, central and Amazonian Brazil, and northern Bolivia (eastern Pando east to far northern Santa Cruz)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103804346,robcha2,,avibase-A44E7CC9,,,"Destaramento do Ribeirao, Rio Madeira, Brazil.",Descriptions of Seven New Species of Birds discovered by the late Dr. John Natterer in Brazil.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/90417#page/708/mode/1up,Granatellus pelzelni
32273,species,Passeriformes,Cardinalidae,Cardinals and Allies,Granatellus paraensis,"Rothschild, LW, 1906",Bulletin of the British Ornithologists' Club 16 p.81,Rose-bellied Chat,,Rose-bellied Chat,579,"Taxon paraensis is treated as a species separate from Granatellus pelzelni based primarily on divergence in mitochondrial (Dornas et al. 2022) and genomic DNA data (Scott 2022), supported by minor plumage differences. Although vocalizations appear strikingly different (Boesman 2016r), it is unclear if homologous songs have been compared (i.e., female song of paraensis may have been compared to male song of pelzelni); further research needed. After the AviList vote, SACC considered this split and decided against it; this issue thus may warrant reconsideration for a future version of AviList.","tropical northern Brazil (eastern Pará, Maranhão, and Tocantins)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103804365,robcha3,,avibase-5DABDBB9,,,"[Santo Antonio do] Prata, near Para, Brazil.",On two new subspecies of the genera Granatellus and Eulabeornis.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/100946#page/107/mode/1up,Granatellus pelzelni paraensis
