32344,genus,Passeriformes,Cardinalidae,Cardinals and Allies,Chlorothraupis,"Salvin, O; Godman, FD, 1883",Biologia Centrali-Americana. Aves 1 p.297,,,,1195b,Chlorothraupis is retained as a separate genus from Habia based on morphology and depth of divergence in mitochondrial-dominated and genomic DNA data (Barker et al. 2015; Scott et al. 2022).,,,,,,,,F,"Phoenicothraupis carmioli [Lawrence, 1868]; type by subsequent designation (Ridgway, 1884, Proc. U.S. Nat. Mus., 6 (1883), p. 412).",,,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/14589#page/355/mode/1up,Chlorothraupis
32345,species,Passeriformes,Cardinalidae,Cardinals and Allies,Chlorothraupis carmioli,"(Lawrence, GN, 1868)",Annals of the Lyceum of Natural History of New York 9(1870) p.100,Carmiol's Tanager,Carmiol's Tanager,Carmiol's Tanager,581,"Taxon frenata is treated as a species separate from Chlorothraupis carmioli based on genetics, supported by vocal and plumage differences. Genomic data (Scott 2022) indicate that C. carmioli is paraphyletic, with frenata recovered as sister to C. olivacea. Although formal bioacoustic analyses are lacking, vocalizations of frenata differ consistently from carmioli and are readily distinguished (Ridgely & Greenfield 2001; Hilty 2022), and differences in plumage, although minor, are commensurate with those between other species of Chlorothraupis.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103811314,olitan1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/olitan1/,avibase-6C96417C,,,"Angostura [, Costa Rica] .",A catalogue of the birds found in Costa Rica.,,Phoenicothraupis carmioli
