32349,species,Passeriformes,Cardinalidae,Cardinals and Allies,Chlorothraupis frenata,"Berlepsch, HHCL, 1907",Ornis. Internationale Zeitschrift für die gesammte Ornithologie 14 p.349,Yellow-lored Tanager,Yellow-lored Tanager,Yellow-lored Tanager,581,"Taxon frenata is treated as a species separate from Chlorothraupis carmioli based on genetics, supported by vocal and plumage differences. Genomic data (Scott 2022) indicate that C. carmioli is paraphyletic, with frenata recovered as sister to C. olivacea. Although formal bioacoustic analyses are lacking, vocalizations of frenata differ consistently from carmioli and are readily distinguished (Ridgely & Greenfield 2001; Hilty 2022), and differences in plumage, although minor, are commensurate with those between other species of Chlorothraupis.",tropical southern Colombia to central Bolivia (La Paz eastward to western Santa Cruz),,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103811345,cartan2,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/cartan2/,avibase-F455871D,,,"Marcapata, Peru.",Descriptions of new species and conspecies of Neotropical birds.,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/106225#page/377/mode/1up,Chlorothraupis carmioli frenata
