32791,species,Passeriformes,Thraupidae,Tanagers and Allies,Xenodacnis parina,"Cabanis, JL, 1873","Journal für Ornithologie 21, no.123 p.312 pl.4 fig.1,2",Tit-like Dacnis,,Tit-like Dacnis,620,"Taxon petersi (polytypic) is treated as a species separate from Xenodacnis parina (monotypic) based on differences in plumage, size, and vocalizations, with the disjunct population at Arequipa placed in X. petersi. More detailed analyses of genetics, morphology, and vocalizations would be informative. After this issue was considered by AviList, SACC considered and rejected this proposal, which will likely be reconsidered for a future version of AviList.","inter-Andean valleys of south-central Peru (Junín, Ayacucho, Apurímac, and Cusco)",,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103839796,tildac2,,avibase-D7703EFB,,,"Maraynioc, Peru.",[Über zwei von Herrn C. Jelski in West-Peru entdeckte Vögel].,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/101685#page/324/mode/1up,Xenodacnis parina
32792,species,Passeriformes,Thraupidae,Tanagers and Allies,Xenodacnis petersi,"Bond, J; Meyer de Schauensee, R, 1939",Notulae Naturae 40 p.1,Streaked Dacnis,,Streaked Dacnis,620,"Taxon petersi (polytypic) is treated as a species separate from Xenodacnis parina (monotypic) based on differences in plumage, size, and vocalizations, with the disjunct population at Arequipa placed in X. petersi. More detailed analyses of genetics, morphology, and vocalizations would be informative. After this issue was considered by AviList, SACC considered and rejected this proposal, which will likely be reconsidered for a future version of AviList.",,,LC,https://datazone.birdlife.org/species/factsheet/103840020,tildac3,,avibase-4226846A,,,"Yanac, Dept. of Ancash, Peru.",Description of a new species and subspecies of Xenodacnis.,https://ia800302.us.archive.org/34/items/bub_gb_gw9l1RqUf6sC/bub_gb_gw9l1RqUf6sC.pdf,Xenodacnis petersi
