33421,species,Passeriformes,Thraupidae,Tanagers and Allies,Anisognathus igniventris,"(d'Orbigny, ACVMD; de Lafresnaye, NFAA, 1837)",Magasin de Zoologie 7 cl.2 p.32,Scarlet-bellied Mountain Tanager,Scarlet-bellied Mountain Tanager,,607,"Taxon lunulatus (polytypic) is treated as conspecific with Anisognathus igniventris based on available evidence. Plumage differences seem minor, apparent vocal differences have not been thoroughly documented (Boesman 2016w), and mitochondrial DNA divergence (Sedano & Burns 2010; Freeman et al. 2023) is comparable to that found between other subspecies in this complex; however, more thorough geographic and genetic sampling could be informative.",,,NE,,sbmtan1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/sbmtan1/,avibase-9FCCD579,,,"Apolobamba [,Bolivia] .","Synopsis Avium, in ejus per Americam meridionalem itinere, collectarum et ab ipso viatore necnon.",https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/114101#page/148/mode/1up,A[glaia] igniventris
