33439,species,Passeriformes,Thraupidae,Tanagers and Allies,Chlorochrysa calliparaea,"(Tschudi, JJ, 1844)",Archiv für Naturgeschichte 10 p.286,Orange-eared Tanager,Orange-eared Tanager,,610,"Taxon fulgentissima (monotypic) is treated as a subspecies of Chlorochrysa calliparaea (polytypic) based on available evidence. Although the plumage of fulgentissima differs noticeably from subspecies bourcieri, the plumage of nominate calliparaea is intermediate between these two (Hellmayr 1936; Zimmer 1943a). Analyses of genetic and vocal data may shed light on species limits in this group.",,,NE,,oretan1,https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/oretan1/,avibase-E8B48699,,,"Peru; type from 'Chinchon forests/' Junin, fide Hellmayr, 1936, Field Mus. Nat. Hist. Publ., Zool. Ser., 13, pt. 9, p. 76.",,https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/48694#page/300/mode/1up,C[allospiza] calliparaea
